[{"sha":"a781761eda225ba85c2b3b64ba2b74c0c54fbecf","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGE3ODE3NjFlZGEyMjViYTg1YzJiM2I2NGJhMmI3NGMwYzU0ZmJlY2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"iceweasel-oai","email":"iceweasel@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T18:27:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T18:27:44Z"},"message":"[codex] fix Windows ConPTY input handling (#29734)\n\n## Why\n\nWindows unified-exec TTY input did not behave like the non-Windows PTY\npath. ConPTY sessions could receive the wrong line ending or mishandle\nbackspace, especially when sending input to a foreground program through\nPowerShell or cmd. The local, legacy restricted, and elevated paths also\nhandled this normalization separately.\n\n## What changed\n\n- share one stateful Windows TTY input normalizer across local, legacy\nrestricted, and elevated runner paths\n- translate LF and split CRLF into one Windows terminal Enter, encode\nbackspace as DEL, and preserve UTF-8 and control bytes such as Ctrl-C\n- add Windows integration coverage for Unicode input, backspace, Enter,\nand PowerShell foreground-child Ctrl-C behavior\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-utils-pty` (13 tests passed; the Unicode\nintegration test retried once)\n- the Unicode integration test passed five consecutive runs with retries\ndisabled\n- integration coverage sends `cafeé 漢字` through cmd and PowerShell and\nverifies that Ctrl-C interrupts a running PowerShell foreground child","tree":{"sha":"0d77c692f57113d3d8cb92b86403450bf7649474","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/0d77c692f57113d3d8cb92b86403450bf7649474"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a781761eda225ba85c2b3b64ba2b74c0c54fbecf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPCGgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyhgQAKIZ4VOTrUNBX8hS8YNQXmlM\noA54al8a2dRVxU+ByKWB05dS/NMqhRx8ZDjBczSNOHYMux0zHstWBkpD67KwnM9z\nZWUP4BnLGs3klIHZFEtL4cJ4rh65NriuXua6iTFYtheDYnv5UkRCmOcJcx8oBtnP\nQ/mdXBrp4rxLQMzpmxkrtATvdNACEi5DD6Ewy/tdMnxBhJk9r+hZ/NNdz9kyobdz\n4qaGZfePw9aWvgXqQxQq8iQWiu2pkkjE5HMY5COLB9vQRhMLELf+9Zz/pCBkBCx7\nTqvTUSgc2QJnJNKoVgUt6U06rhNq8SqnzsOfQg1l/BmsKZfxtyP7AhJ96VHi0j4H\nug0Y5Ycd92i+3DQ7d6YT9tmogiEKhZ8x/sKKdagPPXSqD8ZTFM3qcS8tbDfzAVcD\nhHZLdlrg1r/BedQhjMD7nDRqaRClsZgUTiI6oBpBG/NMbk/puiHkSatguyY0GNr5\n8zPCflyZqdNNgLk6iWHhZL1S72mQaOBTij6OZJ3w11rqNQfjsqVxDv6MiVwuMg6t\nYjPScgXoiavSaKsgKKFSF5viAWzE8ujvWTwTOEV+shf/WeCYTGCyD2JF8H93mSyb\nRx7DNYEb5Ian3RQAhJ4UvqZnLOkKC5Ko4WMgUjckQmaDuKFhPy0ilqjp4fUT9rIl\nzu/9SzP+IsMC52iIhM0C\n=T9dh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0d77c692f57113d3d8cb92b86403450bf7649474\nparent 8a6a34be7524b5c313ea63698355cb67dd93c2be\nauthor iceweasel-oai <iceweasel@openai.com> 1782325664 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782325664 -0700\n\n[codex] fix Windows ConPTY input handling (#29734)\n\n## Why\n\nWindows unified-exec TTY input did not behave like the non-Windows PTY\npath. ConPTY sessions could receive the wrong line ending or mishandle\nbackspace, especially when sending input to a foreground program through\nPowerShell or cmd. The local, legacy restricted, and elevated paths also\nhandled this normalization separately.\n\n## What changed\n\n- share one stateful Windows TTY input normalizer across local, legacy\nrestricted, and elevated runner paths\n- translate LF and split CRLF into one Windows terminal Enter, encode\nbackspace as DEL, and preserve UTF-8 and control bytes such as Ctrl-C\n- add Windows integration coverage for Unicode input, backspace, Enter,\nand PowerShell foreground-child Ctrl-C behavior\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-utils-pty` (13 tests passed; the Unicode\nintegration test retried once)\n- the Unicode integration test passed five consecutive runs with retries\ndisabled\n- integration coverage sends `cafeé 漢字` through cmd and PowerShell and\nverifies that Ctrl-C interrupts a running PowerShell foreground child","verified_at":"2026-06-24T18:27:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a781761eda225ba85c2b3b64ba2b74c0c54fbecf","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a781761eda225ba85c2b3b64ba2b74c0c54fbecf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a781761eda225ba85c2b3b64ba2b74c0c54fbecf/comments","author":{"login":"iceweasel-oai","id":234057055,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNtXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234057055?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/iceweasel-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8a6a34be7524b5c313ea63698355cb67dd93c2be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8a6a34be7524b5c313ea63698355cb67dd93c2be","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8a6a34be7524b5c313ea63698355cb67dd93c2be"}]},{"sha":"8a6a34be7524b5c313ea63698355cb67dd93c2be","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDhhNmEzNGJlNzUyNGI1YzMxM2VhNjM2OTgzNTVjYjY3ZGQ5M2MyYmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T18:08:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T18:08:39Z"},"message":"Fix environment skill discovery after merge (#29887)\n\n## Why\n\nThe merge of #29831 with the new `fs/walk` environment discovery path\nleft three `SkillFileDiscovery` initializers without the new namespace\nfields. This makes `codex-core-skills` fail to compile and breaks CI for\nevery PR based on current `main`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- collect plugin roots from the directory entries already returned by\n`fs/walk`\n- keep the selected root as the namespace fallback\n- initialize empty discovery results with empty namespace sets\n\nThis preserves the bounded `fs/walk` implementation while restoring the\nnamespace caching added by #29831.","tree":{"sha":"2fcf3747258f8bb0beb43dac7cf9e634c1c73a75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2fcf3747258f8bb0beb43dac7cf9e634c1c73a75"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8a6a34be7524b5c313ea63698355cb67dd93c2be","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPB0nCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA64wQAFkx7uzjGG+TSPPfJrmgwsog\nXMTGYXvUKRjbSyOryyawLMeFZx2wcHEAL10pQy/KvaWt27d8x1ZdPYUX56G0I9hI\nmk2pUGRIQKggjxBs+3eCBF7aPb02jSTYLM/CzvttqeUHFrtTGuYBQwrP1TP65niL\nyeCb5TE3+Q8H9XPqK02uzu+OFZB1mMniIt0hh9e4zPfKEE+vdI2i69BTL7L08xI4\n8azzPNtwrTJNPGUNORThr4N/8SAixUXEYvwUrMp7KpKE6wIhFhZfycZZKUIyzI5S\nIbLUR7iT4ir2ygWbFlxRpfepd8yZgfxjPyxsjVumksJGVoKTP5cRo4upAurKFEFO\nyAphHZF0NfhqdAf3ASZZAvr5nEzDk61usSekJCRTbAieQBPjOWWOtYGgwIRRfw27\nl/eKDesTN/HozRZKmsagSG5VGkymzEzwIPT+aAifbMeunmGZLnds7/kiZlFvbn66\nGNDXGRp4AVf+0y3omvDVhXBEyYZDtvZY50rsqxL1L0LWka9MlVXX86NfaTUJVB5Q\nva+Yoo/UPZ75zPmX7YI/M/SxE1fNvxmOQ+k7ejoMd9/lbqBjU6pgoOtzwgc3E7bl\n+27DAOvv3Ci3Xf12n7d19uFJwbAZUy3k93YK2G4Kqsq0wUwanM9spzDxuzpMXVb5\n7F8mG0rn8yiEkM3/alPz\n=zRv8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2fcf3747258f8bb0beb43dac7cf9e634c1c73a75\nparent 93c79046d669d39632215b5c74fcc7c69fcb4d5b\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782324519 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782324519 +0100\n\nFix environment skill discovery after merge (#29887)\n\n## Why\n\nThe merge of #29831 with the new `fs/walk` environment discovery path\nleft three `SkillFileDiscovery` initializers without the new namespace\nfields. This makes `codex-core-skills` fail to compile and breaks CI for\nevery PR based on current `main`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- collect plugin roots from the directory entries already returned by\n`fs/walk`\n- keep the selected root as the namespace fallback\n- initialize empty discovery results with empty namespace sets\n\nThis preserves the bounded `fs/walk` implementation while restoring the\nnamespace caching added by #29831.","verified_at":"2026-06-24T18:08:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8a6a34be7524b5c313ea63698355cb67dd93c2be","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8a6a34be7524b5c313ea63698355cb67dd93c2be","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8a6a34be7524b5c313ea63698355cb67dd93c2be/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"93c79046d669d39632215b5c74fcc7c69fcb4d5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/93c79046d669d39632215b5c74fcc7c69fcb4d5b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/93c79046d669d39632215b5c74fcc7c69fcb4d5b"}]},{"sha":"93c79046d669d39632215b5c74fcc7c69fcb4d5b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDkzYzc5MDQ2ZDY2OWQzOTYzMjIxNWI1Yzc0ZmNjN2M2OWZjYjRkNWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T18:06:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T18:06:35Z"},"message":"ci: fail jobs that dirty the worktree (#29720)\n\n## Why\n\nCI jobs should not silently leave tracked changes or untracked files in\nthe repository worktree.\n\n## What\n\n- Add a shared final worktree-cleanliness action to 19 checkout-bearing\nPR and main CI jobs.\n- Ignore the intentional SDK scratch directory and nested V8 checkout.\n- Pin Bazelisk in shared CI setup so `.bazelversion` remains\nauthoritative, avoiding `MODULE.bazel.lock` deltas on Windows runners.\n- Leave `rust-ci-full` and release-only workflows unchanged.\n- Update `AGENTS.md` to discourage review bots from asking for\n`MODULE.bazel.lock` changes.","tree":{"sha":"3a3fd6e3b7536cd9b6dbaaeb062e5c1ab1ba6fd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3a3fd6e3b7536cd9b6dbaaeb062e5c1ab1ba6fd6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/93c79046d669d39632215b5c74fcc7c69fcb4d5b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPByrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAm7AQAK8QMABxQHHI1USzudb8qm2H\nGr0m+6v24MmSlBVZ5h7ZeDyiSOQS5qC+fpvfvAHTvFsdjZfCLIcXk11hqb+pyMlg\nm8RHOhghIhodiwYQszEypkq3R9X1NB4+rPGqchCSocmXo/7WmnHCz7K9iiZGAB0T\nkFM+k1F5maMVSoTH8t7HtYdhXenGd14Hs3Fk+8WTWglUxruZXS1+lchbbWLTVPZv\nJsvrPewPzyV52RbUWt/FQWsER5SsELWgLfYW0XMA9vKT/Ur57T4yMjolMesLNYna\n1e3k3nvyjROESrWBV13Wt2nZ1akh9alX/73IzYNT/WGK9JcnUpXl0sMS56NaP0OE\nbLhGb5gyiSboG1RIKnqfb4VMju08lAg4JoVdmBxn1GaWRWeNYKmXLNb4+BHGSJWr\nSXJQZp1zBxkp+vY2daDDe6xANuZnc3BSo9aAzTRAWavPz3zZ/5AhlQreAJCv3fXg\nH9AnG6Wvo+Eq+XUhQ/ISK2jzigVhdAAHJt3+gK8aulTsf1Q1cfcAi8OHu85KU7RP\nzbj64zR2k8BQ7rYVPcaygJLQGrjjND2i71n9saVFDuY5NqADQERxpb47HBXu1gCB\nuPdWPc+XZl67/MRRrSoHMgmeQPydRBSI0nBX/jpb6wf3aCQ8Vy7JkZRfIFQuRc45\nffsPJ8Vj1VLky+r8wtTr\n=ygVr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3a3fd6e3b7536cd9b6dbaaeb062e5c1ab1ba6fd6\nparent 390b73133b0707ce877ec924b0011c06b776b9e8\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1782324395 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782324395 -0700\n\nci: fail jobs that dirty the worktree (#29720)\n\n## Why\n\nCI jobs should not silently leave tracked changes or untracked files in\nthe repository worktree.\n\n## What\n\n- Add a shared final worktree-cleanliness action to 19 checkout-bearing\nPR and main CI jobs.\n- Ignore the intentional SDK scratch directory and nested V8 checkout.\n- Pin Bazelisk in shared CI setup so `.bazelversion` remains\nauthoritative, avoiding `MODULE.bazel.lock` deltas on Windows runners.\n- Leave `rust-ci-full` and release-only workflows unchanged.\n- Update `AGENTS.md` to discourage review bots from asking for\n`MODULE.bazel.lock` changes.","verified_at":"2026-06-24T18:06:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/93c79046d669d39632215b5c74fcc7c69fcb4d5b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/93c79046d669d39632215b5c74fcc7c69fcb4d5b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/93c79046d669d39632215b5c74fcc7c69fcb4d5b/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"390b73133b0707ce877ec924b0011c06b776b9e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/390b73133b0707ce877ec924b0011c06b776b9e8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/390b73133b0707ce877ec924b0011c06b776b9e8"}]},{"sha":"390b73133b0707ce877ec924b0011c06b776b9e8","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDM5MGI3MzEzM2IwNzA3Y2U4NzdlYzkyNGIwMDExYzA2Yjc3NmI5ZTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T16:14:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T16:14:34Z"},"message":"Cache plugin namespace during executor skill discovery (#29831)\n\n## Why\n\nExecutor skill discovery runs before the remote skills catalog is\navailable. For a remote environment, each `ExecutorFileSystem` operation\nbecomes an exec-server RPC.\n\nPreviously, every discovered `SKILL.md` independently resolved its\nplugin namespace by walking its ancestors and probing both supported\nmanifest locations. In the common `plugin/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md`\nlayout, that repeats 8 RPCs per skill even though every skill under the\nplugin root uses the same namespace. These lookups happen while skills\nare parsed, so their cost grows linearly with the skill count and adds\ndirectly to first-turn latency.\n\nA selected capability root can also contain standalone skills, multiple\nsibling plugins, nested plugins, or symlinked directories. The\noptimization therefore needs to retain the nearest-ancestor namespace\nfor each skill rather than assuming the selected root represents exactly\none plugin.\n\n## What changed\n\n- record plugin-root candidates from directory entries already returned\nduring skill discovery\n- prune candidates that are not ancestors of any discovered `SKILL.md`\nbefore reading manifests\n- resolve each relevant plugin root once, with one fallback lookup per\ncanonical traversal root for symlinked directories\n- select the nearest cached plugin namespace for each discovered skill\n- avoid namespace lookup entirely when the root contains no skills\n\nNo additional directory traversal is required. Namespace work now scales\nwith the number of plugin roots that contain discovered skills, rather\nthan the total number of skills or unrelated sibling plugins. Standalone\nand nested-plugin names keep their previous behavior.\n\n## Benchmarks\n\nI used a temporary counting `ExecutorFileSystem` around the real local\nfilesystem. Each filesystem operation was counted as one remote RPC and\ngiven 1 ms of injected latency. Each variant ran three times; times\nbelow are medians.\n\n### One plugin with 100 skills\n\n| Operation | Before | After | Delta |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| `get_metadata` | 1,002 | 303 | -699 |\n| `read_file` | 200 | 101 | -99 |\n| `read_directory` | 102 | 102 | 0 |\n| **Total filesystem RPCs** | **1,304** | **506** | **-798 (-61.2%)** |\n| **Median load time** | **2.890 s** | **0.997 s** | **2.90× faster** |\n\nThe namespace-specific work drops from 800 RPCs to 2 in this layout.\n\n### Multiple plugins under one selected root\n\nThese runs compare the correct pre-optimization implementation with the\nfinal nearest-plugin-root cache. The total plugin skill count stays at\n100 while the number of plugin roots changes.\n\n| Layout | Before RPCs | After RPCs | Reduction | Before | After |\nSpeedup |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| 2 plugins × 50 skills | 1,312 | 530 | 59.6% | 1,819 ms | 711 ms |\n2.56× |\n| 10 plugins × 10 skills | 1,344 | 578 | 57.0% | 1,850 ms | 778 ms |\n2.38× |\n| 50 plugins × 2 skills | 1,504 | 818 | 45.6% | 2,094 ms | 1,086 ms |\n1.93× |\n| 10 plugins × 10 skills + 10 standalone skills | 1,596 | 630 | 60.5% |\n2,209 ms | 860 ms | 2.57× |\n\nThe remaining cost grows with the number of relevant plugin manifests.\nEach relevant manifest is read once instead of once per skill, while\nsibling plugins with no discovered skills are not read. Absolute latency\nsavings depend on the executor's real RPC latency.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-skills` (109 passed across the library and\nintegration-test binaries)\n- one integration test covers standalone, outer-plugin, nested-plugin,\nand unused sibling-plugin layouts, and asserts the exact set of\nmanifests read","tree":{"sha":"5623b7f77c6d69d549ea9a68b3bc5110e15205c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5623b7f77c6d69d549ea9a68b3bc5110e15205c1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/390b73133b0707ce877ec924b0011c06b776b9e8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPAJqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATBoQAFs3fL3/bhFigBF3RGS8e2Ke\nIfrlO9mkm7KyekUce0mPSleuFxMFyNbfklv/r/H94XtEkOD9LnGmaZK0hGaKLe7t\nEbnjmvvVSakYmcnMA3hYUNirRCMT/BP2lC//cL0d8DsKI7DKUviFHnsQH3dDIToQ\n0DjtNw85H2wzKqNNJMLqaxtwpemh+sBPpzZ00UuRKbTkTrDV6JVfrBCluOpl4ny+\nqOQevdeHDT0Sk/5Fb5mix7lwj5+O9//LekKCvsHCtKEzGMdJ3rEjQVgOhzbWSeYQ\nSC31sXzwUGqO/wdwv56dK8avY0v9TBzV1vfqKfj7aECBzRb80f4ZOIJ1ldC/bboM\nBKGq73dcjelKs/hXg5Jn58WZ4QNu1JhEPyWF+JaDPvt4jwBTcpyK2WsGY2sQZjUc\n9Qx92k7z8/2w2Nm081CEASJx2nnH9VwjATUAvVbmcHIvvDJnCXxINxWkSGq6r3tj\nV0cBqP/X0YbtUxhGB/6sUDAohbhsHgggifh3HB29UaR3oUagdKvRNGOR5RAYKSa6\neszN1LxSE+zz4k7HiUiSC+kAFa2iJ8rJjkIIMwdbZnTivAJOTbHJRgvjRvKiLkWz\nHZkQVhl8saMQZwXNlPzjXljYg2+W9vJ0PO4o6s1gtiZeoagPGuJp/Tw/B7Gzxw/K\nk9gQrba5gSI03w6yrorO\n=SiOk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5623b7f77c6d69d549ea9a68b3bc5110e15205c1\nparent 3694b48a82343d94b58c62fa9af335710c3a6187\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782317674 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782317674 +0100\n\nCache plugin namespace during executor skill discovery (#29831)\n\n## Why\n\nExecutor skill discovery runs before the remote skills catalog is\navailable. For a remote environment, each `ExecutorFileSystem` operation\nbecomes an exec-server RPC.\n\nPreviously, every discovered `SKILL.md` independently resolved its\nplugin namespace by walking its ancestors and probing both supported\nmanifest locations. In the common `plugin/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md`\nlayout, that repeats 8 RPCs per skill even though every skill under the\nplugin root uses the same namespace. These lookups happen while skills\nare parsed, so their cost grows linearly with the skill count and adds\ndirectly to first-turn latency.\n\nA selected capability root can also contain standalone skills, multiple\nsibling plugins, nested plugins, or symlinked directories. The\noptimization therefore needs to retain the nearest-ancestor namespace\nfor each skill rather than assuming the selected root represents exactly\none plugin.\n\n## What changed\n\n- record plugin-root candidates from directory entries already returned\nduring skill discovery\n- prune candidates that are not ancestors of any discovered `SKILL.md`\nbefore reading manifests\n- resolve each relevant plugin root once, with one fallback lookup per\ncanonical traversal root for symlinked directories\n- select the nearest cached plugin namespace for each discovered skill\n- avoid namespace lookup entirely when the root contains no skills\n\nNo additional directory traversal is required. Namespace work now scales\nwith the number of plugin roots that contain discovered skills, rather\nthan the total number of skills or unrelated sibling plugins. Standalone\nand nested-plugin names keep their previous behavior.\n\n## Benchmarks\n\nI used a temporary counting `ExecutorFileSystem` around the real local\nfilesystem. Each filesystem operation was counted as one remote RPC and\ngiven 1 ms of injected latency. Each variant ran three times; times\nbelow are medians.\n\n### One plugin with 100 skills\n\n| Operation | Before | After | Delta |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| `get_metadata` | 1,002 | 303 | -699 |\n| `read_file` | 200 | 101 | -99 |\n| `read_directory` | 102 | 102 | 0 |\n| **Total filesystem RPCs** | **1,304** | **506** | **-798 (-61.2%)** |\n| **Median load time** | **2.890 s** | **0.997 s** | **2.90× faster** |\n\nThe namespace-specific work drops from 800 RPCs to 2 in this layout.\n\n### Multiple plugins under one selected root\n\nThese runs compare the correct pre-optimization implementation with the\nfinal nearest-plugin-root cache. The total plugin skill count stays at\n100 while the number of plugin roots changes.\n\n| Layout | Before RPCs | After RPCs | Reduction | Before | After |\nSpeedup |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| 2 plugins × 50 skills | 1,312 | 530 | 59.6% | 1,819 ms | 711 ms |\n2.56× |\n| 10 plugins × 10 skills | 1,344 | 578 | 57.0% | 1,850 ms | 778 ms |\n2.38× |\n| 50 plugins × 2 skills | 1,504 | 818 | 45.6% | 2,094 ms | 1,086 ms |\n1.93× |\n| 10 plugins × 10 skills + 10 standalone skills | 1,596 | 630 | 60.5% |\n2,209 ms | 860 ms | 2.57× |\n\nThe remaining cost grows with the number of relevant plugin manifests.\nEach relevant manifest is read once instead of once per skill, while\nsibling plugins with no discovered skills are not read. Absolute latency\nsavings depend on the executor's real RPC latency.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-skills` (109 passed across the library and\nintegration-test binaries)\n- one integration test covers standalone, outer-plugin, nested-plugin,\nand unused sibling-plugin layouts, and asserts the exact set of\nmanifests read","verified_at":"2026-06-24T16:14:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/390b73133b0707ce877ec924b0011c06b776b9e8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/390b73133b0707ce877ec924b0011c06b776b9e8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/390b73133b0707ce877ec924b0011c06b776b9e8/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3694b48a82343d94b58c62fa9af335710c3a6187","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3694b48a82343d94b58c62fa9af335710c3a6187","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3694b48a82343d94b58c62fa9af335710c3a6187"}]},{"sha":"3694b48a82343d94b58c62fa9af335710c3a6187","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDM2OTRiNDhhODIzNDNkOTRiNThjNjJmYTlhZjMzNTcxMGMzYTYxODc","commit":{"author":{"name":"charlesgong-openai","email":"charlesgong@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T15:56:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T15:56:57Z"},"message":"[codex] show external import result counts (#29567)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Show per-type import counts in the `/import` review UI and started\nmessage.\n- Render completion results as a multi-line summary with total\nimported/failed counts and one row per import type.\n- Add snapshot coverage for the updated review and completion output.\n\n<img width=\"537\" height=\"322\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-23 at 9 41 20 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/166542eb-2097-4b2b-8130-8f6fd8c680ce\"\n/>\n\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI previously only reported that Claude Code import started or\nfinished. Users could not see how many items of each type were selected\nor how many actually imported versus failed.","tree":{"sha":"45fc74f6f117de9844a7b733ea3ad87b07c6c0f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/45fc74f6f117de9844a7b733ea3ad87b07c6c0f3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3694b48a82343d94b58c62fa9af335710c3a6187","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO/5JCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZe4QAHdtMb23im7bc3VcX9fj0QhU\nIYEmAQNeSvBrYlZraHtbY7CChqHSh/EMvbf1X3qGqdwF1DK+b8A4cSxnnbacTcRS\n8+tfZmIP+4sICfqpK8GqRhxbV809o2eJmZUJtXwK9kg1GfHQd1iKIlbzby3xD1bq\nkRqvEFbMHk4OBIHWBajs4SIeanxWytj98PfUtn8qb3Xm8DSndwgAplaf8feYEX+k\n2l3+uG7CpvhJc8mrDms+JoULAIDRzCGlEbUQd2YgG9PNL6LkP3yASlHi3Y+XakhF\nGwuAp+TJniYLPouZyp26+KUMFoBwvIkSaEHqusU11l9VEgc3kDSr1dEj4ctAIvFb\nbhWFBnAn5LR6eGBGY4cP0Nr9G80Egib1m10xaXCcCa1dsWa43SfsOrzxv1yfNgLC\nlQEzRLotP+Oouz7UUPa4H1swYdvqVaRlItZEBC5YvMSVkPDvWG5RWqAdMsOq2i96\nyqEjrmdRyLaEWu9XC5WuIjopBF+5lJt/1/iPRNReirLZToD5MeKgH+iOSV9fIVNT\n9HrEXJ8hMBfmcjlYGBamZ4YSS1/i3TawKVD4B9QcKshUUXZG8EGpBkGk90JQydfM\n9ET1megMpLcrpSjT9FEQthZKhaJiApYRmFIFkjbSRIR5jt0UlefwroLPVxiPFnHK\npsps5vOZm8ByqgmlO3D/\n=ZQtH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 45fc74f6f117de9844a7b733ea3ad87b07c6c0f3\nparent 69b76e9d075198b14beff200a2ecf53364cd2c40\nauthor charlesgong-openai <charlesgong@openai.com> 1782316617 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782316617 -0700\n\n[codex] show external import result counts (#29567)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Show per-type import counts in the `/import` review UI and started\nmessage.\n- Render completion results as a multi-line summary with total\nimported/failed counts and one row per import type.\n- Add snapshot coverage for the updated review and completion output.\n\n<img width=\"537\" height=\"322\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-23 at 9 41 20 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/166542eb-2097-4b2b-8130-8f6fd8c680ce\"\n/>\n\n\n## Why\n\nThe TUI previously only reported that Claude Code import started or\nfinished. Users could not see how many items of each type were selected\nor how many actually imported versus failed.","verified_at":"2026-06-24T15:56:58Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3694b48a82343d94b58c62fa9af335710c3a6187","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3694b48a82343d94b58c62fa9af335710c3a6187","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3694b48a82343d94b58c62fa9af335710c3a6187/comments","author":{"login":"charlesgong-openai","id":200841148,"node_id":"U_kgDOC_iXvA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200841148?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesgong-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesgong-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"69b76e9d075198b14beff200a2ecf53364cd2c40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/69b76e9d075198b14beff200a2ecf53364cd2c40","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/69b76e9d075198b14beff200a2ecf53364cd2c40"}]},{"sha":"69b76e9d075198b14beff200a2ecf53364cd2c40","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY5Yjc2ZTlkMDc1MTk4YjE0YmVmZjIwMGEyZWNmNTMzNjRjZDJjNDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T15:32:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T15:32:35Z"},"message":"Use fs/walk for environment skill discovery (#29842)\n\nStack 2 of 3. Base: #29841. Follow-up: #29844.\n\n## What changes\n\nEnvironment skill discovery currently walks remote filesystems through\nrepeated `readDirectory` and `getMetadata` calls. This switches that\nscan to the bounded `fs/walk` operation from the base PR.\n\n```text\nBefore: readDirectory(root) -> getMetadata(...) -> readDirectory(child) -> ...\nAfter:  fs/walk(root, limits) -> filter the result for SKILL.md\n```\n\nThis makes environment skill discovery one RPC while preserving\ntraversal warnings and the existing depth and directory limits. The scan\nalso has an explicit entry limit. The follow-up restores\ndirectory-symlink traversal.","tree":{"sha":"afc381c44003953dfcdf6eadb828e21dab45800b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/afc381c44003953dfcdf6eadb828e21dab45800b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/69b76e9d075198b14beff200a2ecf53364cd2c40","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO/iTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnc0QAJYZGaaj7FFthln3Q2MrbLW7\nCscWBi+h6OjynyubTPHXQVcLw8ryi3asIbeaK6vUp9uxwNRByANj7jye6Z/4FgLd\n0rMO0qkCINsBcJOo2fFnVyqjQvXcwwljiFOKNJ/oZDlvmRGDkl03IiVa21tn70o6\nOpm4YS0TAdeivwCY28q4wDJIT6TJDgGwgE3RrCZy9znGiiGon1I1S26VDmP4uaAu\njAFJzAkqJDv0Zn3jMirNcBNkA36QYvASakd5NJrJqOKDylPnqHotVwz2JYBFhFZQ\nBYkewf931G5cEC12lg8SEsI2IvDqiOi5sCHIZmIWIH4k6TjKtpMl7Ra9CXHRdj9w\ndkeKrqrS81Tv2vk7a5vUbEJIutDmAdO5+/52/BkNT3NUkjgnvWIpMBeKwRFTT00E\nuzfnFJgcR/VmxWbHTT/0/8ysWVx9RPjBmEElGOXzkftQ2Nn2r3lu85EHEos7iLPz\n08X0OqWFIUdpa/ijCpDJB6YEjC374zijSmFBDNok3HChbN2DG+gCBgN3Kkm43b7i\nGyLNvHlhhfFy0q1vS/TLaDqmVuJiZdHnXjeyvVxqe3sO2lqswdtGjdgYnJHotava\nngqjSQI8Q93UkhPl7XvIv1CUqdc5jxRNpTPjCMfe1aG14vYMsJZMfszFoLZBQiWD\nTluisrIXGr5F9UyFyELu\n=Lsws\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree afc381c44003953dfcdf6eadb828e21dab45800b\nparent c14623d04c97c87b38193b454a10168b4eee8edf\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782315155 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782315155 +0100\n\nUse fs/walk for environment skill discovery (#29842)\n\nStack 2 of 3. Base: #29841. Follow-up: #29844.\n\n## What changes\n\nEnvironment skill discovery currently walks remote filesystems through\nrepeated `readDirectory` and `getMetadata` calls. This switches that\nscan to the bounded `fs/walk` operation from the base PR.\n\n```text\nBefore: readDirectory(root) -> getMetadata(...) -> readDirectory(child) -> ...\nAfter:  fs/walk(root, limits) -> filter the result for SKILL.md\n```\n\nThis makes environment skill discovery one RPC while preserving\ntraversal warnings and the existing depth and directory limits. The scan\nalso has an explicit entry limit. The follow-up restores\ndirectory-symlink traversal.","verified_at":"2026-06-24T15:32:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/69b76e9d075198b14beff200a2ecf53364cd2c40","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/69b76e9d075198b14beff200a2ecf53364cd2c40","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/69b76e9d075198b14beff200a2ecf53364cd2c40/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c14623d04c97c87b38193b454a10168b4eee8edf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c14623d04c97c87b38193b454a10168b4eee8edf","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c14623d04c97c87b38193b454a10168b4eee8edf"}]},{"sha":"c14623d04c97c87b38193b454a10168b4eee8edf","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGMxNDYyM2QwNGM5N2M4N2IzODE5M2I0NTRhMTAxNjhiNGVlZThlZGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T15:05:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T15:05:43Z"},"message":"Add a bounded filesystem walk RPC (#29841)\n\nStack 1 of 3. Follow-ups: #29842 and #29844.\n\n## What changes\n\nAdds a general bounded `fs/walk` operation to the exec server.\n\nThe operation returns file and directory entries plus recoverable\nper-path errors. It skips symlinks, preserves the existing filesystem\nsandbox routing, and enforces depth, directory, entry, and response-size\nlimits.\n\nThis PR only defines and wires the filesystem operation. It does not\nchange any callers yet.","tree":{"sha":"2d52ec7b8e4de57531483ec1fc7fb953c6b6b8c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2d52ec7b8e4de57531483ec1fc7fb953c6b6b8c9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c14623d04c97c87b38193b454a10168b4eee8edf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO/JHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACzsQAA6Nz/rF3aiBQQmA4Ek6uR1M\np0aHS4qV1UlGcx4lXqBU1mkMQpAcPMkqzoNXIgcWip2n4y4ZsauO902E8Fdk2Jtf\noX4djfkmZEXyOG1KdxCvaAfg4CZIjfqkpaTpqTUwTl4HKy3VHoy6IChvMVU5mQZ7\nXhAI1GR+V9B+BEQj7FuEcTkcr0CdlXf9hDLIMbXCTRiMkc8/Y6f7XOu7djkL2C9d\nH5BkSx6bQKlTZ0XzPKwqLdcqf+KYe28XD43X0lyyaKBkipgcE+gz3v4cAwWoMm65\nvI3wOrPBOtDXMUHiDnkAkDUgPkN+LJaOfy3t08ot3vfnv6Nv81OehoIAyC98BqJ+\nRpOlWgfCQWHqovEnjfcAmDyVlV81ScX4UCtq/Ui69O7+t4zpdv4lCPfPsRllHoSh\nJC+dAKJw2JuR6NEf3xpX3OZz/9gS6RJKgqnwyYhDNlfRdZ+5Vwvwy9x7kMetoOVb\nlCM70IemvzfgOCzEmy/l1fNqZeB0BWOK9fdsbALMswgFk1w64KQAci+IRdvy0wi5\n/Lvr+LJfqU9HMpwf4TudfJDlg5NqVNFe67kgCL8ZnUaSeFJoz+tJXe36GL+51q3I\nKpxv5x23rjPGE4z2mUc/bHYJx1Srqpud9ZfHKy5fuGzM8RRXiPVdnraszz7ISnL4\n7haUFdPrTltOFCdWkt98\n=CZdm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2d52ec7b8e4de57531483ec1fc7fb953c6b6b8c9\nparent b4f0f3eff1303ea445a218afb039e0079df0afce\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782313543 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782313543 +0100\n\nAdd a bounded filesystem walk RPC (#29841)\n\nStack 1 of 3. Follow-ups: #29842 and #29844.\n\n## What changes\n\nAdds a general bounded `fs/walk` operation to the exec server.\n\nThe operation returns file and directory entries plus recoverable\nper-path errors. It skips symlinks, preserves the existing filesystem\nsandbox routing, and enforces depth, directory, entry, and response-size\nlimits.\n\nThis PR only defines and wires the filesystem operation. It does not\nchange any callers yet.","verified_at":"2026-06-24T15:05:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c14623d04c97c87b38193b454a10168b4eee8edf","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c14623d04c97c87b38193b454a10168b4eee8edf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c14623d04c97c87b38193b454a10168b4eee8edf/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b4f0f3eff1303ea445a218afb039e0079df0afce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b4f0f3eff1303ea445a218afb039e0079df0afce","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b4f0f3eff1303ea445a218afb039e0079df0afce"}]},{"sha":"b4f0f3eff1303ea445a218afb039e0079df0afce","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGI0ZjBmM2VmZjEzMDNlYTQ0NWEyMThhZmIwMzllMDA3OWRmMGFmY2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T14:43:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T14:43:10Z"},"message":"Persist agent messages as response items (#29829)\n\n## Why\n\nInter-agent messages are recorded in live history as\n`ResponseItem::AgentMessage`, but rollouts stored\n`InterAgentCommunication` and rebuilt the response item during resume.\nThis made the rollout differ from the actual Responses history.\n\n## What changed\n\n- store the prepared `agent_message` response item directly\n- keep `trigger_turn` in a small local metadata record for fork\ntruncation\n- keep reading older `inter_agent_communication` rollout items","tree":{"sha":"98c3ff526f3893700bba1ec355bb783b192d629f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/98c3ff526f3893700bba1ec355bb783b192d629f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b4f0f3eff1303ea445a218afb039e0079df0afce","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO+z+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+7gQAAbNjM/XNI+RPDrKvcAnh1Ty\n/k43tCiHDhZ4eDH0gUULf6UpSPPRzgYebGZ2NiP73jVn0I106r7PbliPCmgw4rxA\nrHbcmjhkdm/gGm8YyuJ+S0bfqKXAGzUuC5nDgMn+pblk0afCX10tsWsmc3ZKx+N9\nyy3mButECqJOU1lYWHQPNIwey+7oUF87SGyl3zQHpXLDcrQivl9D21XrMyGSPELw\nbA7BRbqYreeHM3qnjhfS3He9TfUiLjYpUaDtuc02uQQaC2qC7dlpvrEP4pCBdIe8\na/ocmQ9C3bsJD//9oYUBX1ZBXBjKnc3oiGh9FHjnbSfgbP+RYIMZiu6fOkJYcq3f\nrxAEU6LlnfcFmIvBZWsi33rxjmsgJroJsvVjEOhX5TvhtcwwUwIYk7l5UsChUXsM\nYRQ7TAFSzZuwsGXasQkFbJ0QDp/EJJkzz2f00iyWv6w+I2G66i+M4ha3vFHL7qcu\nEngKQWezZkC+l78nVYfbQ027+cnklbcLelAcQb04/Z2iC1Ja+JbArWm7n+2S1cpL\nnYsJADbnHEioAS0mlD0mInlxXrWLVL/mPrXxE+u/PR2COu+PKiWBAv42RlLyJEbQ\nR5H0o6yuag01zOpFa/1oxxrxe893IreC3vNJg/z3lUEac9z6djBxCadzpvXn9pGF\nQ9cYB091lC09eMfjwIci\n=FpoC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 98c3ff526f3893700bba1ec355bb783b192d629f\nparent f959e7fc9832dfa0ebfb6542ab1bbf829638ac24\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782312190 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782312190 +0100\n\nPersist agent messages as response items (#29829)\n\n## Why\n\nInter-agent messages are recorded in live history as\n`ResponseItem::AgentMessage`, but rollouts stored\n`InterAgentCommunication` and rebuilt the response item during resume.\nThis made the rollout differ from the actual Responses history.\n\n## What changed\n\n- store the prepared `agent_message` response item directly\n- keep `trigger_turn` in a small local metadata record for fork\ntruncation\n- keep reading older `inter_agent_communication` rollout items","verified_at":"2026-06-24T14:43:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b4f0f3eff1303ea445a218afb039e0079df0afce","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b4f0f3eff1303ea445a218afb039e0079df0afce","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b4f0f3eff1303ea445a218afb039e0079df0afce/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f959e7fc9832dfa0ebfb6542ab1bbf829638ac24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f959e7fc9832dfa0ebfb6542ab1bbf829638ac24","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f959e7fc9832dfa0ebfb6542ab1bbf829638ac24"}]},{"sha":"f959e7fc9832dfa0ebfb6542ab1bbf829638ac24","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY5NTllN2ZjOTgzMmRmYTBlYmZiNjU0MmFiMWJiZjgyOTYzOGFjMjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"alexsong-oai","email":"alexsong@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T08:57:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T08:57:34Z"},"message":"[codex] Emit implicit skill usage for support reads (#29731)\n\n## Summary\n- Index all enabled skills for command-based usage detection, regardless\nof `allow_implicit_invocation`.\n- Preserve `allow_implicit_invocation` for the model-visible implicit\nrouting list.\n- Add regression coverage for a support/preflight skill whose `SKILL.md`\nis read and whose script is run while implicit invocation is disabled.\n\n## Root cause\n`allow_implicit_invocation` was used for both model routing and\ncommand-based usage-event detection. That meant support skills like\n`data-analytics:user-context` could be read or run by other skills, but\nthose accesses could not emit implicit usage events.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core-skills\nservice::tests::skills_for_config_indexes_usage_detection_for_non_implicit_skills`\n- `just test -p codex-core-skills` now has the new test passing, but 3\nunrelated local tests fail because\n`/Users/alexsong/.agents/skills/test/SKILL.md` is invalid/missing YAML\nfrontmatter.","tree":{"sha":"926ec0f658c2741be33354975b29d7d64b48874d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/926ec0f658c2741be33354975b29d7d64b48874d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f959e7fc9832dfa0ebfb6542ab1bbf829638ac24","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO5v+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5IYQABAGkqcnP9gt7+eFfTyGL8b+\n8Cmyz/MDcIXCzmfupcRTwGjSO6fqpA5tCTLp0QEW+Cv8zM2iejlQacvSh0G4rd50\n7bZJxoXsM9UrV4L+QXNH4M76kR/n9XgitWOtf+xS0uMiH9Bm1VUSpko+XTEgp8b2\nhZC2DFsIMLXDLEJjDgmeE4c1nBOmfbg8VdZYFZsOdyja4Qgkir6cY7FsPGZAFDfL\nz0lGDvUfMvP6EuRoCHQryYhHTg0Ofpe6vK+mhZN8ya1hd6shj5pKn0JisUkpcOGa\nfksVLh2ft2XTyNbenqdbS4g6iFJny+2700sOmU7/pG7m0BLLASw/PnX6bJLnUOgl\n+YzZ2mPWArhJkTVyMn7mzRLLTw/0gkYgPuMluMX5pC57/INEYwtxXo7EOUaSGUhZ\nOwscPWP5/cDSEmSOtKZwBl4r1/n5ghESUOA+0+rBLMJzGbVUSdqzj9hgxuZLrc8Y\n7hgCgFq+9pPhCGfmuoALhGcA20qh6iE2d1JKYG1poUg252Mt/EYuVJhSFIlT5cg3\nJqCsv52jO+brUGo5zcjtuHwsG/YwyG79GBrf5KtlHd8nMuagGTcOmW81V+ku64qK\ndrMd/E0um91vkpeM9mD2pj/K0ONkqB4Wh/gvOykjjdegyu9j8JdT6kFW4yvWx5Jp\nuIE8HQEzu56l/PUGpvXa\n=MpHb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 926ec0f658c2741be33354975b29d7d64b48874d\nparent 3e39e92f03431a83d004d9ecdb90d8c82fc24d02\nauthor alexsong-oai <alexsong@openai.com> 1782291454 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782291454 +0000\n\n[codex] Emit implicit skill usage for support reads (#29731)\n\n## Summary\n- Index all enabled skills for command-based usage detection, regardless\nof `allow_implicit_invocation`.\n- Preserve `allow_implicit_invocation` for the model-visible implicit\nrouting list.\n- Add regression coverage for a support/preflight skill whose `SKILL.md`\nis read and whose script is run while implicit invocation is disabled.\n\n## Root cause\n`allow_implicit_invocation` was used for both model routing and\ncommand-based usage-event detection. That meant support skills like\n`data-analytics:user-context` could be read or run by other skills, but\nthose accesses could not emit implicit usage events.\n\n## Validation\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core-skills\nservice::tests::skills_for_config_indexes_usage_detection_for_non_implicit_skills`\n- `just test -p codex-core-skills` now has the new test passing, but 3\nunrelated local tests fail because\n`/Users/alexsong/.agents/skills/test/SKILL.md` is invalid/missing YAML\nfrontmatter.","verified_at":"2026-06-24T08:57:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f959e7fc9832dfa0ebfb6542ab1bbf829638ac24","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f959e7fc9832dfa0ebfb6542ab1bbf829638ac24","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f959e7fc9832dfa0ebfb6542ab1bbf829638ac24/comments","author":{"login":"alexsong-oai","id":256201575,"node_id":"U_kgDOD0VTZw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256201575?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/alexsong-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3e39e92f03431a83d004d9ecdb90d8c82fc24d02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3e39e92f03431a83d004d9ecdb90d8c82fc24d02","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3e39e92f03431a83d004d9ecdb90d8c82fc24d02"}]},{"sha":"3e39e92f03431a83d004d9ecdb90d8c82fc24d02","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDNlMzllOTJmMDM0MzFhODNkMDA0ZDllY2RiOTBkOGM4MmZjMjRkMDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T08:46:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T08:46:07Z"},"message":"Keep executor plugin MCP paths URI-native (#29628)\n\n## Why\n\nExecutor-owned plugin roots are `PathUri`, but MCP config normalization\nstill converts them into a native `Path` using the app-server host's\nrules. Relative `cwd` values can therefore resolve against the wrong\nfilesystem when host and executor path conventions differ.\n\nThis PR keeps executor MCP paths URI-native until the selected\nenvironment launches the server, while retaining the existing host\nparser behavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Keep one shared MCP normalization path with narrow host-`Path` and\nexecutor-`PathUri` entrypoints.\n- Preserve native host resolution for locally installed plugin MCP\nconfigs.\n- For executor configs, default `cwd` to the plugin root and resolve\nrelative working directories with the root URI's path convention.\n- Accept explicit executor `file:` URIs only when they remain within the\nselected plugin root.\n- Preserve the selected environment id and existing remote\nenvironment-variable ownership rules.\n- Route the executor plugin provider through the URI-native entrypoint\nwithout converting the root on the host.\n- Ensure `codex doctor` does not probe executor-owned stdio commands or\nforeign working directories on the host.\n- Cover foreign Windows roots, relative and absolute executor working\ndirectories, traversal rejection, runtime resolution, and doctor\nbehavior.\n\n```text\nplugin root:    file:///C:/plugins/demo\nconfigured cwd: scripts\n                  |\n                  v\nresolved cwd:  file:///C:/plugins/demo/scripts\n                  |\n                  v\nlaunch through the selected executor\n```\n\nNo new provider or filesystem abstraction is introduced.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #29614 — add lexical `PathUri` containment.\n2. #29620 — share URI-native manifest path resolution.\n3. #28918 — keep selected plugin roots and resources URI-native.\n4. #29626 — load executor skills without host path conversion.\n5. **This PR** — resolve executor MCP working directories without host\npath conversion.","tree":{"sha":"c02919eae3148e19bbf43d9704863f095440f8e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c02919eae3148e19bbf43d9704863f095440f8e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/3e39e92f03431a83d004d9ecdb90d8c82fc24d02","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO5lPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3twQAH7ZcuOHn96R0E/q3VKfBHW6\nUXP0Wt8gHj1aOvPuFV+sH9Ud/Sma4M82nl4iIcFpfUR4+G41rz9nrcfSJFot6DWe\nFG0WEZ6d2VBoZmtkrce8xrUHxkXFi1H0F5kKvoUeTPQkeC3GnkfPX5yBcpHgSKPw\nhJqCxibTbj15yB0MSjb3B5ne1y1cX/9Ufmgz14spiJi1Zq2gZuw6HoJXDpnRnL3y\nAlyo5WEJ/WLa9EGcdtXunAui37IhGy04Uetbl+ow/4lew/ZjRMAokXXwqSQBgS5V\nY73XO9W3l/+qEtKonHSig8p8yqtHki+zHSUBRwIg9LqrIRcywxYgBnBsWKA85TRN\n+vAtQvLpD5fWTqGgROHd7KaklGL3K23Hs4SRfY5Q+r/l+riKEK/IexjayA4J/DcZ\nsqHz0ZoLYkDFENBWPI35HN2OE54sCCG4fnjhYVZyX7rRQKVu/f6Lh7rO+FT3lWJz\nuRXPgePBqTF1t7tGdp8wYF2SoJF4UDbM/ymU2w0yH7AvkKXgfPqYTMg+lDcySJyw\nS+zRSfir3/SxZNgFex+4y16OkFegN9C3YbPfloLTptVjP03DOla19s3fjrJicr78\n7E063+kFtXMPwv45VbRbTsjNzWNsuBsMLQsEU/aPnfbMvsjQ8yszEh2romWpATh3\nBGku+DIQe3W2dD1pNssv\n=+Gmc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c02919eae3148e19bbf43d9704863f095440f8e2\nparent 2a320fedb53bc0ce89d2887e5b8c2896bc079ca7\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782290767 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782290767 +0100\n\nKeep executor plugin MCP paths URI-native (#29628)\n\n## Why\n\nExecutor-owned plugin roots are `PathUri`, but MCP config normalization\nstill converts them into a native `Path` using the app-server host's\nrules. Relative `cwd` values can therefore resolve against the wrong\nfilesystem when host and executor path conventions differ.\n\nThis PR keeps executor MCP paths URI-native until the selected\nenvironment launches the server, while retaining the existing host\nparser behavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Keep one shared MCP normalization path with narrow host-`Path` and\nexecutor-`PathUri` entrypoints.\n- Preserve native host resolution for locally installed plugin MCP\nconfigs.\n- For executor configs, default `cwd` to the plugin root and resolve\nrelative working directories with the root URI's path convention.\n- Accept explicit executor `file:` URIs only when they remain within the\nselected plugin root.\n- Preserve the selected environment id and existing remote\nenvironment-variable ownership rules.\n- Route the executor plugin provider through the URI-native entrypoint\nwithout converting the root on the host.\n- Ensure `codex doctor` does not probe executor-owned stdio commands or\nforeign working directories on the host.\n- Cover foreign Windows roots, relative and absolute executor working\ndirectories, traversal rejection, runtime resolution, and doctor\nbehavior.\n\n```text\nplugin root:    file:///C:/plugins/demo\nconfigured cwd: scripts\n                  |\n                  v\nresolved cwd:  file:///C:/plugins/demo/scripts\n                  |\n                  v\nlaunch through the selected executor\n```\n\nNo new provider or filesystem abstraction is introduced.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #29614 — add lexical `PathUri` containment.\n2. #29620 — share URI-native manifest path resolution.\n3. #28918 — keep selected plugin roots and resources URI-native.\n4. #29626 — load executor skills without host path conversion.\n5. **This PR** — resolve executor MCP working directories without host\npath conversion.","verified_at":"2026-06-24T08:46:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3e39e92f03431a83d004d9ecdb90d8c82fc24d02","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3e39e92f03431a83d004d9ecdb90d8c82fc24d02","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3e39e92f03431a83d004d9ecdb90d8c82fc24d02/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2a320fedb53bc0ce89d2887e5b8c2896bc079ca7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2a320fedb53bc0ce89d2887e5b8c2896bc079ca7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2a320fedb53bc0ce89d2887e5b8c2896bc079ca7"}]},{"sha":"2a320fedb53bc0ce89d2887e5b8c2896bc079ca7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDJhMzIwZmVkYjUzYmMwY2U4OWQyODg3ZTViOGMyODk2YmMwNzljYTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"rhan-oai","email":"rhan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T07:15:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T07:15:04Z"},"message":"[codex] Remove auto-compaction opt-out (#29815)\n\n## Summary\n\n- remove the default-on `auto_compaction` feature flag and generated\nconfig schema entries\n- restore unconditional pre-turn, model-switch/hash, and mid-turn\nautomatic compaction\n- expose `new_context` whenever token-budget tooling is enabled\n- remove the disabled-auto-compaction integration coverage introduced by\n#28260\n\n## Motivation\n\nRoll back the internal auto-compaction escape hatch added in #28260.\nAutomatic compaction should no longer be suppressible with `--disable\nauto_compaction`; existing manual `/compact` behavior remains unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just write-config-schema`\n- `just test -p codex-features` — 53 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core 'suite::compact::'` — 36 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core\nsuite::token_budget::new_context_tool_starts_new_window_before_follow_up`\n— 1 passed\n- `just fix -p codex-core -p codex-features`\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core` — 2,778 passed, 59 failed, 16 skipped;\nfailures were outside the changed compaction paths and were dominated by\nmissing first-party test binaries and shell-snapshot timeouts","tree":{"sha":"7ff3ba5bff454b90671b6b8ed5d2c0a15fc3e625","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7ff3ba5bff454b90671b6b8ed5d2c0a15fc3e625"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2a320fedb53bc0ce89d2887e5b8c2896bc079ca7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO4P4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdy0QABP/yaidb0u0rThzx1Ngf8nP\n2vPOVcrHCisHcnZUvtkiKT6FKEfskBejjWTxmBuA1U4mjujf4oDux9FJxLta7vT7\nP6UtRAWBHsRcg7V/o1t/ugwhG354aoJ1y8pmK95w/1ehmVCksXN/mMGPVFT/3ByN\nG8V9tbUGLrzxQsvlAkVdL6LqWy9MI0YvcVoonVgUknaWTQyXYX1nRH5JffU9Tzyx\nV+7zom68UWVAN6KlYHvfwPvzYYakNJhYEyY3VRRKV7jiAUNACka040maHuH+Vzti\n1rnqzwjXDJvxYKNg0fg9GtiXMRyjtWmpfjLI2VshKJlFyTeIRlCTLuZ3Ly1OkwiT\nEheF3cK8VLv3wCwa9LBfS9iDt62cx4uWRcojmY5ntAkV9/diqpqWeeocAaXqcwdw\n0HA919nqhIH/5A2Xxk9Ec7nejksCWGLJa3LbexqE4jJ4mVWHAtSJvsx6ibkBIzVi\n8ka2AV3Mo9u9XiPK26zFiDFwj4JQ/q+5a7gBuIXI1JlOxuJOemiqOrarZX7naI8F\n55fKUqSsy5ESDYvMZLS4dJGWKixzovyEJAUFbXvNGQnd2AIkKXmtacLjGRyTn/7v\n48uFi/9ib0VXz3GJJacmt1HHPOHcPfqukDHI1dg5MQ3G8yVduh+ri8Pbumt2Y7RS\nIqSd3X1Y3qLvIT276sEL\n=iB7W\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7ff3ba5bff454b90671b6b8ed5d2c0a15fc3e625\nparent 31e428a1ef3396a0e962687e61f11c224b9f4dbc\nauthor rhan-oai <rhan@openai.com> 1782285304 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782285304 -0700\n\n[codex] Remove auto-compaction opt-out (#29815)\n\n## Summary\n\n- remove the default-on `auto_compaction` feature flag and generated\nconfig schema entries\n- restore unconditional pre-turn, model-switch/hash, and mid-turn\nautomatic compaction\n- expose `new_context` whenever token-budget tooling is enabled\n- remove the disabled-auto-compaction integration coverage introduced by\n#28260\n\n## Motivation\n\nRoll back the internal auto-compaction escape hatch added in #28260.\nAutomatic compaction should no longer be suppressible with `--disable\nauto_compaction`; existing manual `/compact` behavior remains unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just write-config-schema`\n- `just test -p codex-features` — 53 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core 'suite::compact::'` — 36 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core\nsuite::token_budget::new_context_tool_starts_new_window_before_follow_up`\n— 1 passed\n- `just fix -p codex-core -p codex-features`\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core` — 2,778 passed, 59 failed, 16 skipped;\nfailures were outside the changed compaction paths and were dominated by\nmissing first-party test binaries and shell-snapshot timeouts","verified_at":"2026-06-24T07:15:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2a320fedb53bc0ce89d2887e5b8c2896bc079ca7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2a320fedb53bc0ce89d2887e5b8c2896bc079ca7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2a320fedb53bc0ce89d2887e5b8c2896bc079ca7/comments","author":{"login":"rhan-oai","id":214716640,"node_id":"U_kgDODMxQ4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214716640?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/