ance types (#29722)\n\n## Why\n\nConfig layer provenance describes how effective configuration was\nassembled, so it belongs with the config loader rather than in\napp-server's serialized API types.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Moved `ConfigLayerSource`, `ConfigLayerMetadata`, and `ConfigLayer`\nownership into `codex-config`.\n- Kept app-server's wire payloads unchanged and added explicit\nconversions at the app boundary.\n- Removed lower-level app-server-protocol dependencies from config\nconsumers.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is PR 3 of 6, stacked on [PR\n#29721](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29721). Review only the\ndelta from `codex/split-auth-domain-types`. Next: [PR\n#29723](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29723).\n\n## Validation\n\n- `codex-config` coverage passed.\n- App-server config-manager and config RPC coverage passed.","tree":{"sha":"14e4839ce3f06fc447eed4aea76195ccb5ebb3c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/14e4839ce3f06fc447eed4aea76195ccb5ebb3c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1d65ccabd59795b0342bd4a60bd1944f5cc4763e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO1b4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnfYQAHBRMrcwxYytf2MYYUDN2l/O\nfijLchOxkHK83cgqffyDuJM2uHlymO80CSZmHQuUB2p7Qod2D9G2sM76JhkxDClF\nqoy0BVLzKWckVoqXeUv9EmhFK+qosCTofxlFuDenulpke1GbBtgbZM98u737nD8e\nX1JictuPq0IXRXy96/isOrrRPybOSDCYCmjllOz1iPNzZeY3jSl1wLIfwfGSXX/U\nHTimKV0dYbpUtlNVMGl+XwO4Y7z2+3belvm60QUKbtUGzP7lbzn6Mex2cooEc6Wl\npOd8bNQyv0Pi5pGXC4+rdiUnvvPCX1wEza/cz7XFa7y/qBcnsqiuJ581Qzo01sdV\n5kpoXgO0XS6wXtkEeOF38nqSDsRzVcWsyK/6jHxvAPw5I7jGtxvPVzI2/3+VmAj8\nr6ZcD3GArWj7DkUNR0fH3d96MrtAa640AXLwT90jhMjfsQPrVLcyDBqA3kDr1GNT\nsY5lCLfnTG1AgPrtjn44hJcGU9OhHTJhXVtQsPGfSJGqkaANqpw9sxnVmj5d0AKN\n0c7gNBm7FtuYhwO2Ykn2uzmp8xAhFarEZnUSQ/4sSjZUxlFWkbgMdGBEJJZkphzG\nukcew10hoZkkFdxV49fig8OA+QOcETRyQMvRYBiJp4nVxdnttw/Pf/yUsnMKjDfA\n1e4deG2vaaClhJJssAsu\n=6X/G\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 14e4839ce3f06fc447eed4aea76195ccb5ebb3c0\nparent 4fe02f4fcf408125882b103b7d2f85ff1f2a4837\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1782273784 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782273784 +0000\n\nconfig: own layer provenance types (#29722)\n\n## Why\n\nConfig layer provenance describes how effective configuration was\nassembled, so it belongs with the config loader rather than in\napp-server's serialized API types.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Moved `ConfigLayerSource`, `ConfigLayerMetadata`, and `ConfigLayer`\nownership into `codex-config`.\n- Kept app-server's wire payloads unchanged and added explicit\nconversions at the app boundary.\n- Removed lower-level app-server-protocol dependencies from config\nconsumers.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is PR 3 of 6, stacked on [PR\n#29721](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29721). Review only the\ndelta from `codex/split-auth-domain-types`. Next: [PR\n#29723](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29723).\n\n## Validation\n\n- `codex-config` coverage passed.\n- App-server config-manager and config RPC coverage passed.","verified_at":"2026-06-24T04:03:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1d65ccabd59795b0342bd4a60bd1944f5cc4763e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1d65ccabd59795b0342bd4a60bd1944f5cc4763e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1d65ccabd59795b0342bd4a60bd1944f5cc4763e/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4fe02f4fcf408125882b103b7d2f85ff1f2a4837","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4fe02f4fcf408125882b103b7d2f85ff1f2a4837","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4fe02f4fcf408125882b103b7d2f85ff1f2a4837"}]},{"sha":"4fe02f4fcf408125882b103b7d2f85ff1f2a4837","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRmZTAyZjRmY2Y0MDgxMjU4ODJiMTAzYjdkMmY4NWZmMWYyYTQ4Mzc","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T03:13:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T03:13:11Z"},"message":"[plugins] Enforce marketplace source admission requirements (#29753)\n\n## Why\n\nManaged marketplace source requirements only become effective when every\nlocal marketplace mutation path applies the same admission decision.\nThis change centralizes that decision so CLI, app-server, and\nexternal-agent migration flows cannot add, install from, or refresh a\ndisallowed source.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Match exact normalized Git repository URLs with an optional exact\n`ref`.\n- Match Git hosts with managed regular expressions.\n- Match local marketplaces by exact absolute path.\n- Preserve the expected path/name boundary for managed OpenAI\nmarketplaces.\n- Enforce source admission during marketplace add, plugin install, and\nconfigured Git marketplace upgrade.\n- Continue upgrading independent marketplaces when one source is\nrejected and return a per-marketplace error.\n- Load the effective requirements stack at CLI, app-server, and\nexternal-agent migration entry points.\n\nThis PR does not filter already configured marketplaces at runtime; that\nremains in draft follow-up #29691.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is PR 2 of 3 and is based on #29690, which introduces the\nrequirements data shape and merge behavior.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Source matcher coverage for Git URL/ref, host-pattern, local-path, and\nmanaged marketplace cases.\n- Marketplace add and plugin install coverage for allowed and rejected\nsources.\n- Marketplace upgrade coverage for rejection and per-marketplace\ncontinuation.","tree":{"sha":"70d87dad53a5983e112217296673ce3808308efa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/70d87dad53a5983e112217296673ce3808308efa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4fe02f4fcf408125882b103b7d2f85ff1f2a4837","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO0tHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkycQAGZ55sZQ8Y6ANyeincydZ52E\nn/gnVB2JQ9J3wyoHjfC7b8YHKHwbG9NNZ/Z9EbztD+R105Y1GYisvmI5tJdMHhWM\nxGAXlmjyGr5bN2ZO+ssKebWAevO9w5/nMI/g7ZkFZfP6fRx+Gg4bbxYw7aAYQ0Cq\n275Y65CmJ7Vwe3M6amAqEowUGG/g0J++eVUkJ/R6qDRzwQ6v+R2VTsrCo+cLVse0\nBHVIWvOpADnVHRfTSZ9uyaoqs+qjqL/vEYh86RG2RNP/rezSFDQV9Rum+Irnzb2F\nBLOcsijktUqCh2a8ZUrna1lqw9I87JY1F0Bcxg559ewVYgXZwhNG3wkxnC/HlSdk\n/nvNMhZUdYhlJn8ZSlqMBzED4j3B0uf2QqliBKCRr6remksuhkiTUxJ6zYg1J61y\nw52LvdyWTfJDL9ZP/qDNsiJooWjyisSVv+uq7b80/3VLPQHJAc74lUEPJseaBOdH\nawAlpRh1wvfuSh7DS6sEJUfEfzG8G+bf7vyXJZdumx7OwLRE999yOkLb9y4YLWTK\ngul12DwTBn8/Qxjehr5VUSaSXkeKAk7PSGkciHhSpIuYeKntAIAOWBOMw2p9TEYQ\nR6i4yAgyjeH3IunGAhytuhuW7AyLj2Kd/q5ZK6020ycgoumD7kDZ/LzmUxj6u7ES\nR9/GrvYMYyGk/1Up18KV\n=z/82\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 70d87dad53a5983e112217296673ce3808308efa\nparent 31372078d1de71a512e31b4f7f364beeb42c76ac\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1782270791 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782270791 -0700\n\n[plugins] Enforce marketplace source admission requirements (#29753)\n\n## Why\n\nManaged marketplace source requirements only become effective when every\nlocal marketplace mutation path applies the same admission decision.\nThis change centralizes that decision so CLI, app-server, and\nexternal-agent migration flows cannot add, install from, or refresh a\ndisallowed source.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Match exact normalized Git repository URLs with an optional exact\n`ref`.\n- Match Git hosts with managed regular expressions.\n- Match local marketplaces by exact absolute path.\n- Preserve the expected path/name boundary for managed OpenAI\nmarketplaces.\n- Enforce source admission during marketplace add, plugin install, and\nconfigured Git marketplace upgrade.\n- Continue upgrading independent marketplaces when one source is\nrejected and return a per-marketplace error.\n- Load the effective requirements stack at CLI, app-server, and\nexternal-agent migration entry points.\n\nThis PR does not filter already configured marketplaces at runtime; that\nremains in draft follow-up #29691.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is PR 2 of 3 and is based on #29690, which introduces the\nrequirements data shape and merge behavior.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Source matcher coverage for Git URL/ref, host-pattern, local-path, and\nmanaged marketplace cases.\n- Marketplace add and plugin install coverage for allowed and rejected\nsources.\n- Marketplace upgrade coverage for rejection and per-marketplace\ncontinuation.","verified_at":"2026-06-24T03:13:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4fe02f4fcf408125882b103b7d2f85ff1f2a4837","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4fe02f4fcf408125882b103b7d2f85ff1f2a4837","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4fe02f4fcf408125882b103b7d2f85ff1f2a4837/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"31372078d1de71a512e31b4f7f364beeb42c76ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/31372078d1de71a512e31b4f7f364beeb42c76ac","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/31372078d1de71a512e31b4f7f364beeb42c76ac"}]},{"sha":"31372078d1de71a512e31b4f7f364beeb42c76ac","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDMxMzcyMDc4ZDFkZTcxYTUxMmUzMWI0ZjdmMzY0YmVlYjQyYzc2YWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T03:10:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T03:10:20Z"},"message":"auth: move domain mode below app wire types (#29721)\n\n## Why\n\nAuthentication mode is a domain concept used by login, model selection,\ntelemetry, and transports. Keeping the canonical type in app-server\nprotocol forces those lower-level crates to depend on an unrelated wire\nAPI.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added canonical `codex_protocol::auth::AuthMode` domain values.\n- Kept the app-server wire DTO unchanged and added an explicit app-side\nconversion.\n- Removed production app-server-protocol dependencies from login,\nmodel-provider-info, models-manager, and otel call paths.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is PR 2 of 6, stacked on [PR\n#29714](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29714). Review only the\ndelta from `codex/split-json-rpc-protocols`. Next: [PR\n#29722](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29722).\n\n## Validation\n\n- Auth and login coverage passed in the focused protocol/domain test\nrun.\n- App-server account and auth conversion coverage passed.","tree":{"sha":"7c5d85524ee2a09fca240906d39898c64391975d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7c5d85524ee2a09fca240906d39898c64391975d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/31372078d1de71a512e31b4f7f364beeb42c76ac","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO0qcCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnowQAD+tIOWaGVv3q5FHdFIDwn1I\njpe6Kk2b/DsmFtuGkI6kQYsZ6Y/RyY62GXU4YzBDNPAZzvFEGO7YRLxknFcLVlHy\nyM99dIWQi7C0JqsD/cuiZ+laXGRfZUqDKPyvD66Vp+e2GDvmb4kOBPslM4acVWjW\nQbgURtpKxqWtodx072qUzip8s4V69Rx8emBxUkc2TMgMaMAJaP3Sg1o5L7pUhJKo\na5UMzZiTsnloNGYm4LkIuyrpIkO5uDIEzT8md09br4Y/uK2TtjtKOkj81TyTXJb5\nqPQ0377GmkgmZNA1RCSGDPpmXdv+kE7GcjKr0SRHzNxYY43GpwxG6pSQHgnnsyrw\n2QlrAtoTindcJNTnFD9gr2RTevmPf20D6lcL/gZb8LffKLkXbRNoCZCWraF1F3HO\nL7690GhFTpND61Gj1uSWDDfsN9PKqA7lavERYbrb0S+I0lKyR2fgvRr4lm9Kl97q\nYhXeLEEup0JR/Iki8Y7AR12HlsilN1Kd6n4lWGnHJoql6LmdI3JV/st4CkT/zVdH\nrFqoLFB1+OQKzTOAf1TBDevBsVk4Ve6EmwHqCj6tcliTsx3SuFHFhLsnFR4/Y+PS\ntEmSiLx4vegaL/kjWwgySs55jat2Z/80UQqlP8mW9rggXd5b1wIObiGIvpHfgFlC\nQ6dA7mb27DDa0oG8AsPJ\n=05qE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7c5d85524ee2a09fca240906d39898c64391975d\nparent 806a4b66c9ad1f9e901e3e2cfeefdb403a0d6a07\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1782270620 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782270620 +0000\n\nauth: move domain mode below app wire types (#29721)\n\n## Why\n\nAuthentication mode is a domain concept used by login, model selection,\ntelemetry, and transports. Keeping the canonical type in app-server\nprotocol forces those lower-level crates to depend on an unrelated wire\nAPI.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added canonical `codex_protocol::auth::AuthMode` domain values.\n- Kept the app-server wire DTO unchanged and added an explicit app-side\nconversion.\n- Removed production app-server-protocol dependencies from login,\nmodel-provider-info, models-manager, and otel call paths.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is PR 2 of 6, stacked on [PR\n#29714](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29714). Review only the\ndelta from `codex/split-json-rpc-protocols`. Next: [PR\n#29722](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29722).\n\n## Validation\n\n- Auth and login coverage passed in the focused protocol/domain test\nrun.\n- App-server account and auth conversion coverage passed.","verified_at":"2026-06-24T03:10:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/31372078d1de71a512e31b4f7f364beeb42c76ac","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/31372078d1de71a512e31b4f7f364beeb42c76ac","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/31372078d1de71a512e31b4f7f364beeb42c76ac/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"806a4b66c9ad1f9e901e3e2cfeefdb403a0d6a07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/806a4b66c9ad1f9e901e3e2cfeefdb403a0d6a07","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/806a4b66c9ad1f9e901e3e2cfeefdb403a0d6a07"}]},{"sha":"806a4b66c9ad1f9e901e3e2cfeefdb403a0d6a07","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDgwNmE0YjY2YzlhZDFmOWU5MDFlM2UyY2ZlZWZkYjQwM2EwZDZhMDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T03:03:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T03:03:19Z"},"message":"[codex] Assign response item IDs in forked history (#29767)\n\n## Why\n\nFork-specific response items, including the subagent usage hint, are\nappended directly to `InitialHistory::Forked`. This bypasses the normal\nhistory insertion path that assigns missing response item IDs when\n`Feature::ItemIds` is enabled, so the child could reconstruct and\npersist those items without IDs.\n\n## What changed\n\n- When `Feature::ItemIds` is enabled, assign missing IDs to top-level\n`ResponseItem`s while materializing `InitialHistory::Forked`, before\nboth reconstruction and persistence.\n- Preserve existing IDs and use the same owned rollout items for live\nhistory and persistence.\n- Extract the existing single-item ID allocation logic for reuse by the\nfork path.\n- Add coverage that verifies a fork-only developer message receives the\nsame ID in live and persisted history with the feature enabled.\n\nNormal history recording, compacted-history replacement, and fork\nhandling all continue to honor `Feature::ItemIds`. External-agent\nimports, normal resume, and nested legacy compaction checkpoints are\nunchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nrecord_initial_history_reconstructs_forked_transcript`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nrecord_initial_history_assigns_and_persists_id_for_forked_response_item`","tree":{"sha":"3c6a3956ee7c4718ba80379cad639c25bee08a74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3c6a3956ee7c4718ba80379cad639c25bee08a74"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/806a4b66c9ad1f9e901e3e2cfeefdb403a0d6a07","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO0j3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAD8kQAJrJWrdYALRMazHqdDCN0pdo\nwiiVHZLnsPkzGmvT/NyzGP8AXmeeWe65FG2IraKOVbXrt/Q0Ls5TEDULiuNsiFuJ\nW7ah/nQJmbFzXN42NtZad96GJVTozx+++H3vrDwjsFA+w/7c0sGHs/VUM/3J6+7Q\nOZrFluIa4j1aoLT+6DTxzlGmR1VtQodva3fKSX4/MvCYSrAjbVg3v+cVheJ2RgwL\ntnBh94S/poFcRxgDrJu0MP+fXu+y6mwLPpOXoDmmulTqmzoNAmdWJKmUs/vFQ251\n7tfQWkmxQNIag7zt8GJBPzb4LGAcrRqdNOa39l06/04oOt1A9EDNJSldx0ZHQzld\nhSjodqcQZD7c2x65a4kyztzNqlltK4k8Pu3ZTfIMKnIc3d2+EepRW9ewzU4Totoy\nwNpIY2nxYMLW5KQ22FjJi1gHqFffe/QMe11aGVU9zXCbOdHyn/BCdiAOE4cdjCPV\nuaXfdD62yaITY9wnujovm5HcR2Wl+JF5EkD/mbX5kjh6ETHoDRMzEI/b23BjEPPX\n29dIoIpdeEhNyMs5EUZbXTA7QSLBr3tPwCjaf/U7E3nUF1amUPvaCTb7ZPbtiPTX\n+8lsshqj802goqB5g+v4/9OSaAMsSz/pcrjNb3AmhH/Pl2dVzj1tFDrK1/QF56Ry\nRgQq1YTFkfS4RGXGeX8k\n=IRin\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3c6a3956ee7c4718ba80379cad639c25bee08a74\nparent ff78e212155af07ec2db2abbcbd037fbc9d0889f\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1782270199 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782270199 +0000\n\n[codex] Assign response item IDs in forked history (#29767)\n\n## Why\n\nFork-specific response items, including the subagent usage hint, are\nappended directly to `InitialHistory::Forked`. This bypasses the normal\nhistory insertion path that assigns missing response item IDs when\n`Feature::ItemIds` is enabled, so the child could reconstruct and\npersist those items without IDs.\n\n## What changed\n\n- When `Feature::ItemIds` is enabled, assign missing IDs to top-level\n`ResponseItem`s while materializing `InitialHistory::Forked`, before\nboth reconstruction and persistence.\n- Preserve existing IDs and use the same owned rollout items for live\nhistory and persistence.\n- Extract the existing single-item ID allocation logic for reuse by the\nfork path.\n- Add coverage that verifies a fork-only developer message receives the\nsame ID in live and persisted history with the feature enabled.\n\nNormal history recording, compacted-history replacement, and fork\nhandling all continue to honor `Feature::ItemIds`. External-agent\nimports, normal resume, and nested legacy compaction checkpoints are\nunchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nrecord_initial_history_reconstructs_forked_transcript`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nrecord_initial_history_assigns_and_persists_id_for_forked_response_item`","verified_at":"2026-06-24T03:03:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/806a4b66c9ad1f9e901e3e2cfeefdb403a0d6a07","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/806a4b66c9ad1f9e901e3e2cfeefdb403a0d6a07","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/806a4b66c9ad1f9e901e3e2cfeefdb403a0d6a07/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ff78e212155af07ec2db2abbcbd037fbc9d0889f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ff78e212155af07ec2db2abbcbd037fbc9d0889f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ff78e212155af07ec2db2abbcbd037fbc9d0889f"}]},{"sha":"ff78e212155af07ec2db2abbcbd037fbc9d0889f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZmNzhlMjEyMTU1YWYwN2VjMmRiMmFiYmNiZDAzN2ZiYzlkMDg4OWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T02:51:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T02:51:31Z"},"message":"[codex] Ignore local curated plugins when remote catalog is active (#29765)\n\n## Summary\n\n- suppress configured `openai-curated` plugins when the remote plugin\nfeature is enabled and auth uses the Codex backend\n- preserve `openai-api-curated` and non-Codex-backend behavior while\nincluding remote catalog activation in the plugin load cache key\n- add core plugin coverage and an app-server integration test for\nruntime feature enablement\n\n## Why\n\nThe Codex app enables remote plugins through process-local runtime\nfeature enablement, which can happen after app-server startup tasks have\nalready observed legacy local plugin state. The existing conflict logic\nonly preferred a remote plugin when the same plugin was already\ninstalled remotely, so a configured legacy-only plugin could continue\nexposing skills and other capabilities from `openai-curated`.\n\n## Impact\n\nWhen the remote catalog is active, legacy `openai-curated` plugins no\nlonger contribute skills, MCP servers, apps, or hooks. Remote installed\nplugins continue to load normally, and `openai-api-curated` remains\nunaffected. This does not change remote fetch, bundle sync, or uninstall\nbehavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins\nremote_global_catalog_ignores_local_curated_plugins\nremote_plugin_feature_keeps_local_curated_without_codex_backend`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nruntime_remote_plugin_enablement_excludes_local_curated_plugin_skills`\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"9f36da0c6981da95c9baf6a91966e313aaf0b10d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9f36da0c6981da95c9baf6a91966e313aaf0b10d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ff78e212155af07ec2db2abbcbd037fbc9d0889f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO0YzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU2EQAJyBrCTS8ZTLxxyFia+y2C1+\nqqt7RfAk/tT9WszVpH2U+Fkwra23DODiT9C3TbcHQpLyBY0yGfkAcyEwF7k0/Sh7\n698BSd0zufxkM2e79y+Ml+mNEuQVVivbFIAwlbnxNvTmuiN0DYvptExLYZtV3S2O\nEvHUhgoc4kZT58hM2qKbxJj66mQJNc2SOXaxcfrcQNmkfsC8rHYWXoV4YPmuz6iC\naP4WExxgiPWyiXma/42t2+JmdmdLo7CXRmxdhaOHI5BH1LZv03RmFqsAnywHFPBu\nfjqxoQXCBg1ypuBeuHBsP9X9VJA6nWlzVrJF3S+WDhNXm5+kwI8/54WF77fEzMo0\nI8kAqbMRyeOpVLfIVmQn7DSO8sIfIUb0UX9CE3VvPlyyt6QAx2oBv8el8nEH2tFK\nV1pg/wzxrZVuC4xe/h+GyyrieITNfKkEO52ubaYd+toWj0UAMiEAcfnXAhUDQCD8\nI7UzUYNTVa7XitwiUbkl00e8NwG2C/Ckuwmat3iLWanIiHsY+NX9AqsqPs17JHsQ\nKtFp3fkX/H4LFK2hZshEUQtSTAIqAi43AFad/dAv6UVreLxky/gUWWzodxO84poL\nBcWiiNGGoSwL8kvN+19R0w1ApmiDiAN/Vqawpog+vbbaPkPunGtAahtEnBLNIU/k\nRwqLYebHvAC13Yto1CP9\n=ncBd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9f36da0c6981da95c9baf6a91966e313aaf0b10d\nparent 2696e7199bd964aed3811e386235703d4966db27\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1782269491 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782269491 -0700\n\n[codex] Ignore local curated plugins when remote catalog is active (#29765)\n\n## Summary\n\n- suppress configured `openai-curated` plugins when the remote plugin\nfeature is enabled and auth uses the Codex backend\n- preserve `openai-api-curated` and non-Codex-backend behavior while\nincluding remote catalog activation in the plugin load cache key\n- add core plugin coverage and an app-server integration test for\nruntime feature enablement\n\n## Why\n\nThe Codex app enables remote plugins through process-local runtime\nfeature enablement, which can happen after app-server startup tasks have\nalready observed legacy local plugin state. The existing conflict logic\nonly preferred a remote plugin when the same plugin was already\ninstalled remotely, so a configured legacy-only plugin could continue\nexposing skills and other capabilities from `openai-curated`.\n\n## Impact\n\nWhen the remote catalog is active, legacy `openai-curated` plugins no\nlonger contribute skills, MCP servers, apps, or hooks. Remote installed\nplugins continue to load normally, and `openai-api-curated` remains\nunaffected. This does not change remote fetch, bundle sync, or uninstall\nbehavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins\nremote_global_catalog_ignores_local_curated_plugins\nremote_plugin_feature_keeps_local_curated_without_codex_backend`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nruntime_remote_plugin_enablement_excludes_local_curated_plugin_skills`\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-24T02:51:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ff78e212155af07ec2db2abbcbd037fbc9d0889f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ff78e212155af07ec2db2abbcbd037fbc9d0889f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ff78e212155af07ec2db2abbcbd037fbc9d0889f/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2696e7199bd964aed3811e386235703d4966db27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2696e7199bd964aed3811e386235703d4966db27","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2696e7199bd964aed3811e386235703d4966db27"}]},{"sha":"2696e7199bd964aed3811e386235703d4966db27","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDI2OTZlNzE5OWJkOTY0YWVkMzgxMWUzODYyMzU3MDNkNDk2NmRiMjc","commit":{"author":{"name":"xl-openai","email":"xl@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T02:42:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T02:42:13Z"},"message":"[plugins] Add marketplace source requirements (#29690)\n\n## Why\n\nManaged deployments need a mergeable way to declare which marketplace\nsources Codex may use. An enterprise-keyed TOML table avoids array merge\nambiguity and lets every requirements layer use the existing config\nprecedence rules without a marketplace-specific merger.\n\n## Requirements shape\n\n```toml\n[marketplaces]\nrestrict_to_allowed_sources = true\n\n[marketplaces.allowed_sources.company_plugins]\nsource = \"git\"\nurl = \"https://github.com/example/company-plugins.git\"\nref = \"main\"\n\n[marketplaces.allowed_sources.internal_git]\nsource = \"host_pattern\"\nhost_pattern = \"^git\\\\.example\\\\.com$\"\n\n[marketplaces.allowed_sources.local_plugins]\nsource = \"local\"\npath = \"/opt/company/codex-plugins\"\n```\n\n`restrict_to_allowed_sources` follows normal scalar precedence.\n`allowed_sources` follows normal recursive TOML table merge behavior:\ndistinct keys accumulate and fields under the same key use normal layer\nprecedence. The final `source` value later selects which fields the\nmarketplace admission policy interprets.\n\nThe raw rule fields remain optional while requirements layers are\ncomposed, so a higher-priority layer can override only `ref`, `url`, or\nanother individual field. Source-specific validation and normalization\nintentionally belong to the marketplace admission layer, not\nrequirements merging.\n\nThis initial shape includes `git`, `host_pattern`, and `local` sources.\nIt does not add npm or path-pattern rules.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add the marketplace requirements TOML shape to\n`ConfigRequirementsToml`, `ConfigRequirementsWithSources`, and\n`ConfigRequirements`.\n- Carry marketplace requirements through the existing regular\nrequirements merge path.\n- Keep allowed-source entries as raw partial tables for downstream\npolicy interpretation.\n- Cover partial same-key overlays, source changes, unknown fields, and\nunmodified local paths.\n\nThis PR defines and composes the requirements only. Source admission is\nimplemented by the next PR in the stack.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is PR 1 of 3. #29753 adds source admission on top of this PR; draft\n#29691 will add runtime enforcement after it is rebased later.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-config marketplace_`","tree":{"sha":"69e2b00cd5e67902b209565dedaa29fe13d71e58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/69e2b00cd5e67902b209565dedaa29fe13d71e58"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2696e7199bd964aed3811e386235703d4966db27","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO0QGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzewQAA1vBHwCyZHzX+VU5wFUq8mR\nz/lrvDvLt3AM3fMY1cy9+5Uvic5KjEy6ud8T/D0pASB7ihz5nnlPs1IHrs+n8xFM\nbRZftQW6K/+XYfREnOfidVbT5mHX8zgrqtewOhIK7TgqXZTEmBvaIT3SFB6CUd3l\nODtboH5UWYILG/voefUKZRB22lv94ZeDyuE9ehZnws4CyHzK6l1t+FN4g+DjA0tu\n4Acge0ai1FCsXM5Kr7D1vB5yhDTxo2sK0tk6lkbAMLtAFUen2vSpKmuZaTkxRnHq\n44xnQ29u9Lp80WVi/OYVyzQTVaXXfOjkhPktXcn6wQ19roELlcMUXRP1Hmhiw0Zw\nEHPA5x+M6yBOvXs/DKLEd9BJfAfQA7loX1Wh14pAHcHirfU33fXghCYsiY9njNRD\nm/J+xeWK1MYJrgCA5QR7DHp8ybkoGQBKG6eyJu0mAsC6LA5Q5RPkiBS2LHGt9dwd\n7yIB6+ApGdRkE770sdny42ylQwNEro3psswt2siit+8y4/fhA6kJxq2VAgcuLfGm\nhEzBc648VG3DcN5/JnZj6xyOFcY37fPJb5N8QrQSqHOrn0xxDH6pcGGptZr46FGo\noQR0NyW2Zk73DJfhu2at0epgr4+U6EwSJ+0HM7sPlANLJokAjAK8Foe1rkxyIkYJ\nJJISj7CSTyEYoGQs+P2f\n=1ln0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 69e2b00cd5e67902b209565dedaa29fe13d71e58\nparent 6f65b9a98c4172fac9ba7200a9c498e91fcb84ec\nauthor xl-openai <xl@openai.com> 1782268933 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782268933 -0700\n\n[plugins] Add marketplace source requirements (#29690)\n\n## Why\n\nManaged deployments need a mergeable way to declare which marketplace\nsources Codex may use. An enterprise-keyed TOML table avoids array merge\nambiguity and lets every requirements layer use the existing config\nprecedence rules without a marketplace-specific merger.\n\n## Requirements shape\n\n```toml\n[marketplaces]\nrestrict_to_allowed_sources = true\n\n[marketplaces.allowed_sources.company_plugins]\nsource = \"git\"\nurl = \"https://github.com/example/company-plugins.git\"\nref = \"main\"\n\n[marketplaces.allowed_sources.internal_git]\nsource = \"host_pattern\"\nhost_pattern = \"^git\\\\.example\\\\.com$\"\n\n[marketplaces.allowed_sources.local_plugins]\nsource = \"local\"\npath = \"/opt/company/codex-plugins\"\n```\n\n`restrict_to_allowed_sources` follows normal scalar precedence.\n`allowed_sources` follows normal recursive TOML table merge behavior:\ndistinct keys accumulate and fields under the same key use normal layer\nprecedence. The final `source` value later selects which fields the\nmarketplace admission policy interprets.\n\nThe raw rule fields remain optional while requirements layers are\ncomposed, so a higher-priority layer can override only `ref`, `url`, or\nanother individual field. Source-specific validation and normalization\nintentionally belong to the marketplace admission layer, not\nrequirements merging.\n\nThis initial shape includes `git`, `host_pattern`, and `local` sources.\nIt does not add npm or path-pattern rules.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add the marketplace requirements TOML shape to\n`ConfigRequirementsToml`, `ConfigRequirementsWithSources`, and\n`ConfigRequirements`.\n- Carry marketplace requirements through the existing regular\nrequirements merge path.\n- Keep allowed-source entries as raw partial tables for downstream\npolicy interpretation.\n- Cover partial same-key overlays, source changes, unknown fields, and\nunmodified local paths.\n\nThis PR defines and composes the requirements only. Source admission is\nimplemented by the next PR in the stack.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is PR 1 of 3. #29753 adds source admission on top of this PR; draft\n#29691 will add runtime enforcement after it is rebased later.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-config marketplace_`","verified_at":"2026-06-24T02:42:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2696e7199bd964aed3811e386235703d4966db27","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2696e7199bd964aed3811e386235703d4966db27","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2696e7199bd964aed3811e386235703d4966db27/comments","author":{"login":"xl-openai","id":184293535,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvwYnw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184293535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/xl-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xl-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6f65b9a98c4172fac9ba7200a9c498e91fcb84ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6f65b9a98c4172fac9ba7200a9c498e91fcb84ec","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6f65b9a98c4172fac9ba7200a9c498e91fcb84ec"}]},{"sha":"6f65b9a98c4172fac9ba7200a9c498e91fcb84ec","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZmNjViOWE5OGM0MTcyZmFjOWJhNzIwMGE5YzQ5OGU5MWZjYjg0ZWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T02:36:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T02:36:17Z"},"message":"[codex] Update bundled skill installer guidance (#29768)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Update the bundled skill installer's post-install guidance to say the\nskill will be available on the user's next turn.\n- Remove the obsolete instruction to restart Codex.\n\n## Why\n\nCodex refreshes its skill catalog between turns. The existing bundled\ninstruction predates that behavior and causes the model to recommend an\nunnecessary restart.\n\n## Impact\n\nReleased Codex builds will materialize accurate post-install guidance\nfor the bundled system skill.\n\n## Related\n\n- Canonical skill change: https://github.com/openai/skills/pull/507\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nskills_changed_notification_is_emitted_after_skill_change` (passed\nduring investigation)\n\nNo test code was added because the existing live-refresh path and\nfocused integration test already verify that skill changes are picked up\nwithout restarting.","tree":{"sha":"bc6668632cbfea441a3835e0196570b93ff95285","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/bc6668632cbfea441a3835e0196570b93ff95285"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6f65b9a98c4172fac9ba7200a9c498e91fcb84ec","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqO0KhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlGIQAFVIUys1JrOljCjvlPPthhIO\noz7DetUF82ivGt+gIOhTsFq/Ykk1BjUVXi1jAOyrz0D8igYTjMeDoUxdpAzAvvEm\nV/efh10b6Xhyq5bQbdRu+gw1Fe8sNh0u23nH/xFoYuA/1baVeuDp/mxdizIZF2Cs\nonHP/gnmAp8LZSWbsA68MVf86BkF6qEp3ZtboypgsqYs3ALIPuehMX1xPry3nHbZ\nH4N65MHKRtFSGtM+nNb6R7OVz58+moSHYXytMWzGFQvatL4ZANKY6vONIQGKanCY\nUv0DHVBr8v3ofcmociiJ1eu91MdJu+veCQlOzR6NmyY70yoJKJ2rrhmCk4veqy9w\n7hQMC2mSwNVCscIeHLs2wmZ4OmXoZj4+sH/4dTy8dE/K0mGvfaJHqxcXv/7aWbk7\ndQ9W4qm7K1247jMtCwZ/VrdpxMlK/UPFlDBKfep9OVQLJVDy16bGaOVCojI35Fhs\nqz+RLKJWBx8HgyA6KuaLUf4OkWFxG4NtM8wYmpNr+C0PtJt46eheQ68Fw8OBJfYp\n+N5fZ+NVa3uvI2wnyipgRtz4m5+Z1EEt1R2bHJHCWVR1sycIdQP5Z2IXoz0ugCBR\nN+vFQ7sUljsWVif4H4ZXniCaSdLJIZrtnW+EdFstqUjRROTzJD88TEkDUNsGOhnH\nwth6Pin0u1v88zciKBKE\n=6ecR\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bc6668632cbfea441a3835e0196570b93ff95285\nparent 176af2b5105edafffc752241698050b119d7839c\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1782268577 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782268577 -0700\n\n[codex] Update bundled skill installer guidance (#29768)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Update the bundled skill installer's post-install guidance to say the\nskill will be available on the user's next turn.\n- Remove the obsolete instruction to restart Codex.\n\n## Why\n\nCodex refreshes its skill catalog between turns. The existing bundled\ninstruction predates that behavior and causes the model to recommend an\nunnecessary restart.\n\n## Impact\n\nReleased Codex builds will materialize accurate post-install guidance\nfor the bundled system skill.\n\n## Related\n\n- Canonical skill change: https://github.com/openai/skills/pull/507\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nskills_changed_notification_is_emitted_after_skill_change` (passed\nduring investigation)\n\nNo test code was added because the existing live-refresh path and\nfocused integration test already verify that skill changes are picked up\nwithout restarting.","verified_at":"2026-06-24T02:36:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6f65b9a98c4172fac9ba7200a9c498e91fcb84ec","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6f65b9a98c4172fac9ba7200a9c498e91fcb84ec","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6f65b9a98c4172fac9ba7200a9c498e91fcb84ec/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"176af2b5105edafffc752241698050b119d7839c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/176af2b5105edafffc752241698050b119d7839c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/176af2b5105edafffc752241698050b119d7839c"}]},{"sha":"176af2b5105edafffc752241698050b119d7839c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDE3NmFmMmI1MTA1ZWRhZmZmYzc1MjI0MTY5ODA1MGIxMTlkNzgzOWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"pakrym-oai","email":"pakrym@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T01:53:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T01:53:35Z"},"message":"[codex] Reuse compacted history replacement for new context windows (#29762)\n\n## Why\n\n`start_new_context_window` independently replaced in-memory history and\npersisted a compacted checkpoint instead of using the shared\ncompacted-history path. That bypassed the centralized missing-item-ID\nassignment when `item_ids` is enabled, so fresh context messages could\nenter the new context window and its persisted replacement history\nwithout IDs.\n\nThis follows up on the token-budget compaction reset flow introduced in\n[#29743](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29743).\n\n## What changed\n\n- Delegate new context-window installation to\n`replace_compacted_history`.\n- Reuse its ID assignment, in-memory replacement, world-state baseline,\ncheckpoint persistence, turn-context persistence, and session-start\nbookkeeping.\n- Add focused coverage that verifies generated IDs are present in live\nhistory and preserved in the persisted replacement history.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nstart_new_context_window_assigns_and_persists_item_ids`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nnew_context_tool_starts_new_window_before_follow_up`","tree":{"sha":"73bc6677a59f77fa3d46c80f4c3aa2e02c550203","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/73bc6677a59f77fa3d46c80f4c3aa2e02c550203"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/176af2b5105edafffc752241698050b119d7839c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOzifCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/coQAGBiiB1Ig8MIwS46PWnrZ9U8\nUGmLtY15wsBkOI8JGThDflSQouekzFC6qFHQu22gHVoEdb3Ui7nxJOwGTaCNVi5M\nxTbkfVz+KJRlzWDmEFe6yfUVHH77uPGUBQZHt+02Ehd5w9Gx/dZiwLM7OXSqXjb3\njI5ee3Jb2wkdVGsYkjZeIu+23C7Ku0aB/rCFyitb3Kv54KCB2E7oYQZ5S24AAbn5\nFnuMxhOFx99xnHZegzkzifeGs9APx2LWEEyOEWs+kUrW5S/iO67H59QPuoRXJ6Lx\nS0xjIWJZRI42GKwtHgJYwJ45ctEOIDFpxngbg89G/YAaR1Lvcoo+G7MWSi1Wnhaa\n9dEaRi3Nl3fwVW5kM4IYXVqXvRbt17/d7QTyMP0LQMUSvwZ/2xKPtMiEkdnzEE+L\nHYk83Q0oq8dsSgff7XAT+CfPcU3NJ/jTrSq5CnewRvXd1/E10FHLgtdSds/PChzz\nPehPaT0fmwFWZBM5TNMyn+IeY8U2fJE5JSCKVp3GsGdnxi2W0b+LrN902HBYA4M6\nzWSAmxQUCOhez+qMgpYwn8Zlt5MLmIVJjnRTMprXJxGSZfd6EzZjsd7iw7wUfalP\nQv7CRAXirrbuLbOTwDktfkvaBiY55CXSjPVfjVPk3EHYS2FqGc7Jdrpmuy7dimUl\nfbpmu5VmtCterfjNKmtm\n=oBs0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 73bc6677a59f77fa3d46c80f4c3aa2e02c550203\nparent 61f5a849308e1f160a30de7beaaa16e2a6d17902\nauthor pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com> 1782266015 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782266015 -0700\n\n[codex] Reuse compacted history replacement for new context windows (#29762)\n\n## Why\n\n`start_new_context_window` independently replaced in-memory history and\npersisted a compacted checkpoint instead of using the shared\ncompacted-history path. That bypassed the centralized missing-item-ID\nassignment when `item_ids` is enabled, so fresh context messages could\nenter the new context window and its persisted replacement history\nwithout IDs.\n\nThis follows up on the token-budget compaction reset flow introduced in\n[#29743](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29743).\n\n## What changed\n\n- Delegate new context-window installation to\n`replace_compacted_history`.\n- Reuse its ID assignment, in-memory replacement, world-state baseline,\ncheckpoint persistence, turn-context persistence, and session-start\nbookkeeping.\n- Add focused coverage that verifies generated IDs are present in live\nhistory and preserved in the persisted replacement history.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nstart_new_context_window_assigns_and_persists_item_ids`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nnew_context_tool_starts_new_window_before_follow_up`","verified_at":"2026-06-24T01:53:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/176af2b5105edafffc752241698050b119d7839c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/176af2b5105edafffc752241698050b119d7839c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/176af2b5105edafffc752241698050b119d7839c/comments","author":{"login":"pakrym-oai","id":204937752,"node_id":"U_kgDODDcaGA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204937752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/pakrym-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pakrym-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"61f5a849308e1f160a30de7beaaa16e2a6d17902","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/61f5a849308e1f160a30de7beaaa16e2a6d17902","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/61f5a849308e1f160a30de7beaaa16e2a6d17902"}]},{"sha":"61f5a849308e1f160a30de7beaaa16e2a6d17902","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDYxZjVhODQ5MzA4ZTFmMTYwYTMwZGU3YmVhYWExNmUyYTZkMTc5MDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Won Park","email":"won@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T01:51:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T01:51:49Z"},"message":"Let image generation extension hosts control output persistence (#29711)\n\n## Why\n\nSome extension hosts need generated images returned without writing them\nto the local filesystem or giving the model a local path.\n\n## What changed\n\n**tl;dr**: we now conduct all extension operations in the image gen\nextension\n\n- Let hosts provide an optional image save root when installing the\nextension.\n- Save images and return path hints only when a save root is configured.\n- Return image data without saving or adding a path hint when no save\nroot is configured.\n- Preserve the extension-provided `saved_path` instead of persisting\nextension images again in core.\n- Leave built-in image generation unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-image-generation-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nstandalone_image_generation_returns_saved_path_hint_to_model`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nextension_tool_uses_granted_turn_permissions_without_local_persistence`\n- `just test -p codex-core tools::handlers::extension_tools::tests`\n- tested on CODEX CLI on both save_root: CODEX_HOME and None \n- tested on CODEX APP on both as well","tree":{"sha":"d3a7b945bce85df4cfcd841a609f1669ba6dfccb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d3a7b945bce85df4cfcd841a609f1669ba6dfccb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/61f5a849308e1f160a30de7beaaa16e2a6d17902","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOzg1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAh1MQAHTfLuieR+OBRYxN3v402jNO\nWShSVkeNpAAAwL0m3wPhCohe0NHoAvKjP3r8teIAZY1vL+xhox7pjC0eWjc4MAN3\n5Yw2lVJS7gHQUjSw+BdZ06oBTtAQOzj3vSdR635MwHX+9+GoTINoWGALZwKp9iZc\nCjhVHE1DKsOpeNd+46QOObwqKrJYd6PDVRxm7Ee8cdCHuW6sJqMhRl0f3c8Hzp2f\nVdpC+CpF/O3/ZXjbGjUwM8bkJRv8ChaKz5rAKQ3ZpSBTQl20fswHQWy2CUvD/o7H\nlMhsytcsUPixPjf19UzBGVE1fT18pWB9+JGqKcgcyQrJ+tMyqfSksmClby2SdkjH\nW74AHhC3W1s3eowJp+oUcIdMu3Bg1ErTjDdWYpSx1HQ40pc3hkhjZhpUYbCIqHEs\n0ooSCZt+D73TFawJl2cjynEWq9wgJyVNW9w7b7eG7sFaZsCTnt04Ua8DntJ4aPxe\nc1lqBmS57HpqhrQoJ8lhziBg9TV/pw2YY4dABrfaGmRpCYh7qfOI+1RuACZjVh89\nhL4pFSD5hWMTDnMXrGOr13zZATOr0Fs3fdfWeQRye+ypiPr26IEXmguxeoMlSS5S\n0TJbuoyrTqXbg1e2G/NbY3a+TGGpN71w/RRp4sN+pSpGhmDsrPObeBwcPU4n1+35\nR+vRqdGyJCeEiXmXaLxk\n=ApRn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d3a7b945bce85df4cfcd841a609f1669ba6dfccb\nparent 283bc4cf011047314b4804c0f1ccd06e4f6a95c5\nauthor Won Park <won@openai.com> 1782265909 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782265909 -0700\n\nLet image generation extension hosts control output persistence (#29711)\n\n## Why\n\nSome extension hosts need generated images returned without writing them\nto the local filesystem or giving the model a local path.\n\n## What changed\n\n**tl;dr**: we now conduct all extension operations in the image gen\nextension\n\n- Let hosts provide an optional image save root when installing the\nextension.\n- Save images and return path hints only when a save root is configured.\n- Return image data without saving or adding a path hint when no save\nroot is configured.\n- Preserve the extension-provided `saved_path` instead of persisting\nextension images again in core.\n- Leave built-in image generation unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-image-generation-extension`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nstandalone_image_generation_returns_saved_path_hint_to_model`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nextension_tool_uses_granted_turn_permissions_without_local_persistence`\n- `just test -p codex-core tools::handlers::extension_tools::tests`\n- tested on CODEX CLI on both save_root: CODEX_HOME and None \n- tested on CODEX APP on both as well","verified_at":"2026-06-24T01:51:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/61f5a849308e1f160a30de7beaaa16e2a6d17902","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/61f5a849308e1f160a30de7beaaa16e2a6d17902","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/61f5a849308e1f160a30de7beaaa16e2a6d17902/comments","author":{"login":"won-openai","id":262224683,"node_id":"U_kgDOD6E7Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/262224683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/won-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/won-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"283bc4cf011047314b4804c0f1ccd06e4f6a95c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/283bc4cf011047314b4804c0f1ccd06e4f6a95c5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/283bc4cf011047314b4804c0f1ccd06e4f6a95c5"}]},{"sha":"283bc4cf011047314b4804c0f1ccd06e4f6a95c5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDI4M2JjNGNmMDExMDQ3MzE0YjQ4MDRjMGYxY2NkMDZlNGY2YTk1YzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T01:06:29Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T01:06:29Z"},"message":"test: add app-server auto environment helper (#29746)\n\n## Why\n\nStart moving towards app-server tests defaulting to running against\nremote & foreign OS executors. To do so we need a point of indirection\nsimilar to core integration tests' `build_with_auto_env`, but with the\nflexibility of letting tests control environment registration if they\nneed to.\n\n## What\n\nThis adds:\n\n- `TestAppServer::new_with_auto_env()` for constructing an app server\nwith a default environment defined by the test runner (e.g. bazel)\n- `TestAppServer::auto_env_params()` for tests to easily acquire turn\nenv params tailored to the automatic environment\n- `TestAppServer::send_thread_start_request_with_auto_env()` to make it\neasy for tests to start a thread using the automatic environment\n\nThe above methods all fail if the test calling them has set up an\nenvironment where the automatic environment configuration conflicts with\ntest-created state.\n\n## Validation\n\nAdds a couple of basic smoke tests to the app-server test suite.\nFollow-ups will migrate more tests to use it.","tree":{"sha":"18c47d0fd6bc5f2dc63c6154f89930492a570859","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/18c47d0fd6bc5f2dc63c6154f89930492a570859"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/283bc4cf011047314b4804c0f1ccd06e4f6a95c5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOy2VCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3lsQAIrV34GGv/Wo6B88xMhhh52m\nwISeeZGavS1ty516csNR4V6GMmyF+0ykg6bjkKVNsXI1/heTT1uzAIII9X8d8/or\n+tGG5ToFtMKxbeMgzq3ZVOrcDddGybmynQMb1qe4R/eNYc29InK0/T0RqZTuQfgd\nFBpF1lRcmgbPXDVCc87/F7OWwFdK2btynUAmMhzBw2VuM4YwZVyv1lWxoFDbqGcO\nc5TCajfZA9XvcNXFOGJZxzXO0BnJrC2KRzIcl6z/a3tnLL6aSrmF+3E4lOVZfprz\nLMqeGiXXLstMB/YbVnEESmMWT6uA0IUiV+H2NKZT0zXo9WC6kqz/6EPqS8MDf71T\nnOgzh+zthU/KvO9TgteQ4+mzSFmWucYaLaHejbiDFr71wOWqcDHFsCMWPSj3yI57\n3KUSTRYQVS6N/sPKyqVDgHNHwR6D5ZkdxyG8DyhW6oJ6QWF8CfaRt9l0p2Jkif27\na+SNmSFVc/OZXgaNVsamSmDACkJBoolf4cMwEEohn8IC0MyIyBqNuWF7CCIEaDYN\nWAKbuvw7o4+lgRtFMXBFjLuDD7LhcQn3b/FzR5W9/vcTzLKjjI0gLa8hQdEsyyVG\n1cC8bSraV6AWzp0D5pvg/xx0qMCsXD8pax7epqvl/vSOIZdKszQoGfoH3Ojs2Y5v\nYFmA0eV1+63PZ+iqAOVK\n=9J92\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 18c47d0fd6bc5f2dc63c6154f89930492a570859\nparent 97dce078c57895d9cc184be923dc26b102e19493\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1782263189 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782263189 +0000\n\ntest: add app-server auto environment helper (#29746)\n\n## Why\n\nStart moving towards app-server tests defaulting to running against\nremote & foreign OS executors. To do so we need a point of indirection\nsimilar to core integration tests' `build_with_auto_env`, but with the\nflexibility of letting tests control environment registration if they\nneed to.\n\n## What\n\nThis adds:\n\n- `TestAppServer::new_with_auto_env()` for constructing an app server\nwith a default environment defined by the test runner (e.g. bazel)\n- `TestAppServer::auto_env_params()` for tests to easily acquire turn\nenv params tailored to the automatic environment\n- `TestAppServer::send_thread_start_request_with_auto_env()` to make it\neasy for tests to start a thread using the automatic environment\n\nThe above methods all fail if the test calling them has set up an\nenvironment where the automatic environment configuration conflicts with\ntest-created state.\n\n## Validation\n\nAdds a couple of basic smoke tests to the app-server test suite.\nFollow-ups will migrate more tests to use it.","verified_at":"2026-06-24T01:06:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/283bc4cf011047314b4804c0f1ccd06e4f6a95c5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/283bc4cf011047314b4804c0f1ccd06e4f6a95c5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/283bc4cf011047314b4804c0f1ccd06e4f6a95c5/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"97dce078c57895d9cc184be923dc26b102e19493","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/97dce078c57895d9cc184be923dc26b102e19493","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/97dce078c57895d9cc184be923dc26b102e19493"}]},{"sha":"97dce078c57895d9cc184be923dc26b102e19493","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDk3ZGNlMDc4YzU3ODk1ZDljYzE4NGJlOTIzZGMyNmIxMDJlMTk0OTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T00:57:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T00:57:03Z"},"message":"chore: assign `amsg_` IDs to agent messages (#29750)\n\n## Why\n\nThe `ItemIds` path fills in missing IDs before response items are\npersisted and emitted as raw item events. `ResponseItem::AgentMessage`\nis part of that same response-item stream, but it was skipped by the\nmissing-ID repair path, leaving agent messages without stable item IDs\nwhile messages and tool items received generated IDs.\n\nAgent messages recorded through `InterAgentCommunication` also need the\ngenerated ID to survive rollout persistence and resume. Otherwise\nclients can observe an `amsg_` ID for the live raw response item, then\nsee that same persisted agent message lose its item ID after restart.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Assign missing `ResponseItem::AgentMessage` IDs with the `amsg_`\nprefix.\n- Persist the generated item ID on `InterAgentCommunication` and replay\nit back into the reconstructed `ResponseItem::AgentMessage` on resume.\n- Keep the persisted ID out of the model-visible inter-agent message\nenvelope.\n- Keep `CompactionTrigger` and `Other` skipped because they do not get\ngenerated item IDs.\n- Update session/protocol tests for agent-message ID assignment and\nresume preservation.\n\n## Manual Testing\n\nRun the local dev build using `just c --enable item_ids` to ensure this\ncode is exercised:\n\n\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/blob/322e33512b2d38d38d705e2ef692a8aca50decac/codex-rs/core/src/session/mod.rs#L2713-L2715\n\nIn the `.jsonl` file, I saw entries like:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-24T00:44:03.098Z\",\n  \"type\": \"inter_agent_communication\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"id\": \"amsg_019ef715-849a-7a50-becc-ce63c6a9c994\",\n```\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nrecord_inter_agent_communication_preserves_item_id_in_rollout_and_resume`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nrecord_inter_agent_communication_sets_turn_id_in_rollout_and_resume`\n- `just test -p codex-protocol\ninter_agent_communication_response_input_item_preserves_commentary_phase`","tree":{"sha":"87f23220f55563756c2045a584dcf62145141392","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/87f23220f55563756c2045a584dcf62145141392"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/97dce078c57895d9cc184be923dc26b102e19493","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOytfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdkoQACEap2wxfILKqW6sS5FhN1xn\nF5p/lpv/TOawkNSPM7h894pzq+vwDPeF17LN7mvh5OlgnNv4M3wbFfp1M8RSIHP8\nxuoL9DS6bc7PBVMLLgWlLlK3/HJSuUHw6S/DDMsP5agZBSUvSjTJgQ6k3k4LctRA\ndx/vo6F6xLLH5GTJhcbgSuWtz4PpqHvcS/APHRmEfClTIJR/Gpuzht+KCqTvFlMM\nfw+j6sirb8zqjSiutmVYmCOV9q2Vs1KiqxwYejEFzK2iFEi3J/1TVw2Q2dn7Wyc8\nwJcPoEzuuiRO60kZwpf94w38Gvq7JH4s7oeKw1BjEtim+rPEUDVi3scMkAfHHCfD\nF8YGhGkqoHdqyirgkj0woGllyTbs/g4WOtWri2Fr3XkrbyjBzOc1AXHqqZR1eDcD\n0OfaqNTVY+v5LUIry+S7mnBr1QxLIs7pbUzgruklRVWjLoN4mzeeGyamJaUajg6C\no6vVxrFGcBlRzdIyeo/1Tqy6R/Z7IxYl8mxtd6vRqAkHceeCNZ1hN6fNpHSQYcAi\nhtjxC/oVOLk2I6BgHtQaZfQ0z1EcG9EdXb4HfGPuKCjvP6g9TB8N7IyFdqZi1bCG\nyjEdGoLnNL0nVlEqmsgB8u84qck1X3NfW9pFYKgE5N9nGDooS6LWnYUDEWPNgfWW\nzG5fgz8yvm+uydNOl7AN\n=H2s6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 87f23220f55563756c2045a584dcf62145141392\nparent 322e33512b2d38d38d705e2ef692a8aca50decac\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1782262623 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782262623 -0700\n\nchore: assign `amsg_` IDs to agent messages (#29750)\n\n## Why\n\nThe `ItemIds` path fills in missing IDs before response items are\npersisted and emitted as raw item events. `ResponseItem::AgentMessage`\nis part of that same response-item stream, but it was skipped by the\nmissing-ID repair path, leaving agent messages without stable item IDs\nwhile messages and tool items received generated IDs.\n\nAgent messages recorded through `InterAgentCommunication` also need the\ngenerated ID to survive rollout persistence and resume. Otherwise\nclients can observe an `amsg_` ID for the live raw response item, then\nsee that same persisted agent message lose its item ID after restart.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Assign missing `ResponseItem::AgentMessage` IDs with the `amsg_`\nprefix.\n- Persist the generated item ID on `InterAgentCommunication` and replay\nit back into the reconstructed `ResponseItem::AgentMessage` on resume.\n- Keep the persisted ID out of the model-visible inter-agent message\nenvelope.\n- Keep `CompactionTrigger` and `Other` skipped because they do not get\ngenerated item IDs.\n- Update session/protocol tests for agent-message ID assignment and\nresume preservation.\n\n## Manual Testing\n\nRun the local dev build using `just c --enable item_ids` to ensure this\ncode is exercised:\n\n\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/blob/322e33512b2d38d38d705e2ef692a8aca50decac/codex-rs/core/src/session/mod.rs#L2713-L2715\n\nIn the `.jsonl` file, I saw entries like:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-24T00:44:03.098Z\",\n  \"type\": \"inter_agent_communication\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"id\": \"amsg_019ef715-849a-7a50-becc-ce63c6a9c994\",\n```\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nrecord_inter_agent_communication_preserves_item_id_in_rollout_and_resume`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nrecord_inter_agent_communication_sets_turn_id_in_rollout_and_resume`\n- `just test -p codex-protocol\ninter_agent_communication_response_input_item_preserves_commentary_phase`","verified_at":"2026-06-24T00:57:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/97dce078c57895d9cc184be923dc26b102e19493","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/97dce078c57895d9cc184be923dc26b102e19493","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/97dce078c57895d9cc184be923dc26b102e19493/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"322e33512b2d38d38d705e2ef692a8aca50decac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/322e33512b2d38d38d705e2ef692a8aca50decac","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/322e33512b2d38d38d705e2ef692a8aca50decac"}]},{"sha":"322e33512b2d38d38d705e2ef692a8aca50decac","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDMyMmUzMzUxMmIyZDM4ZDM4ZDcwNWUyZWY2OTJhOGFjYTUwZGVjYWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"rphilizaire-openai","email":"rphilizaire@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T00:46:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T00:46:54Z"},"message":"[codex] trace MCP startup latency (#28630)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add trace-level instrumentation around per-server MCP setup, client\nconstruction, initialization, and initial tool listing\n- trace Codex Apps tool and server-info cache loads\n- attach `server_name` to server-scoped spans so slow startup work can\nbe attributed to a specific MCP server\n\n## Why\n\n`session_init.mcp_manager_init` can occasionally be slow, but its\nexisting coarse span does not identify whether time is spent loading the\nCodex Apps cache, constructing a client, initializing a transport, or\nlisting tools. These definition-level spans provide that breakdown\nwithout changing startup behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-mcp` (87 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-rmcp-client` (86 passed, 2 skipped)","tree":{"sha":"bc10481e1728e953ab519a98168bf1a6476547ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/bc10481e1728e953ab519a98168bf1a6476547ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/322e33512b2d38d38d705e2ef692a8aca50decac","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOyj+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1zMQAFwIP37IihH4dS7hW4pQFDlg\nevP0Vld85mPtODLpGBVsvpidgPpltlw0REBJBH1I8DupHp3l6fxeOEjAhSpBsuEg\nt0nA3yzJDgSf4n2tDaUX6w8mBJogP/g6uUNpUexgVEAKgW0NT7FAIBHUr61+sDAI\n0gEjBGMSh/p5ZYoCjSl2pIlqRI/8BdT6jIfb5mcNURf2sYhq0SG7esbdz+nvfW2l\n8icpW5DaPREQBo5DeL5S3UHjl1o1+9+cbk+cRofTJsGuIS9MAFdRjG+MbwyyA6jF\n4IDukP3qKoXnmmZDXq8JmqXTgo3NpLyNkm1ify8NTp4P91durtkLVy/N3qA9Apto\nYcYqvu6IfFWu6sShTwl69SuY0w6DfK4ySvc+t6UlOnHl42uCLVdAZ5sDhS5Ec13Y\nFEi7+4QmZF4L1WM6+bbnxL/vtkFUh+K6h+IH0PREnYa5UiWdBNZyRYUgVjg77I/A\nCuhcE1tnwKYzT+zfnOY3/LQMZYe5u7FqPTcD+LghvoOpHbUSCH789TmjWSukuNO5\nyWR8Y9nf0e8pDfZcrn1TpNVj6MNgGxCNOOB+sddlcKY3wrm5PYWiFY5yLqZtK/Df\nuI9LYUJBd6krJDxT+aG/dDCcl/X+TEy0xgJ7YTiRDfyfCDttoKC/YRJc0IeW1lDV\nO4v3oqroTThnIEy3X4zZ\n=xK7W\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bc10481e1728e953ab519a98168bf1a6476547ec\nparent 61ff4d087e23428335b2917e6def3fc47fab6425\nauthor rphilizaire-openai <rphilizaire@openai.com> 1782262014 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782262014 -0700\n\n[codex] trace MCP startup latency (#28630)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add trace-level instrumentation around per-server MCP setup, client\nconstruction, initialization, and initial tool listing\n- trace Codex Apps tool and server-info cache loads\n- attach `server_name` to server-scoped spans so slow startup work can\nbe attributed to a specific MCP server\n\n## Why\n\n`session_init.mcp_manager_init` can occasionally be slow, but its\nexisting coarse span does not identify whether time is spent loading the\nCodex Apps cache, constructing a client, initializing a transport, or\nlisting tools. These definition-level spans provide that breakdown\nwithout changing startup behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-mcp` (87 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-rmcp-client` (86 passed, 2 skipped)","verified_at":"2026-06-24T00:46:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/322e33512b2d38d38d705e2ef692a8aca50decac","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/322e33512b2d38d38d705e2ef692a8aca50decac","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/322e33512b2d38d38d705e2ef692a8aca50decac/comments","author":{"login":"rphilizaire-openai","id":200841089,"node_id":"U_kgDOC_iXgQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200841089?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rphilizaire-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/rphilizaire-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rphilizaire-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rphilizaire-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rphilizaire-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rphilizaire-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rphilizaire-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rphilizaire-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rphilizaire-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rphilizaire-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rphilizaire-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"61ff4d087e23428335b2917e6def3fc47fab6425","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/61ff4d087e23428335b2917e6def3fc47fab6425","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/61ff4d087e23428335b2917e6def3fc47fab6425"}]},{"sha":"61ff4d087e23428335b2917e6def3fc47fab6425","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDYxZmY0ZDA4N2UyMzQyODMzNWIyOTE3ZTZkZWYzZmM0N2ZhYjY0MjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T00:35:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T00:35:34Z"},"message":"core: add wait_for_environment for starting environments (#29745)\n\n## Why\n\nWith `DeferredExecutor`, a sampling request can begin while an\nenvironment is still starting. The model can see that pending state, but\nneeds a way to wait for the environment within the same turn before\ncontinuing.\n\nEnvironment startup is owned by Core, so the wait tool should use the\nsame request-frozen `StepContext` that advertised the starting\nenvironment. This keeps tool registration and execution tied to the\nexact startup operation the model saw, even if live thread state later\nchanges.\n\nSupersedes #29735.\n\n## What\n\n- register `wait_for_environment` when the current `StepContext`\ncontains starting environments\n- wait on the selected `StartingTurnEnvironment` shared resolution and\nreturn a bounded ready or failed result\n- rebuild the next request normally, removing the wait tool and exposing\nready environment tools, or reporting the environment as unavailable\nafter failure\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core deferred_executor_`\n- verifies the wait tool is replaced by environment-backed tools after\nstartup\n- verifies startup failure removes both the wait tool and unavailable\nenvironment tools while notifying the model","tree":{"sha":"eba463272b445439cf19ceb1ab396f117aa7f1ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/eba463272b445439cf19ceb1ab396f117aa7f1ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/61ff4d087e23428335b2917e6def3fc47fab6425","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOyZWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGoAQAIAKcX0/GnZGJsec4JG0baw0\nM+lFtUjJ+r76JfqeaFWEn1L9uP3yFxj+MM7nTEvIXTT6sbWWMlEFG0NOhu9weKy4\nFwW6NMrKQ9FX18Pl6RtwDCz/GA62Knocqplay9SiK8hiuwUha8wCb3yVtZvlvGIm\nExdTDR800LeeDUyQmcUFflnKXBn7THt4temFyutKiW8PTaJ3fNRwvxLK0bwVAAl7\n0BlcNDUOkQLyt4wRppM54XzO7O6qIGC1Je9gSIui/3TtpWpP90yMsM2+CVolX/7e\n0m438poFykRVKTyAy+h8rUTP6z6loObS0YD/+Ca4KszPieCyKD6ilzR7m/nQtZnP\nU/1y5TkqkIEJ7jm3OfHqFU4iO6RPsA1wDDOC4pW7xnTSOuB/6yVTIbW0VnqAaUZB\nrZNlZqCBkr3zm/rOMbUN5kKFce9vssYNvBy7BYU+Sgxnc4rPO5NZi/Dcb3tiirYZ\nNL5bNhhGONh1FtCoqv1u2g7CHAbUgH27p8pun7kH+wh308QUzbObf2/cAh1V5fxR\nit3HjDKUii2YIpgR7/kses0l3yGdRdpuX/J5d6IuxcveOIfJeidgpoCkysbH1w+n\nb8k5RK2f9wreNhWe3sz4RXWChxtohuJq4Ahm6+NtUtuVpy5h7C/bc5HKSI5ZcCKB\npvBbCw10ws1XUI8aLm5K\n=idc3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree eba463272b445439cf19ceb1ab396f117aa7f1ae\nparent 1acb722e8afeba0cd54c9019f140830d05fdf5e7\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1782261334 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782261334 +0000\n\ncore: add wait_for_environment for starting environments (#29745)\n\n## Why\n\nWith `DeferredExecutor`, a sampling request can begin while an\nenvironment is still starting. The model can see that pending state, but\nneeds a way to wait for the environment within the same turn before\ncontinuing.\n\nEnvironment startup is owned by Core, so the wait tool should use the\nsame request-frozen `StepContext` that advertised the starting\nenvironment. This keeps tool registration and execution tied to the\nexact startup operation the model saw, even if live thread state later\nchanges.\n\nSupersedes #29735.\n\n## What\n\n- register `wait_for_environment` when the current `StepContext`\ncontains starting environments\n- wait on the selected `StartingTurnEnvironment` shared resolution and\nreturn a bounded ready or failed result\n- rebuild the next request normally, removing the wait tool and exposing\nready environment tools, or reporting the environment as unavailable\nafter failure\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core deferred_executor_`\n- verifies the wait tool is replaced by environment-backed tools after\nstartup\n- verifies startup failure removes both the wait tool and unavailable\nenvironment tools while notifying the model","verified_at":"2026-06-24T00:35:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/61ff4d087e23428335b2917e6def3fc47fab6425","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/61ff4d087e23428335b2917e6def3fc47fab6425","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/61ff4d087e23428335b2917e6def3fc47fab6425/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1acb722e8afeba0cd54c9019f140830d05fdf5e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1acb722e8afeba0cd54c9019f140830d05fdf5e7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1acb722e8afeba0cd54c9019f140830d05fdf5e7"}]},{"sha":"1acb722e8afeba0cd54c9019f140830d05fdf5e7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDFhY2I3MjJlOGFmZWJhMGNkNTRjOTAxOWYxNDA4MzBkMDVmZGY1ZTc","commit":{"author":{"name":"alexsong-oai","email":"alexsong@openai.com","date":"2026-06-24T00:23:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-24T00:23:38Z"},"message":"Support thread-level originator overrides (#29477)\n\n## Why\n\nWork(TPP) threads can be launched from the Desktop app, but if they all\nkeep the Desktop app's default originator then downstream attribution\ncannot distinguish local Work launches from cloud-backed Work launches.\n`thread/start.serviceName` already carries that launch signal, while\n`SessionMeta.originator` is the durable thread-level value that survives\nresume and fork.\n\nThis change converts the Desktop Work service names into an effective\noriginator at thread creation time, persists that originator with the\nthread, and keeps using it for later model requests and memory writes.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Map `CODEX_WORK_LOCAL` and `CODEX_WORK_CLOUD` service names to\nper-thread originators, while preserving\n`CODEX_INTERNAL_ORIGINATOR_OVERRIDE` as the highest-precedence override.\n- Persist the effective originator in `SessionMeta.originator`, read it\nback on resume/fork, and inherit the parent originator for subagent\nspawns when there is no persisted session metadata.\n- Handle truncated `SpawnAgentForkMode::LastNTurns` forks by falling\nback to the live parent originator when the forked history no longer\nincludes `SessionMeta`.\n- Thread the per-thread originator through Responses headers,\nwebsocket/compaction request paths, thread-store creation, rollout\nmetadata, and memory stage-one telemetry.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nagent::control::tests::spawn_thread_subagent_inherits_parent_originator_without_fork\nagent::control::tests::spawn_thread_subagent_fork_last_n_turns_inherits_parent_originator_without_session_meta\nthread_manager::tests::originator_override_precedes_service_name_remapping`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nagent::control::tests::resume_thread_subagent_restores_stored_metadata_and_effective_multi_agent_mode`\n- `just test -p codex-memories-write`\n- `just fix -p codex-core -p codex-memories-write`\n- `git diff --check`","tree":{"sha":"fd27db0f7f7f7f6e8b3b77ae9116275e11bb53f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/fd27db0f7f7f7f6e8b3b77ae9116275e11bb53f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1acb722e8afeba0cd54c9019f140830d05fdf5e7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOyOKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVh4QAH0fs7L+Vz6c6aNvWZE+ObEX\n2z2ETqt+5CeGJcrUCxitEaRtXnE+BVWpBh5DH9XGYK918W0gPGyIQ9l+oIv9v8Vu\nERIXllqSnBYIdpM35lML1fbrH29M8ikI1zwQsR3/0RabD13kfar6CGn6iIGHN8nm\ng3vlgnpwidm13vBtjkP7YRbLwdAjCOGpkAgKKZ2Nzf3n/awsjKfni6s0bcEiQyLY\n4aCHdeA7NDpT/KoqHad/vnl6WSBtFYXvzL2db1cDR9T2iOqs15vnKqZv0QMi+XzU\nYishRdBLUPyrPJw4ziGTSONpcSBvHsja1A4qTbZuSHZNxErKTsNNn9vQ9pPaDasp\n7vDR+G3BhfhLCn1rq09agtKe64wDaENRa+WF7Jv2DpNVS5xCdcBfqZPODwK9dj0w\nXruDI9PHce9xDemMS1p9mPDsP4PiskLEM46DLuNqMRj74pGptD12iVZSO96JiGq4\nEQ20ozFJJQEvBYuoKKcx+rjze1AWB/8slRGcLEFy+rQMkyowEPGUvVy4wjQ0g/Im\n8QPgMSu/9b3hAx8lDrj0mp0rHUWieDaqK3jC8oWNTviFz669G3ioATy+4UXnjeCR\nLDbkiAqqIMl5VpoJx/FJCsjI/7mbYvNo82lyQ/HuptJ0lOzhWAXDKtAe6jl/Easg\nKMXhG2JXfeRuvWoBYEBa\n=YzO2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fd27db0f7f7f7f6e8b3b77ae9116275e11bb53f8\nparent 32b65bbf7a304f9231d81226ed3bb649739b73a6\nauthor alexsong-oai <alexsong@openai.com> 1782260618 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782260618 -0700\n\nSupport thread-level originator overrides (#29477)\n\n## Why\n\nWork(TPP) threads can be launched from the Desktop app, but if they all\nkeep the Desktop app's default originator then downstream attribution\ncannot distinguish local Work launches from cloud-backed Work launches.\n`thread/start.serviceName` already carries that launch signal, while\n`SessionMeta.originator` is the durable thread-level value that survives\nresume and fork.\n\nThis change converts the Desktop Work service names into an effective\noriginator at thread creation time, persists that originator with the\nthread, and keeps using it for later model requests and memory writes.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Map `CODEX_WORK_LOCAL` and `CODEX_WORK_CLOUD` service names to\nper-thread originators, while preserving\n`CODEX_INTERNAL_ORIGINATOR_OVERRIDE` as the highest-precedence override.\n- Persist the effective originator in `SessionMeta.originator`, read it\nback on resume/fork, and inherit the parent originator for subagent\nspawns when there is no persisted session metadata.\n- Handle truncated `SpawnAgentForkMode::LastNTurns` forks by falling\nback to the live parent originator when the forked history no longer\nincludes `SessionMeta`.\n- Thread the per-thread originator through Responses headers,\nwebsocket/compaction request paths, thread-store creation, rollout\nmetadata, and memory stage-one telemetry.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\nagent::control::tests::spawn_thread_subagent_inherits_parent_originator_without_fork\nagent::control::tests::spawn_thread_subagent_fork_last_n_turns_inherits_parent_originator_without_session_meta\nthread_manager::tests::originator_override_precedes_service_name_remapping`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nagent::control::tests::resume_thread_subagent_restores_stored_metadata_and_effective_multi_agent_mode`\n- `just test -p codex-memories-write`\n- `just fix -p codex-core -p codex-memories-write`\n- `git diff --check`","verified_at":"2026-06-24T00:23:38Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1acb722e8afeba0cd54c9019f140830d05fdf5e7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1acb722e8afeba0cd54c9019f140830d05fdf5e7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1acb722e8afeba0cd54c9019f140830d05fdf5e7/comments","author":{"login":"alexsong-oai","id":256201575,"node_id":"U_kgDOD0VTZw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256201575?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/alexsong-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexsong-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"32b65bbf7a304f9231d81226ed3bb649739b73a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/32b65bbf7a304f9231d81226ed3bb649739b73a6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/32b65bbf7a304f9231d81226ed3bb649739b73a6"}]},{"sha":"32b65bbf7a304f9231d81226ed3bb649739b73a6","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDMyYjY1YmJmN2EzMDRmOTIzMWQ4MTIyNmVkM2JiNjQ5NzM5YjczYTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T23:59:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T23:59:04Z"},"message":"core: reset context for token budget compaction (#29743)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen `Feature::TokenBudget` is enabled, compaction should behave like\n`new_context`: start a fresh context window with the standard injected\ncontext, without asking the server to summarize old history and without\ncarrying prior user or assistant messages into the next model request.\n\nThis is still a compaction operation from the client lifecycle\nperspective. Manual `/compact` and auto-compaction should keep the same\nobservable side effects that clients and hooks expect, including compact\nhooks and `TurnItem::ContextCompaction`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `compact_token_budget` to run token-budget manual and inline\nauto-compaction through a shared compaction lifecycle.\n- Split pending `new_context` requests from forced context-window\nstartup: `take_new_context_window_request()` consumes pending requests,\nand `start_new_context_window()` installs a fresh context window.\n- Routed token-budget manual `/compact` and inline auto-compaction to\ninstall a fresh context window locally instead of calling server/local\nsummarization.\n- Preserved compact lifecycle side effects for token-budget compaction\nby running pre/post compact hooks and emitting `ContextCompaction` item\nstart/completion events.\n- Updated token-budget tests to assert fresh window IDs, absence of\nserver-side compaction calls, dropped prior transcript messages/tool\noutput after reset, and compact hook/item lifecycle behavior.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\ntoken_budget_context_uses_new_window_after_compaction`\n- `just test -p codex-core token_budget_compaction_runs_compact_hooks`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ntoken_budget_mid_turn_auto_compaction_resets_before_active_follow_up`\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com>","tree":{"sha":"325eb91b7a6c25e0c273759add260932dd23e38b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/325eb91b7a6c25e0c273759add260932dd23e38b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/32b65bbf7a304f9231d81226ed3bb649739b73a6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOx3ICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAkCQQAA3rQgz5LT8qctn/D/TgKdlk\nv+jF3QuWPHJo7cX5UTkXdXdbmC+8m53dKFbtQ7RXk0SbkW8e7gkB0bNaqRxhO2sM\nEBmmdwxWegnpMHcNl/c61q1Nk1hNnVyV1kuwoD5zY0NYbKfKYpqww+QaMx1oK+L3\nahMT/RoSOUyZHyDGklsxNkpoOi5b4JQ66CzA1aArkAAr3/GP6szBFfIgp3S5lAFR\n4zAFX8FOjnXWj3ncZwQ6z2fVOX/J8hpCYmN+WZYZX0yhHw/krmtGG/c5ujwzXiT3\nEJ6fxjNVn5BtnnwZH2vKnEKy6Bi7SIghSKFVn0SQSRDXJB4fEj7yv+JE6u4Of+dc\nOl9PcI6wabRfnLcULg1IRecCQhhe99KiUssaR5NLmBhWn4iFoh1LXqDsYsuO4Jcl\n4j5Zqt+IcEt80JjJUF62Wy8XCALAChlS80fHDc0anBmv1jBn3v10cH7lvX1Qx0gl\n6U+P1z4t6h4uAZvNgeHLoZ4j2kxCC8DTzDjbzM8SDzlMZssx3c61LCaknSlq6eEv\nEno+z5hwpW1LC0/qEJ4YvChgqHASa+ore2PiLm8NrXyM9hIDOPO1YRDy1t1Z/JKe\nJ7aJ9Yl45n7zQKkR9NHo/trVyT+3qkzL05YmPdkWrZBIVBYxxuzJlDHIWthSSMgA\nNw1eemvGi4f27LXRpoKX\n=iFmB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 325eb91b7a6c25e0c273759add260932dd23e38b\nparent 3b4186986f5f67aa324721d22d81e4f1501fd131\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1782259144 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782259144 -0700\n\ncore: reset context for token budget compaction (#29743)\n\n## Why\n\nWhen `Feature::TokenBudget` is enabled, compaction should behave like\n`new_context`: start a fresh context window with the standard injected\ncontext, without asking the server to summarize old history and without\ncarrying prior user or assistant messages into the next model request.\n\nThis is still a compaction operation from the client lifecycle\nperspective. Manual `/compact` and auto-compaction should keep the same\nobservable side effects that clients and hooks expect, including compact\nhooks and `TurnItem::ContextCompaction`.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `compact_token_budget` to run token-budget manual and inline\nauto-compaction through a shared compaction lifecycle.\n- Split pending `new_context` requests from forced context-window\nstartup: `take_new_context_window_request()` consumes pending requests,\nand `start_new_context_window()` installs a fresh context window.\n- Routed token-budget manual `/compact` and inline auto-compaction to\ninstall a fresh context window locally instead of calling server/local\nsummarization.\n- Preserved compact lifecycle side effects for token-budget compaction\nby running pre/post compact hooks and emitting `ContextCompaction` item\nstart/completion events.\n- Updated token-budget tests to assert fresh window IDs, absence of\nserver-side compaction calls, dropped prior transcript messages/tool\noutput after reset, and compact hook/item lifecycle behavior.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\ntoken_budget_context_uses_new_window_after_compaction`\n- `just test -p codex-core token_budget_compaction_runs_compact_hooks`\n- `just test -p codex-core\ntoken_budget_mid_turn_auto_compaction_resets_before_active_follow_up`\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: pakrym-oai <pakrym@openai.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T23:59:05Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/32b65bbf7a304f9231d81226ed3bb649739b73a6","html_url":"http