\nauthor Andrey Mishchenko <andrey@openai.com> 1782258760 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782258760 -0700\n\nUpdate new_context_window instructions (#29739)","verified_at":"2026-06-23T23:52:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3b4186986f5f67aa324721d22d81e4f1501fd131","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3b4186986f5f67aa324721d22d81e4f1501fd131","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3b4186986f5f67aa324721d22d81e4f1501fd131/comments","author":{"login":"andmis","id":5308024,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzMDgwMjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5308024?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andmis","html_url":"https://github.com/andmis","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andmis/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andmis/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andmis/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andmis/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andmis/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andmis/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andmis/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andmis/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andmis/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1ec3def0b5473fe99ee70e13f841cfb2d91a09f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1ec3def0b5473fe99ee70e13f841cfb2d91a09f2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1ec3def0b5473fe99ee70e13f841cfb2d91a09f2"}]},{"sha":"1ec3def0b5473fe99ee70e13f841cfb2d91a09f2","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDFlYzNkZWYwYjU0NzNmZTk5ZWU3MGUxM2Y4NDFjZmIyZDkxYTA5ZjI","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T23:49:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T23:49:13Z"},"message":"[codex] rename rollout budget error to session budget error (#29744)\n\n## Summary\n\n- rename the rollout-budget exhaustion error from\n`RolloutBudgetExceeded` to `SessionBudgetExceeded`\n- expose the matching app-server v2 wire value as\n`sessionBudgetExceeded`\n- regenerate JSON/TypeScript schema fixtures and update the app-server\ndocs and focused tests\n\nThis is a naming-only follow-up to #29715 based on [Pavel's review\nsuggestion](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29715#discussion_r3463183480).\nRuntime behavior is unchanged.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `just test -p codex-core rollout_budget`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just fmt`\n- `just write-app-server-schema`","tree":{"sha":"5ca1db7b4c79ca40d73e09ec66361d4b5c5c889c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5ca1db7b4c79ca40d73e09ec66361d4b5c5c889c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1ec3def0b5473fe99ee70e13f841cfb2d91a09f2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOxt5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqacQAGxBbBKR+AkW4IoGq9ttEjy7\nyv7LaMwHALnEGGUVvh99xBYV1pcEq27G4CoyLlj5Yg+jPZQgiOsNNB4A/40/ry5J\nRUrawrS4RaQNXdpt3hPByYJYAMRSJ8BOiRElvD2azSkoz8ymhfONHnJsVZFlpsMt\nnrH5oYk8mEqdPzHOUIiFdI0kEMq9egqbpkvfHdSRZsaQDoAUWys8vM/IeWvdCalU\nYHmE9qTShJZtLefYGtc9iwELnpDfA9WaMzvib+UAiVTZ0gzKnd8nO5F+IdTgPtp2\nFVecjD9SVTumRr99m7f1WJ8xPG4KhBsBFNk5IAZ05TO577vwtk5OZDsvhCdrYhKO\nKYPJn7sfUSYbeK1BnOxDSFT9Q0xnUnYU+I2lyf+Bg8AFMOn4QZ/k2L3s5Cv81R2s\neu6ZUOkR40/ELD/ybOjPbddCF4QtzFWDpbOcHU4q8kX9gp97HIY4uStROe1wqHkD\nINXfgUQrdETGOjVpSf084FALvCXL1sLhp9P0vI1evg4xOW+uXFxe0QSkpOShfPuC\nt9CVm3pjcsflfebH1Lcd+LfTy8br0SXCIskIw4g8X043VYOzEo9Ne3+N2gz1g/Ux\nn4ISu1cvJt8+ng7+2MhNcOCHVT7pdzvzevyxJ1Oi9SqFLqg33r/4zTFpg/cSVqMv\nVGKLsgAlZ43xC4pcHEJj\n=U8YS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5ca1db7b4c79ca40d73e09ec66361d4b5c5c889c\nparent 77e7ce13741048772f77c761eed84a81f4403823\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1782258553 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782258553 -0700\n\n[codex] rename rollout budget error to session budget error (#29744)\n\n## Summary\n\n- rename the rollout-budget exhaustion error from\n`RolloutBudgetExceeded` to `SessionBudgetExceeded`\n- expose the matching app-server v2 wire value as\n`sessionBudgetExceeded`\n- regenerate JSON/TypeScript schema fixtures and update the app-server\ndocs and focused tests\n\nThis is a naming-only follow-up to #29715 based on [Pavel's review\nsuggestion](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29715#discussion_r3463183480).\nRuntime behavior is unchanged.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `just test -p codex-core rollout_budget`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol`\n- `just fmt`\n- `just write-app-server-schema`","verified_at":"2026-06-23T23:49:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1ec3def0b5473fe99ee70e13f841cfb2d91a09f2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1ec3def0b5473fe99ee70e13f841cfb2d91a09f2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1ec3def0b5473fe99ee70e13f841cfb2d91a09f2/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"77e7ce13741048772f77c761eed84a81f4403823","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/77e7ce13741048772f77c761eed84a81f4403823","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/77e7ce13741048772f77c761eed84a81f4403823"}]},{"sha":"77e7ce13741048772f77c761eed84a81f4403823","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDc3ZTdjZTEzNzQxMDQ4NzcyZjc3Yzc2MWVlZDg0YTgxZjQ0MDM4MjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T23:08:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T23:08:54Z"},"message":"fix: scope context remaining to body window (#29665)\n\n## Why\n\nWith `model_auto_compact_token_limit_scope = \"body_after_prefix\"`, the\npersistent prefix should not count against the active body window.\n`get_context_remaining` and the token-budget reminder should report the\nsame usable body-after-prefix window that auto-compaction uses, rather\nthan the total token count since the session began.\n\nThis is stacked on #29664 so the mechanical move from `turn.rs` is\nisolated from the behavior fix.\n\n## What\n\n- Extends `ContextWindowTokenStatus` with `context_remaining_tokens`.\n- Updates `get_context_remaining` to use the shared context-window\naccounting.\n- Adds integration coverage for body-after-prefix reminder timing and\n`get_context_remaining` output.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core body_after_prefix_window`\n- `just test -p codex-core auto_compact_body_after_prefix`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`","tree":{"sha":"860ba4f4ceb0e6e11b75aa9850d5a0ce5475f236","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/860ba4f4ceb0e6e11b75aa9850d5a0ce5475f236"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/77e7ce13741048772f77c761eed84a81f4403823","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOxIGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtCMQABzLcgMRQLhm48O26or2Ws4G\n35Q5C0r/x4EY/qBVi+ZTsZ/rM/dz4qJIEIcjnOyEUwaRiRzcsYqU76A2ZFQanp2O\nIdMhhzNdVgaAuhVk3GWcj5W/20fBd/TMu06g0NbMHzkVIkTFnNGZDmKMNSbZpj7/\n/HkvADG3tgLRXIsyKO5y0FQbbqFF0obAt8owifTzvgFM7CKonUsin1fo6I8jsfUU\nVFVchhP7YuUPnVPNHSOhnpbivC11OBE03YUNiGPFY7GGbH2nqORESiQAzdXxk3MS\nRIlSdMjLrq5082wqx+RnYwycg5zEnjC3eMzFubKzQkFWeuT8H5+DJu3ZYH08I8c8\nYpHYi4mdRVqUMUpqIdqnPCdtxad7S7GbuE5YgiZR1eeANIhVJDRUOiVvx1vVuZBI\nqobjj2qjvkHOz+en76sx+U/RxPjk4hB2+OZrBbop28tA06/hlQlVy14VWoa+lKyZ\nY54avIx1zwpKkIrc41WFVN6qEB67UuhkeQ7nPNKxM7RKTrW/lXbrTclEAxJAEpD2\n4E6PwARo5PlSznOaH0gQIeCOBTZGMGkef4eIU6ZWyNXtJSE2m0hvlv3YbXNIto6l\nC4etVsyR/jr6THp/p9fdZvjcJs8ICyvFiX/hYfqki0aXNZufIBAKENZaWFlV6kRn\nFmsf8oSXyvUvEAqARB28\n=ZiC4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 860ba4f4ceb0e6e11b75aa9850d5a0ce5475f236\nparent 4dde907d27489046daf2e2bbe90e59eb6ffecad8\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1782256134 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782256134 +0000\n\nfix: scope context remaining to body window (#29665)\n\n## Why\n\nWith `model_auto_compact_token_limit_scope = \"body_after_prefix\"`, the\npersistent prefix should not count against the active body window.\n`get_context_remaining` and the token-budget reminder should report the\nsame usable body-after-prefix window that auto-compaction uses, rather\nthan the total token count since the session began.\n\nThis is stacked on #29664 so the mechanical move from `turn.rs` is\nisolated from the behavior fix.\n\n## What\n\n- Extends `ContextWindowTokenStatus` with `context_remaining_tokens`.\n- Updates `get_context_remaining` to use the shared context-window\naccounting.\n- Adds integration coverage for body-after-prefix reminder timing and\n`get_context_remaining` output.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core body_after_prefix_window`\n- `just test -p codex-core auto_compact_body_after_prefix`\n- `just fix -p codex-core`","verified_at":"2026-06-23T23:08:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/77e7ce13741048772f77c761eed84a81f4403823","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/77e7ce13741048772f77c761eed84a81f4403823","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/77e7ce13741048772f77c761eed84a81f4403823/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4dde907d27489046daf2e2bbe90e59eb6ffecad8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4dde907d27489046daf2e2bbe90e59eb6ffecad8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4dde907d27489046daf2e2bbe90e59eb6ffecad8"}]},{"sha":"4dde907d27489046daf2e2bbe90e59eb6ffecad8","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRkZGU5MDdkMjc0ODkwNDZkYWYyZTJiYmU5MGU1OWViNmZmZWNhZDg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T22:49:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T22:49:30Z"},"message":"refactor: extract context window token status (#29664)\n\n## Why\n\nThis PR keeps the mechanical helper extraction separate from the\nbehavior change in #29665. The follow-up needs the token-window\naccounting from `turn.rs` in another call path, but reviewing that is\nmuch easier when the helper extraction is separate from the semantic\nchange.\n\n## What\n\n- Adds `session/context_window.rs` with `ContextWindowTokenStatus`.\n- Moves the existing auto-compaction token-status calculation out of\n`session/turn.rs`.\n- Replaces the duplicated inline remaining-token calculation in\n`turn.rs` with `tokens_until_compaction()`.\n\nThis PR is intended to be behavior-preserving. The\n`get_context_remaining` behavior change is stacked separately in #29665.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core auto_compact_body_after_prefix`\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/29664).\n* #29665\n* __->__ #29664","tree":{"sha":"2d814af67df9a7a3e691ef05788fcd7a7d9a43d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2d814af67df9a7a3e691ef05788fcd7a7d9a43d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4dde907d27489046daf2e2bbe90e59eb6ffecad8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOw16CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7bkQABdS4qvEJh8EYA6TljSl0hte\nrRgGQqzVgnc/lhSF3sFP4WQQ1qiNKGWim+RUDQRgxHR9O8vJDYM7d1RYlrFMxKHw\nhK+M2elBtiloLEVVAyGgTGA+q0oeyEHyMVz07AcbstLK3tnrShnobt1a1UD2Yw0P\ncf7hQmnBeduZ1uVW0Rn11bjLMNgFeuBPx6jU9UACS/ewRY5n7Y6cAZ3bjZims13/\ngNJDjkAO5p9zmooUn3L8HoKe4x1NAYtXsQZBFwtOAqotTDD/0XBa2oqRKBcSaEdQ\nME/m7VES41uhaWZT8N8Lji62hi1OC9dal8rf/OhOkPpG53j+bObJ7oDlZJqLqmlW\nPS+lztGmI0ZjgCd6tu74yTVm2nKunvzvb4Ar8p+YAGqOng0ySJsEKQY7tLKZwbBr\n9TK0klv+RilRB6p6X11a5jNm5J1piugWYIw7ecQ22gisR7QtgTTaHfE2xxh4qSlT\nO2TIDeYJp2NL8X/wSRICT9J/cnk1pCdnnkjoDwQrHuTbVQaIkj7Rs1dTT9i0kNJs\n+bfNZ/8WOUtxddDKlGrqmOJE8jys/wqqK+3+DWWzuxEuBptG37u1s77BndDv+WuG\nlAvwXnl+baomcOkw6QFjhZfyjj3G7Z5lYily2b5tvQ8a1jZdxB1RoqeNvXmwL7hx\njwDcbIlFFUe+EqzvNopG\n=d93K\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2d814af67df9a7a3e691ef05788fcd7a7d9a43d2\nparent 829f5b6b59d72a8f3e16036a5896ade90eb96a35\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1782254970 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782254970 -0700\n\nrefactor: extract context window token status (#29664)\n\n## Why\n\nThis PR keeps the mechanical helper extraction separate from the\nbehavior change in #29665. The follow-up needs the token-window\naccounting from `turn.rs` in another call path, but reviewing that is\nmuch easier when the helper extraction is separate from the semantic\nchange.\n\n## What\n\n- Adds `session/context_window.rs` with `ContextWindowTokenStatus`.\n- Moves the existing auto-compaction token-status calculation out of\n`session/turn.rs`.\n- Replaces the duplicated inline remaining-token calculation in\n`turn.rs` with `tokens_until_compaction()`.\n\nThis PR is intended to be behavior-preserving. The\n`get_context_remaining` behavior change is stacked separately in #29665.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core auto_compact_body_after_prefix`\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n[//]: # (BEGIN SAPLING FOOTER)\nStack created with [Sapling](https://sapling-scm.com). Best reviewed\nwith [ReviewStack](https://reviewstack.dev/openai/codex/pull/29664).\n* #29665\n* __->__ #29664","verified_at":"2026-06-23T22:49:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4dde907d27489046daf2e2bbe90e59eb6ffecad8","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4dde907d27489046daf2e2bbe90e59eb6ffecad8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4dde907d27489046daf2e2bbe90e59eb6ffecad8/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"829f5b6b59d72a8f3e16036a5896ade90eb96a35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/829f5b6b59d72a8f3e16036a5896ade90eb96a35","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/829f5b6b59d72a8f3e16036a5896ade90eb96a35"}]},{"sha":"829f5b6b59d72a8f3e16036a5896ade90eb96a35","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDgyOWY1YjZiNTlkNzJhOGYzZTE2MDM2YTU4OTZhZGU5MGViOTZhMzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T22:37:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T22:37:31Z"},"message":"protocol: separate app and exec RPC ownership (#29714)\n\n## Why\n\nThe app-server and exec-server expose separate JSON-RPC APIs, but\nexec-server currently sources its serialized protocol and envelope types\nthrough app-server-oriented code. Giving each API an explicit owner\nmakes the crate boundary legible without introducing shared generic\nenvelopes.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `codex-exec-server-protocol` to own exec DTOs, process IDs, and\nJSON-RPC envelopes.\n- Updated exec-server clients, transports, handlers, and tests to use\nthe new crate.\n- Exposed app-server's existing JSON-RPC types through a public `rpc`\nmodule while retaining root re-exports.\n- Preserved existing wire shapes, including exec `PathUri` behavior.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is PR 1 of 6. Next: [PR\n#29721](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29721), which moves auth\nmode below the app wire boundary.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Exec-server protocol and server coverage passed in the focused\nprotocol test runs.\n- App-server protocol schema fixtures passed.","tree":{"sha":"74ce4b32e537f1baa84f9e4d16b75776219efa39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/74ce4b32e537f1baa84f9e4d16b75776219efa39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/829f5b6b59d72a8f3e16036a5896ade90eb96a35","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOwqrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6CgQAJHdRJQ0nQUAe/l88k7bbN/S\nLc9lmKgrwSWJbQKWkRl+GmvlyEtOj+bskfIE1qqj0nQGhJfFahb5vwzna6eW3coI\nr6bd4xWQnb+iFjelQ9KfQfA2df4zd8OFSOl4QHPTHDQ1IxUPSLHQR0vh/lyffitz\ntyPGSH6PFjvTm7KK+WZH0lB11HihTN/FcHO5SwL25c84q1Ce8vbAH62ItIYaiL1/\n3BPQv4r/leQtU/ISyfPP9ilJhW1DXHZasv0aAuMxHM3rh99oHxmA9sVkCrTL2/Rw\nHfNfASBkx6O4pCiYdw5ybAcODVvdmwwE/T+myfuP8DsgpDGlTOqAyJusFY1uMuVi\ne50CT0s9H0Rv6a2AiR+BYmtWfUW1ABNEhLck7rqCA//1RkZWEqlC5fU/JgpyhaI/\nx1hh6eQpi92Y65xFpx2pYBbrLhXdeXM9ASMqnuCgVUkuP2kUnERTrU96lHbR9/B3\nVou3AZh3SZSRV2XZrq96h1/qZVSQi13mYWo9EV+tC3XMqG1P04zgefIczK35YXQA\nUHyQMAid6/MH297AkkoA2susmtw8b4TNTOeOqvji7FpBwx5EeIDbXJFg/Aop8U96\n2qMz5KKJ6hHuu7QW/PCTIthzVTwuOmp4JdmeheUiiZtf5QWBAczQrQFe7qSJK+JX\npf3Yc4cl9VAReLGgOHBs\n=dgt3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 74ce4b32e537f1baa84f9e4d16b75776219efa39\nparent 220f5b76b2ea38903a67da0444c44b07a4b14a9e\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1782254251 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782254251 +0000\n\nprotocol: separate app and exec RPC ownership (#29714)\n\n## Why\n\nThe app-server and exec-server expose separate JSON-RPC APIs, but\nexec-server currently sources its serialized protocol and envelope types\nthrough app-server-oriented code. Giving each API an explicit owner\nmakes the crate boundary legible without introducing shared generic\nenvelopes.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `codex-exec-server-protocol` to own exec DTOs, process IDs, and\nJSON-RPC envelopes.\n- Updated exec-server clients, transports, handlers, and tests to use\nthe new crate.\n- Exposed app-server's existing JSON-RPC types through a public `rpc`\nmodule while retaining root re-exports.\n- Preserved existing wire shapes, including exec `PathUri` behavior.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is PR 1 of 6. Next: [PR\n#29721](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29721), which moves auth\nmode below the app wire boundary.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Exec-server protocol and server coverage passed in the focused\nprotocol test runs.\n- App-server protocol schema fixtures passed.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T22:37:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/829f5b6b59d72a8f3e16036a5896ade90eb96a35","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/829f5b6b59d72a8f3e16036a5896ade90eb96a35","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/829f5b6b59d72a8f3e16036a5896ade90eb96a35/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"220f5b76b2ea38903a67da0444c44b07a4b14a9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/220f5b76b2ea38903a67da0444c44b07a4b14a9e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/220f5b76b2ea38903a67da0444c44b07a4b14a9e"}]},{"sha":"220f5b76b2ea38903a67da0444c44b07a4b14a9e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDIyMGY1Yjc2YjJlYTM4OTAzYTY3ZGEwNDQ0YzQ0YjA3YTRiMTRhOWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T22:26:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T22:26:06Z"},"message":"Load executor skills without host path conversion (#29626)\n\n## Why\n\nAfter #28918, selected skill roots are `PathUri`, but the executor skill\nprovider still converts them to the app-server host's `AbsolutePathBuf`.\nA foreign Windows root therefore cannot be discovered by a Unix host,\nand the inverse has the same problem.\n\nThis PR keeps executor skill discovery and reads on the filesystem that\nowns the selected root while reusing the existing skill rules.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Generalize the existing skill traversal to operate on `PathUri`\nthrough `ExecutorFileSystem`, preserving its depth, directory, symlink,\nand sibling-metadata concurrency behavior.\n- Add a small environment skill loader that reuses the shared discovery,\nfrontmatter validation, dependency parsing, product policy, and\nprompt-visibility rules.\n- Keep the environment id and entrypoint `PathUri` in the skill catalog,\nthen route `skills.read` back through the same environment filesystem.\n- Preserve the executor's path convention when deriving catalog handles,\nincluding literal backslashes in POSIX filenames.\n- Resolve plugin namespaces from nearby manifests through URI-native\nfilesystem reads.\n- Cover foreign Windows roots, executor-owned reads, namespaces,\nmetadata, policy, and path identity.\n\n```text\nselected root (PathUri)\n        |\n        v\nshared discovery over ExecutorFileSystem\n        |\n        v\nenvironment-bound catalog entry --skills.read--> same ExecutorFileSystem\n```\n\nNo second filesystem abstraction or duplicate traversal implementation\nis introduced.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #29614 — add lexical `PathUri` containment.\n2. #29620 — share URI-native manifest path resolution.\n3. #28918 — keep selected plugin roots and resources URI-native.\n4. **This PR** — load executor skills without host path conversion.\n5. #29628 — resolve executor MCP working directories without host path\nconversion.","tree":{"sha":"a93ac3d68067690869316fc638803f32f0a30fc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a93ac3d68067690869316fc638803f32f0a30fc5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/220f5b76b2ea38903a67da0444c44b07a4b14a9e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOwf+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANuwQABkWs5x//pAqL+tKosc7zWp/\njBgscV2SJj6j3quBkFyj8t9PCDykiAE32JH22sF1QKYQEWBr8ZF6ZxYw0EM4osCc\nisj5cigrjEtx7+2KcesWefJrqpkuGg1Io53gy5k4DmGs310oxksJRoUQZLHJrf8E\nDUXR3BUFLAsppj2PcGlfj6ZnPgObGvodxnB8t8Ja4aQMWNLqOSjrQA61HwrLRkj3\nNW8Y/NYDkqOmlOQGB72KOWjpj5Eye/8OcH5gVnvSUIHIz6N1zpUghFVqZaYCY76z\nifcIaI/hXAz/nzysyXXBXeJmZar9ZVr33xYFZrhWJ0tH9bZ6l2QTaMzCGrjlzYQ+\nDUTELaKS7SLiP/gwyhSSziPBHNnyXygO9DRBI8t0ZAVJpXzgEFAtrrght5GevixN\nOB6DF0CrEWAYw/ESYWdIUyy6UVgQj76KzBeFQAiAkJlmsuzXdA6+VCkxYRj81I+x\ndJ7BJNwX+M42a4/Rzm7OF2OtwTYdHECtE2AXXe4g2mhhyyY/aRg84GnCl6lM149F\n+thNgXdh8RE4KvyPiWMoDN+nUyuGhtFQIy5xp+L8LnASnn2m9TJVI1HoesilFjt2\niTTMmb/qJ05fvNOCw40tTeUkvqIRgEt66c3/S6SMMknAZUknU/DjSP1hurSyoDEu\n5AP0Cjkx1ekQT0ig5VOe\n=xlCi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a93ac3d68067690869316fc638803f32f0a30fc5\nparent db6e676afc3234d2ea2c5d9e337e98088bef5a48\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782253566 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782253566 +0100\n\nLoad executor skills without host path conversion (#29626)\n\n## Why\n\nAfter #28918, selected skill roots are `PathUri`, but the executor skill\nprovider still converts them to the app-server host's `AbsolutePathBuf`.\nA foreign Windows root therefore cannot be discovered by a Unix host,\nand the inverse has the same problem.\n\nThis PR keeps executor skill discovery and reads on the filesystem that\nowns the selected root while reusing the existing skill rules.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Generalize the existing skill traversal to operate on `PathUri`\nthrough `ExecutorFileSystem`, preserving its depth, directory, symlink,\nand sibling-metadata concurrency behavior.\n- Add a small environment skill loader that reuses the shared discovery,\nfrontmatter validation, dependency parsing, product policy, and\nprompt-visibility rules.\n- Keep the environment id and entrypoint `PathUri` in the skill catalog,\nthen route `skills.read` back through the same environment filesystem.\n- Preserve the executor's path convention when deriving catalog handles,\nincluding literal backslashes in POSIX filenames.\n- Resolve plugin namespaces from nearby manifests through URI-native\nfilesystem reads.\n- Cover foreign Windows roots, executor-owned reads, namespaces,\nmetadata, policy, and path identity.\n\n```text\nselected root (PathUri)\n        |\n        v\nshared discovery over ExecutorFileSystem\n        |\n        v\nenvironment-bound catalog entry --skills.read--> same ExecutorFileSystem\n```\n\nNo second filesystem abstraction or duplicate traversal implementation\nis introduced.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #29614 — add lexical `PathUri` containment.\n2. #29620 — share URI-native manifest path resolution.\n3. #28918 — keep selected plugin roots and resources URI-native.\n4. **This PR** — load executor skills without host path conversion.\n5. #29628 — resolve executor MCP working directories without host path\nconversion.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T22:26:07Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/220f5b76b2ea38903a67da0444c44b07a4b14a9e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/220f5b76b2ea38903a67da0444c44b07a4b14a9e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/220f5b76b2ea38903a67da0444c44b07a4b14a9e/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"db6e676afc3234d2ea2c5d9e337e98088bef5a48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/db6e676afc3234d2ea2c5d9e337e98088bef5a48","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/db6e676afc3234d2ea2c5d9e337e98088bef5a48"}]},{"sha":"db6e676afc3234d2ea2c5d9e337e98088bef5a48","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGRiNmU2NzZhZmMzMjM0ZDJlYTJjNWQ5ZTMzN2U5ODA4OGJlZjVhNDg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Channing Conger","email":"cconger@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T22:14:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T22:14:13Z"},"message":"code-mode: Remove Session::is_alive() (#29732)\n\nRemove this unused API. This API is insidious in that it implies that\nalive state should be determinable from the caller, and implies that a\npreflight should indicate routing. Lets drop this, and handle errors\ncorrectly from a failed session in the future.","tree":{"sha":"fa68a8f00526d684a276b8997fa9cbf567f12ea9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/fa68a8f00526d684a276b8997fa9cbf567f12ea9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/db6e676afc3234d2ea2c5d9e337e98088bef5a48","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOwU1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhAUQACTwWzCj+mlWOiXfmu65wSZ1\n9D9fvHROnxpk1dfVm4Svvt4WknmDdrGeeIONcOW4ll5AoIEnFxx60XEpsD6QfVg/\nxZCqExlbpL0EqohRpuJ5Iw03CXxbuXJ8PuwS3B7sDD0WX7wSKETkJBEXw8hKYCKS\ngjcDJgfUySFc09llHPqyYaHXZLXqCsPUyuYq8kGJ0kj3RmNFaX7iJZmIJPgdbyPn\nOMqEGTz5xnsfDwYJqNAL9SCEDkb/ol/iADluPCCSSy0e2jb8SVXv8JpYFZ8v2bua\nMCXtSVFd0xE7XEwbAy1GQWksGgBW5ezqIiTYgVtCxk88dFcJyZjoCwoo1Sf3fkeI\nwf59sxOi66OSqKybSzR8YRgWeQfos+rkkcXsiLarxBSSU/f7XBj+XX1LWtaJiw/t\nFptJRYb4zJ8+ir55SZDUJvQFB6TalVzTiMUsG6iXQCxsikMPQ4gilmowOXVw5bnT\n7ygtAuZoRpJCIrWKKW1WdNjv1dsBkMZIZ0iKir/7T3pDlU7ps8Co4CofgWF1G4s3\nsMx7ssyst4Xa7mNy14tha2gMB8eBN62n9OFtanuV0AEw2q+j40CP8aJyzXcB4hIS\npdMaOwqdrHMSybd/krLmAWBW2SJd6xQYTuwUWHMODEbUmnZJlCckUJZNE9GdYr6I\nLHO9WcuHRFHrYOm3lS3k\n=b8QW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fa68a8f00526d684a276b8997fa9cbf567f12ea9\nparent bbbea919605494e64bb9bc35d69bdb0764e8dadf\nauthor Channing Conger <cconger@openai.com> 1782252853 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782252853 -0700\n\ncode-mode: Remove Session::is_alive() (#29732)\n\nRemove this unused API. This API is insidious in that it implies that\nalive state should be determinable from the caller, and implies that a\npreflight should indicate routing. Lets drop this, and handle errors\ncorrectly from a failed session in the future.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T22:14:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/db6e676afc3234d2ea2c5d9e337e98088bef5a48","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/db6e676afc3234d2ea2c5d9e337e98088bef5a48","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/db6e676afc3234d2ea2c5d9e337e98088bef5a48/comments","author":{"login":"cconger","id":200563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger","html_url":"https://github.com/cconger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bbbea919605494e64bb9bc35d69bdb0764e8dadf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bbbea919605494e64bb9bc35d69bdb0764e8dadf","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bbbea919605494e64bb9bc35d69bdb0764e8dadf"}]},{"sha":"bbbea919605494e64bb9bc35d69bdb0764e8dadf","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJiYmVhOTE5NjA1NDk0ZTY0YmI5YmMzNWQ2OWJkYjA3NjRlOGRhZGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T22:01:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T22:01:28Z"},"message":"[codex] surface rollout budget exhaustion (#29715)\n\n## Summary\n- surface shared rollout-budget exhaustion as\n`CodexErr::RolloutBudgetExceeded` instead of a generic interrupted turn\n- map it through the existing `CodexErrorInfo` and app-server v2\n`codexErrorInfo` path\n- keep local compaction from retrying after the shared rollout budget is\nexhausted\n\nThis gives app-server clients a stable `rolloutBudgetExceeded` error\nthey can classify without guessing from `status=\"interrupted\"`.\n\n## Tests\n- `just test -p codex-core rollout_budget`","tree":{"sha":"6fcbbd5c5b353d83ff9dbd236d7529fc0f44e63f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6fcbbd5c5b353d83ff9dbd236d7529fc0f44e63f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/bbbea919605494e64bb9bc35d69bdb0764e8dadf","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOwI4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAa2gQACz2aGrxvGytYnTOJrsuZ/0c\niTOC6MmbeY1l3LLpONMeSzeMr2mYJYya8kGSDYdGfKCj6GK82XIU5tqUgA5YibPZ\ne9nfhRo9aQnXna4rF305QjxoMlX92gSpOfnxw+XRmMKfPlzXSXuxlvN2npC+fE8N\ncTHAOSJqT7u7BtM8s/mDJ58YeNFMjBUOncM7qjSBwpP+DD5hlM2IEsyHjkmT3ljv\noZzDbjvkfjX6xETxuSDI/3AUPx66N0fT65i6fpbdgcmPlDqPD4oSwRELwkv9ntVt\nJ/pRM8e5H/staV2K2pmA27akut3D871vbiJSYkOR0OTOV0BQ27rJ9tG1M1EjGHOM\nYS31AVZgytcBJz7kk9ZViwGTLKFyD135dLBb/Gvk0AAE4xhUUPXSEQ/cSmPVtY+g\n5bhlQxNtKEiWbeeAn5qQz2pS4CFpA5r63TimA+McOdcchGWIxngXdl4WZs1cq0us\nGtm8PrWwqzzYzb3VnljOdMJqsxn5TAUjFnBiRNgZWk8MNaSKoHE0WKbrrwb1gdlv\nyMl12dy4GdTCCCDWpnF7FQHZz/DZjvj3qY9I2dorZ175UGHd1wOY0qrXjiE/l6Td\nzY/EBbBlJnindaU+Fi4jbc22AMUsMT4PLAinezqB5h1VOl5yU1ce4/Pew5rDwgL/\nxI+HDWl5O8FBvYOt1MM7\n=ON21\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6fcbbd5c5b353d83ff9dbd236d7529fc0f44e63f\nparent be0dfcfbea13c84fa1aa3ed75a0162f0edf8d3f5\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1782252088 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782252088 -0700\n\n[codex] surface rollout budget exhaustion (#29715)\n\n## Summary\n- surface shared rollout-budget exhaustion as\n`CodexErr::RolloutBudgetExceeded` instead of a generic interrupted turn\n- map it through the existing `CodexErrorInfo` and app-server v2\n`codexErrorInfo` path\n- keep local compaction from retrying after the shared rollout budget is\nexhausted\n\nThis gives app-server clients a stable `rolloutBudgetExceeded` error\nthey can classify without guessing from `status=\"interrupted\"`.\n\n## Tests\n- `just test -p codex-core rollout_budget`","verified_at":"2026-06-23T22:01:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bbbea919605494e64bb9bc35d69bdb0764e8dadf","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bbbea919605494e64bb9bc35d69bdb0764e8dadf","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bbbea919605494e64bb9bc35d69bdb0764e8dadf/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"be0dfcfbea13c84fa1aa3ed75a0162f0edf8d3f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/be0dfcfbea13c84fa1aa3ed75a0162f0edf8d3f5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/be0dfcfbea13c84fa1aa3ed75a0162f0edf8d3f5"}]},{"sha":"be0dfcfbea13c84fa1aa3ed75a0162f0edf8d3f5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJlMGRmY2ZiZWExM2M4NGZhMWFhM2VkNzVhMDE2MmYwZWRmOGQzZjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Channing Conger","email":"cconger@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T21:57:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T21:57:44Z"},"message":"[codex] define code mode host handshake protocol (#29515)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add validated protocol-version, capability, and session identifier\ntypes\n- define explicit `ClientToHost` and `HostToClient` JSON envelopes for\nconnection negotiation and session open/close acknowledgements\n- reject invalid states and unknown fields during decoding, with\nexplicit wire-format and round-trip coverage\n\n## Why\n\nThis establishes the transport-neutral encoding shape needed to build\nand test the new code-mode host incrementally. Cell, tool callback, and\nfailure-domain messages are intentionally deferred until their actors\nand behavior tests establish the required semantics.\n\nThis is additive protocol scaffolding and does not change the current\nproduction code-mode implementation.\n\n## Validation","tree":{"sha":"4118fc8d8f60a988fcde086548a85abc96fc6877","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4118fc8d8f60a988fcde086548a85abc96fc6877"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/be0dfcfbea13c84fa1aa3ed75a0162f0edf8d3f5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOwFYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPQ8QABXbZ3AjvZgY7WnHYJKIi4aB\nZsUp9Ot/9DxMAQxmqdw+szvo47v3szqVNrCWWIY4h2wrORmEaOKRrn+h0zmkxScu\nmW3xuCTFXg7PQm7lLWpb0Rr1Hr916S+135zghmTrUKajtCu5AKwmhMC4IOhVf76H\nLxPwQbBTsWGOnPoRa9WDvtuuk/jE29snZiOLVDS8XQ2nXovf8rh8RaROfRkFSz3I\nfOE+GfmyeKDZFlGTn813A++aEaPrUDrf+utpF4wHq7IF/Q2qb+9XpNtKi2Pix67p\nmBrDGgiEA2uivtPnj0NeYY5oAik4hpvj6FXba8VJNDxsXiijxQwSQOYP7XYV7W0I\nyBhRmVAYQ8VNH+l1zL1UIVsIlUlVAzUsFi9fRhTaN/DTeWA4KisSzD4rz+r7mZEl\n1l7nk7hTTK89+viSfoquDilKXt432EiZ99qnMXmb4ZqqDUIWf2UEHEmE+2DUXDt8\nZ2rOtDgCwRXKfvdto6wqylsa6A2hH8oVffy6iRQrYnMMLY6UhpR19TIaW2jP1bOv\nKmDjmvfoif9kvAMWweZL1vNQQvleT7PxD+M6YIiiimLqptq3TqiuEb7//v+Qleni\nqo3cHGAW6W3MX2ePBsaPlyAg0cM9IueVityPruuNEmknJCYpNtK1JWsv0oc4oQPf\n69oChzvtI+425qq5OiB6\n=Nu6C\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4118fc8d8f60a988fcde086548a85abc96fc6877\nparent 2e69966cd8fbb3f0265152af778dd5512c66d151\nauthor Channing Conger <cconger@openai.com> 1782251864 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782251864 -0700\n\n[codex] define code mode host handshake protocol (#29515)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add validated protocol-version, capability, and session identifier\ntypes\n- define explicit `ClientToHost` and `HostToClient` JSON envelopes for\nconnection negotiation and session open/close acknowledgements\n- reject invalid states and unknown fields during decoding, with\nexplicit wire-format and round-trip coverage\n\n## Why\n\nThis establishes the transport-neutral encoding shape needed to build\nand test the new code-mode host incrementally. Cell, tool callback, and\nfailure-domain messages are intentionally deferred until their actors\nand behavior tests establish the required semantics.\n\nThis is additive protocol scaffolding and does not change the current\nproduction code-mode implementation.\n\n## Validation","verified_at":"2026-06-23T21:57:44Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/be0dfcfbea13c84fa1aa3ed75a0162f0edf8d3f5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/be0dfcfbea13c84fa1aa3ed75a0162f0edf8d3f5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/be0dfcfbea13c84fa1aa3ed75a0162f0edf8d3f5/comments","author":{"login":"cconger","id":200563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger","html_url":"https://github.com/cconger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2e69966cd8fbb3f0265152af778dd5512c66d151","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2e69966cd8fbb3f0265152af778dd5512c66d151","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2e69966cd8fbb3f0265152af778dd5512c66d151"}]},{"sha":"2e69966cd8fbb3f0265152af778dd5512c66d151","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDJlNjk5NjZjZDhmYmIzZjAyNjUxNTJhZjc3OGRkNTUxMmM2NmQxNTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T21:51:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T21:51:19Z"},"message":"Make selected plugin roots URI-native (#28918)\n\n## Why\n\nSelected capability roots belong to the executor filesystem, not the\napp-server host. Converting their path strings into the host's native\n`Path` breaks whenever the two machines use different path conventions,\nsuch as a Windows executor behind a Unix app-server.\n\nThis PR establishes `PathUri` as the selected-plugin boundary so the\nexecutor remains authoritative for its paths.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Require `selectedCapabilityRoots[].location.path` to be a canonical\n`file:` URI and deserialize it directly as `PathUri`; native path\nstrings are rejected.\n- Update the app-server schema, generated TypeScript, examples, and\nrequest coverage for the URI contract.\n- Keep selected roots, resolved plugin locations, manifest paths, and\nmanifest resources as `PathUri`.\n- Inspect and read plugin roots and manifests only through the selected\nenvironment's `ExecutorFileSystem`.\n- Parse executor manifests with the shared URI-native parser from #29620\ninstead of projecting them onto the host filesystem.\n- Enforce resource containment lexically and preserve the root URI's\nPOSIX or Windows path convention.\n- Cover foreign Windows plugin roots and URI-native manifest resources.\n\n```text\nthread/start\n  selectedCapabilityRoots[].location.path = \"file:///C:/plugins/demo\"\n                              | PathUri\n                              v\n                    ExecutorFileSystem\n                              |\n                              +--> plugin.json\n                              +--> manifest resources\n```\n\nThis PR stops at the shared selected-plugin representation. The next two\nPRs remove the remaining host-path projections in the skill and MCP\nconsumers.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #29614 — add lexical `PathUri` containment.\n2. #29620 — share URI-native manifest path resolution.\n3. **This PR** — keep selected plugin roots and resources URI-native.\n4. #29626 — load executor skills without host path conversion.\n5. #29628 — resolve executor MCP working directories without host path\nconversion.","tree":{"sha":"91b5646b97a27721e880dbb22aca145dbf1bf28a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/91b5646b97a27721e880dbb22aca145dbf1bf28a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/2e69966cd8fbb3f0265152af778dd5512c66d151","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOv/XCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2r4QAHgY8TiPk5y7n07yQn3oaefP\n3pu5VnFyBFFmi30zJyCDNBzAbfX0j8C49KsG70w44AwChqLLDpF/sHIUSeuArZXN\nsIkfLt2xwX9FxtOaiaoRqMTvhDkY2dEV2N3+FCWNvcQhcfgGzz/jxiZjkm463B9e\n3RPDD9qXKS/WvqHcWItKjvaVpZOboy7mWcGPTkoetndRPhsKe7QDuRK5SxV7yho9\nmFrYcGT4ovu5YXP86PsV9F+dURxGGVV5MhepiWX71g6Axj9Antq2IGOLV5D4BEy/\nNi5i0M6tKrlSu+C1VP5zJgwRkpXjrXXLiBZn1OZcp+U3+0exQHtv7RkRFCPlzIxZ\nnw4eCkg10ZWG25YoexhV7AuhOJqP6VjD7m6MkOsjn1sb8gKuFOK1I75vR4oneCYM\nhEZI2d5T8AFaVmwcGh8Vsd89wou6gvaZUVrmQhyBkfZ0nDyw0kJOPIM3z3tA0ptt\nCkYlfpnjupPIBDyvP5xFbx/SqzxhWtqCQl09sL7iFSFz/PsnW79upLAbZGyivvQq\n1/awgyI+5/L3z0lQaW+LDcW4dGUhXda6FrbNaLhgJYsEomOfG97GeWM7CIsJOkzL\n1J3tv9qppCBzwTVF0AeaFDOvfprVMNc3EVQeOBJn7/650/4XW5jYFdAAHwonBtmL\nXzWc7CqIwMafowHuP5nr\n=Dm4x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 91b5646b97a27721e880dbb22aca145dbf1bf28a\nparent 01f89c8c59fc2d92f7c60bfb834a8f01635e57a1\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782251479 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782251479 +0100\n\nMake selected plugin roots URI-native (#28918)\n\n## Why\n\nSelected capability roots belong to the executor filesystem, not the\napp-server host. Converting their path strings into the host's native\n`Path` breaks whenever the two machines use different path conventions,\nsuch as a Windows executor behind a Unix app-server.\n\nThis PR establishes `PathUri` as the selected-plugin boundary so the\nexecutor remains authoritative for its paths.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Require `selectedCapabilityRoots[].location.path` to be a canonical\n`file:` URI and deserialize it directly as `PathUri`; native path\nstrings are rejected.\n- Update the app-server schema, generated TypeScript, examples, and\nrequest coverage for the URI contract.\n- Keep selected roots, resolved plugin locations, manifest paths, and\nmanifest resources as `PathUri`.\n- Inspect and read plugin roots and manifests only through the selected\nenvironment's `ExecutorFileSystem`.\n- Parse executor manifests with the shared URI-native parser from #29620\ninstead of projecting them onto the host filesystem.\n- Enforce resource containment lexically and preserve the root URI's\nPOSIX or Windows path convention.\n- Cover foreign Windows plugin roots and URI-native manifest resources.\n\n```text\nthread/start\n  selectedCapabilityRoots[].location.path = \"file:///C:/plugins/demo\"\n                              | PathUri\n                              v\n                    ExecutorFileSystem\n                              |\n                              +--> plugin.json\n                              +--> manifest resources\n```\n\nThis PR stops at the shared selected-plugin representation. The next two\nPRs remove the remaining host-path projections in the skill and MCP\nconsumers.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #29614 — add lexical `PathUri` containment.\n2. #29620 — share URI-native manifest path resolution.\n3. **This PR** — keep selected plugin roots and resources URI-native.\n4. #29626 — load executor skills without host path conversion.\n5. #29628 — resolve executor MCP working directories without host path\nconversion.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T21:51:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2e69966cd8fbb3f0265152af778dd5512c66d151","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/2e69966cd8fbb3f0265152af778dd5512c66d151","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/2e69966cd8fbb3f0265152af778dd5512c66d151/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"01f89c8c59fc2d92f7c60bfb834a8f01635e57a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/01f89c8c59fc2d92f7c60bfb834a8f01635e57a1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/01f89c8c59fc2d92f7c60bfb834a8f01635e57a1"}]},{"sha":"01f89c8c59fc2d92f7c60bfb834a8f01635e57a1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDAxZjg5YzhjNTlmYzJkOTJmN2M2MGJmYjgzNGE4ZjAxNjM1ZTU3YTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Bolin","email":"mbolin@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T21:50:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T21:50:50Z"},"message":"core: persist initial context window metadata (#29519)\n\n## Why\n\nPR #29494 made context-window IDs visible to the model by wrapping the\ntoken-budget window payload in `<context_window>`, but rollout JSONL\nconsumers still could not see the initial window identity by tailing the\nsession file. Compacted rollout items carry window IDs only after\ncompaction has happened, so a session with no compaction had no durable\nJSONL record for window 0.\n\nThis change gives tailing consumers a stable initial-window record at\nsession creation time.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added `session_meta.context_window.window_id` for the initial\ncontext-window identity.\n- `CreateThreadParams` now requires `initial_window_id: String`, so\nthread-store callers cannot accidentally create new threads without\nwindow-0 metadata.\n- Live thread creation derives the persisted initial window ID from the\nsame `AutoCompactWindowIds` used to initialize `SessionState`, keeping\nruntime state and JSONL metadata aligned.\n- Rollout reconstruction uses `session_meta.context_window.window_id` as\nthe initial-window fallback and derives `window_number = 0`,\n`first_window_id = window_id`, and `previous_window_id = None`\ninternally.\n- Fork reconstruction intentionally uses the same rollout reconstruction\npath; consumers that need to distinguish copied initial-window metadata\ncan use the rollout `thread_id`.\n- Legacy compactions without `window_number` still use compaction-count\nfallback accounting instead of being reset to window 0 by the\ninitial-window fallback.\n- Compacted rollout metadata still takes precedence once compaction\nrecords exist, preserving the richer chain fields there.\n\n## JSONL Shape\n\nReal rollout JSONL is one object per line. This example is expanded for\nreadability, but shows the new initial `session_meta.context_window`\nrecord followed by the existing compacted rollout item shape that also\ncarries window IDs:\n\n```jsonl\n{\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-22T12:00:00.000Z\",\n  \"type\": \"session_meta\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"session_id\": \"<THREAD_ID>\",\n    \"id\": \"<THREAD_ID>\",\n    \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-22T12:00:00.000Z\",\n    \"cwd\": \"/repo\",\n    \"originator\": \"codex\",\n    \"cli_version\": \"0.0.0\",\n    \"source\": \"cli\",\n    \"model_provider\": \"<MODEL_PROVIDER>\",\n    \"context_window\": {\n      \"window_id\": \"<INITIAL_WINDOW_ID>\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n...\n{\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-22T12:34:56.000Z\",\n  \"type\": \"compacted\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"message\": \"<COMPACTION_SUMMARY>\",\n    \"replacement_history\": [\n      \"...\"\n    ],\n    \"window_number\": 1,\n    \"first_window_id\": \"<INITIAL_WINDOW_ID>\",\n    \"previous_window_id\": \"<INITIAL_WINDOW_ID>\",\n    \"window_id\": \"<NEXT_WINDOW_ID>\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe nested `context_window` object is intentional: it gives rollout\nconsumers a stable namespace for context-window metadata while only\nwriting the non-derivable initial `window_id`. For the initial window,\n`window_number`, `first_window_id`, and `previous_window_id` are derived\ninternally instead of being written to the rollout.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout\nrecorder_materializes_on_flush_with_pending_items`\n- `just test -p codex-core reconstruct_history`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nrecord_initial_history_reconstructs_forked_transcript`\n- `just test -p codex-thread-store`\n- `just test -p codex-state`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nthread_read_returns_summary_without_turns`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout persistence_metrics`","tree":{"sha":"5344709892d67a4363bd415a7a37a084bc9fe645","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5344709892d67a4363bd415a7a37a084bc9fe645"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/01f89c8c59fc2d92f7c60bfb834a8f01635e57a1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOv+6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA95QQAAeAmCdzPPrKqR1/yPtDNVbn\ncgITMp/75XU08ASpb84ClSfv9RNEwEEHFBYbbgXazOo3xiK/QE8gRKbzaPiKdm1F\ne2vIyMU1mbySLw9hzAlJRCJRDOPv+KMViUIkG8dSZHPT/v6QRGNoGfqoejMhfsyn\nKSRFAB4LyqiGS+m6UvdqwpenQNVsOEoeyy5kknLuO6NB1H/C01q123QDsMkUy9oa\nRk7IXJXWKlRtDqQpIJrYAkgPghDK8cRR57C+AYGQEl3s/EJjitlGaDnHaZvoPL+i\nU/Fh4CMAomUauA0phLLqMsJ/Sb5mLMyoIcTzlgij9jd2nmoDeHyIN7243j1+9FMv\nXo7rdNC9WdDC9jxquNy8IpUluf0Cqml1oip6sKyf0f4wUAfydVB1lEpMaZ8eM5jQ\nfm60biS8Z8ShDvzWTJdHfrd2sAPMmFM8FFov+AJKvELeiVBv8Sb4FRvK+cIYmiKj\nvgdHhVuWcy3Fu6LZF04U7VXduysx0imxoCGeKlhSpwG279oICNLle164+p8hOYOX\nqxdA6ZxbLp8E4MYoZcWlvrA0SUxxp2ncr3gr4Do/dvx5Ew35ojIBWekoWRE2KN9x\n9DgK3vsNvp18x2pV/BDVeZ5dRuYODC/rUsOz19WVFaz//uUvhtia53EPas6Kzs4j\n0lCzrbBSYqemk2Q+X1/G\n=llsj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5344709892d67a4363bd415a7a37a084bc9fe645\nparent c26f961b85b9f4eb0218af00a402ed1ab30f3618\nauthor Michael Bolin <mbolin@openai.com> 1782251450 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782251450 +0000\n\ncore: persist initial context window metadata (#29519)\n\n## Why\n\nPR #29494 made context-window IDs visible to the model by wrapping the\ntoken-budget window payload in `<context_window>`, but rollout JSONL\nconsumers still could not see the initial window identity by tailing the\nsession file. Compacted rollout items carry window IDs only after\ncompaction has happened, so a session with no compaction had no durable\nJSONL record for window 0.\n\nThis change gives tailing consumers a stable initial-window record at\nsession creation time.\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Added `session_meta.context_window.window_id` for the initial\ncontext-window identity.\n- `CreateThreadParams` now requires `initial_window_id: String`, so\nthread-store callers cannot accidentally create new threads without\nwindow-0 metadata.\n- Live thread creation derives the persisted initial window ID from the\nsame `AutoCompactWindowIds` used to initialize `SessionState`, keeping\nruntime state and JSONL metadata aligned.\n- Rollout reconstruction uses `session_meta.context_window.window_id` as\nthe initial-window fallback and derives `window_number = 0`,\n`first_window_id = window_id`, and `previous_window_id = None`\ninternally.\n- Fork reconstruction intentionally uses the same rollout reconstruction\npath; consumers that need to distinguish copied initial-window metadata\ncan use the rollout `thread_id`.\n- Legacy compactions without `window_number` still use compaction-count\nfallback accounting instead of being reset to window 0 by the\ninitial-window fallback.\n- Compacted rollout metadata still takes precedence once compaction\nrecords exist, preserving the richer chain fields there.\n\n## JSONL Shape\n\nReal rollout JSONL is one object per line. This example is expanded for\nreadability, but shows the new initial `session_meta.context_window`\nrecord followed by the existing compacted rollout item shape that also\ncarries window IDs:\n\n```jsonl\n{\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-22T12:00:00.000Z\",\n  \"type\": \"session_meta\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"session_id\": \"<THREAD_ID>\",\n    \"id\": \"<THREAD_ID>\",\n    \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-22T12:00:00.000Z\",\n    \"cwd\": \"/repo\",\n    \"originator\": \"codex\",\n    \"cli_version\": \"0.0.0\",\n    \"source\": \"cli\",\n    \"model_provider\": \"<MODEL_PROVIDER>\",\n    \"context_window\": {\n      \"window_id\": \"<INITIAL_WINDOW_ID>\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n...\n{\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-22T12:34:56.000Z\",\n  \"type\": \"compacted\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"message\": \"<COMPACTION_SUMMARY>\",\n    \"replacement_history\": [\n      \"...\"\n    ],\n    \"window_number\": 1,\n    \"first_window_id\": \"<INITIAL_WINDOW_ID>\",\n    \"previous_window_id\": \"<INITIAL_WINDOW_ID>\",\n    \"window_id\": \"<NEXT_WINDOW_ID>\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe nested `context_window` object is intentional: it gives rollout\nconsumers a stable namespace for context-window metadata while only\nwriting the non-derivable initial `window_id`. For the initial window,\n`window_number`, `first_window_id`, and `previous_window_id` are derived\ninternally instead of being written to the rollout.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-protocol`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout\nrecorder_materializes_on_flush_with_pending_items`\n- `just test -p codex-core reconstruct_history`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nrecord_initial_history_reconstructs_forked_transcript`\n- `just test -p codex-thread-store`\n- `just test -p codex-state`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server\nthread_read_returns_summary_without_turns`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout persistence_metrics`","verified_at":"2026-06-23T21:50:51Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/01f89c8c59fc2d92f7c60bfb834a8f01635e57a1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/01f89c8c59fc2d92f7c60bfb834a8f01635e57a1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/01f89c8c59fc2d92f7c60bfb834a8f01635e57a1/comments","author":{"login":"bolinfest","id":655869,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTg2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/655869?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest","html_url":"https://github.com/bolinfest","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bolinfest/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c26f961b85b9f4eb0218af00a402ed1ab30f3618","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c26f961b85b9f4eb0218af00a402ed1ab30f3618","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c26f961b85b9f4eb0218af00a402ed1ab30f3618"}]},{"sha":"c26f961b85b9f4eb0218af00a402ed1ab30f3618","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGMyNmY5NjFiODViOWY0ZWIwMjE4YWYwMGE0MDJlZDFhYjMwZjM2MTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T21:47:00Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T21:47:00Z"},"message":"path-uri: remove legacy path deserialization (#29158)\n\n## Why\n\nI'd originally added `PathUri` legacy path deserialization thinking we'd\nwant it for having `PathUri` in public app-server APIs. Since then we've\nadded `LegacyAppPathString` to handle the messy conversions that we need\nfor backcompat. It's confusing for `PathUri` to support deserializing\nlegacy paths when we don't yet want to actually expose app-server\ncallers or rollout storage to the new URI format.\n\nStacked on top of #29472 to avoid breaking compatibility in case those\ntypes ended up stored somewhere for someone.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Parse deserialized `PathUri` values exclusively as valid `file:` URIs.\n- Replace legacy acceptance coverage with rejection coverage for\ntop-level filesystem paths and sandbox working directories.\n- Serialize CWDs in hand-built exec-server process requests as `PathUri`\nvalues.","tree":{"sha":"abadb5aff99b8b094c2c1d8daeb8489e5685a8c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/abadb5aff99b8b094c2c1d8daeb8489e5685a8c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c26f961b85b9f4eb0218af00a402ed1ab30f3618","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOv7UCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADScQAFVuoB30Bqk51nQiyMee4ey1\ngvBjCwKhm0q3D4Z/zRVjmLmg/RHm9XBgglsfLsnJab4POw9NqAjimgf5tvMA+0iX\nSDQm8YNlWSekxvQlDb6TwlGHVgDvklYVyiGp7EVZrmLlpnZ7LuG3YfKxM1p5VBJG\nLEinAiskCHyzA7xYd7xeK9j1iOAiEMHRDBHED0yEguYTdwZr11HrMnx2YLmrUZGj\ntlovROu4THPnJi3tuhmNNs2Rp+HpAYX798zl0yK9y8qkq1dvgVgFNrDWN9CSSWaD\nfYYr+1psdcdkMxhmU+852teSsxk6aBn0tngjWLZTKsUnWterp6d/+RWv1CHxnILN\nx/IXpYf/7hYPN8Fu+DG/Qlqjs2C3YDlJ0e4yE/XeF/x0oWZBoDsRrkMqiw7N3zO8\nnyTbAMf6jf+5JuSV0IVya3MGaxC0pejWborf44bgrq0fZRRS5U236v3TcWXaaV3W\n9zdpcqzLyZv+pOksMMja7cyO9/8+dHvsp3iY50w1UK0gbbsqt7ERPrTQwqOb+bbf\net3ktkYFGN53lMidjZM896NpdI7annc2Kusd7fqXiC10o16j00sapHWOk04D9HLE\nUhK1FFO50BFyrBe6z24uUu6OwqPcZIsVNH288zM+25Ercf7zWemSo7mqbnm2fMhd\nxGpuLfKUQRuRcfgYrBxy\n=USW4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree abadb5aff99b8b094c2c1d8daeb8489e5685a8c7\nparent 5283522939ebe193f167725d87cd634581465f7b\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1782251220 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782251220 +0000\n\npath-uri: remove legacy path deserialization (#29158)\n\n## Why\n\nI'd originally added `PathUri` legacy path deserialization thinking we'd\nwant it for having `PathUri` in public app-server APIs. Since then we've\nadded `LegacyAppPathString` to handle the messy conversions that we need\nfor backcompat. It's confusing for `PathUri` to support deserializing\nlegacy paths when we don't yet want to actually expose app-server\ncallers or rollout storage to the new URI format.\n\nStacked on top of #29472 to avoid breaking compatibility in case those\ntypes ended up stored somewhere for someone.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Parse deserialized `PathUri` values exclusively as valid `file:` URIs.\n- Replace legacy acceptance coverage with rejection coverage for\ntop-level filesystem paths and sandbox working directories.\n- Serialize CWDs in hand-built exec-server process requests as `PathUri`\nvalues.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T21:47:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c26f961b85b9f4eb0218af00a402ed1ab30f3618","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c26f961b85b9f4eb0218af00a402ed1ab30f3618","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c26f961b85b9f4eb0218af00a402ed1ab30f3618/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5283522939ebe193f167725d87cd634581465f7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5283522939ebe193f167725d87cd634581465f7b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5283522939ebe193f167725d87cd634581465f7b"}]},{"sha":"5283522939ebe193f167725d87cd634581465f7b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDUyODM1MjI5MzllYmUxOTNmMTY3NzI1ZDg3Y2Q2MzQ1ODE0NjVmN2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T21:45:06Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T21:45:06Z"},"message":"core tests: rename automatic environment builder (#29728)\n\n## Why\n\nUse a clearer name for what happens when this helper sets up a test\nenvironment.\n\n## What\n\n- Rename the builder and its harness wrapper to use `auto_env` instead\nof `remote_env` because the helper will set up a local environment if\nconfigured by the build system.","tree":{"sha":"888b298689772ab3dcd1250afe19d8880422a66a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/888b298689772ab3dcd1250afe19d8880422a66a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/5283522939ebe193f167725d87cd634581465f7b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOv5iCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXB8QAG1jURqYsrBlKDQbWwZnXDpN\n1s5gNIGX0A2OQVm343TTYjOX3LASi7NZu+Ce7SiVPTxhtF7osqZ+kFcd6Y7RDAh8\nJnD3gFOaa3zmgf06KkkWvYoC3B5WHcRLXNPwBuB6S73ckxxcVi1lMoApnpSCzGkz\nEIcbW8UIHv+/jGQ6AHOhffG4omhz1I+hvx9HoVsDfZn62a9j2GD2JLz8d8DX+NPS\nBzVAoAKbimbh0SjoM9e7GrfDxvlqkOlq1T1GCsTUhREns+qwPnUKzqofyeQ6g597\nLDFZu9+lmlZE2lMlYc8RimFjGtdfMfJo5I8N8cTmB4eIVM9ks5TK9bLF1qpfwUMW\no0+UL8QbEgCpozaikOPZTjW0GSWVEg+Ro1f5fgrgBLVfsf0rLnWJVZyzchUSORzW\nsQGBnaRcSizkV0CF4N/J1QtTqj68DebM5HCyd/3K6fxANHVCBtc5NXTa/bf9haxm\novQ3Ea/w1SVaI7uN4jz93eTS8nAT3iis35byFzTLfhA/Xx45hcC6CA7iz85RfdyZ\n5BFI8sPYvj2FJfBcIzASKETtenJJRFH2yz2t9a1tElMrpcPS9GNeS+zUz+dVK8Es\nP+j/Le5bzsuwF84B/pPsjvM6WIJYyoeB0zPFytiKLMqyq0Fdz+fnQN57NacSZGKT\nNkq+D6PtGcXNszI8z5KB\n=clnd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 888b298689772ab3dcd1250afe19d8880422a66a\nparent 9a79536e6b22128cd61b842324f7625ae594a901\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1782251106 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782251106 +0000\n\ncore tests: rename automatic environment builder (#29728)\n\n## Why\n\nUse a clearer name for what happens when this helper sets up a test\nenvironment.\n\n## What\n\n- Rename the builder and its harness wrapper to use `auto_env` instead\nof `remote_env` because the helper will set up a local environment if\nconfigured by the build system.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T21:45:06Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5283522939ebe193f167725d87cd634581465f7b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/5283522939ebe193f167725d87cd634581465f7b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/5283522939ebe193f167725d87cd634581465f7b/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9a79536e6b22128cd61b842324f7625ae594a901","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9a79536e6b22128cd61b842324f7625ae594a901","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9a79536e6b22128cd61b842324f7625ae594a901"}]},{"sha":"9a79536e6b22128cd61b842324f7625ae594a901","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDlhNzk1MzZlNmIyMjEyOGNkNjFiODQyMzI0Zjc2MjVhZTU5NGE5MDE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T21:27:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T21:27:13Z"},"message":"test: branch on target OS instead of runner flavor (#29712)\n\n## Why\n\nCore tests should branch on the executor's operating system, not on\nrunner details such as Docker or Wine. This keeps platform behavior\nstable as new test backends are added and reserves Wine-specific skips\nfor actual runner debt.\n\n## What\n\n- Add `TestTargetOs` and target/host-aware skip helpers while keeping\n`TestEnvironment` internal.\n- Replace topology enum access with remote predicates and a narrow\nDocker accessor.\n- Migrate OS-semantic Wine skips, preserve runner-specific gaps, and\ndocument the skip taxonomy.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p core_test_support`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nremote_test_env_can_connect_and_use_filesystem`\n- `bazel test //codex-rs/core:core-all-wine-exec-test\n--test_output=errors` reached test execution; unrelated existing\nview-image, path, and timing failures remain.\n- `just test -p codex-core` and `just test` reached broad test\nexecution; this checkout has unrelated helper, sandbox, and timing\nfailures.","tree":{"sha":"87e650033b792ab39f930018d409da6dde3448dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/87e650033b792ab39f930018d409da6dde3448dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9a79536e6b22128cd61b842324f7625ae594a901","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOvoxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWGcQAEJHHBSsSBp6ea0BGuH/e/2o\nwF/AWvFc5VsKHXBeI91bWAq5faWp1BBXTNM7eVbkOW5mk1A4rNbyD+tX7eNGrdQF\nFGWO+JFAyBD4gYMqLyeA/duxC9YsMjb+el//mgHOvbp9H60aivZAV33X9PmF60yB\nye5PrdRmo3IwYGfLSRzNeod2flCX6IxGX8YQprro2RFwyAUtXi3AT3PkuC8lmcF9\naUFt8UanBUM9l5sBy+EnqDOdgw5fBs2IsTdVh08fdOElGOyvBr3w9qkVtZ+pM5Qo\nIO8ZIZqEUO6xBJcubRCTXfYMW9iO7svSIXLwzKund6bOPArlnQTXBWXjU6h8hQKZ\nqh3gdvtL9ng2+G2mxDGtYh3/BDH67dCwxVy+4UzwJz7mPgMFQjcSNNc1N9lf8RnA\nu33ASM/tH+c/9jp22PyIGoob0Mrl11RdWdi8tlvfitZeYanDMWj4wjSMJEynptgr\nVlCgRGJj0ouq5xsYAXO7KqGxgughYDrpEI0/FtZEdxZU4MtY2DeAHsxKvuAf3rL1\njFrycYC0aPTsAme4EHFH0hx7Cp6Wl0OSI5IzaAj47tbTbJOkcGwHe3zuPBxUWVk6\nJJG3U/cttPyzySy5T7tns/mN2uUiXzyXDyc5iUuXCJ1A6HSWaD+O607jhGQOerSQ\nXqa9f9qFKaUXSD7esv+d\n=u1ib\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 87e650033b792ab39f930018d409da6dde3448dc\nparent 7b40e3523f6a91e2e99e0ba44dfe6601eaa1ac91\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1782250033 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782250033 -0700\n\ntest: branch on target OS instead of runner flavor (#29712)\n\n## Why\n\nCore tests should branch on the executor's operating system, not on\nrunner details such as Docker or Wine. This keeps platform behavior\nstable as new test backends are added and reserves Wine-specific skips\nfor actual runner debt.\n\n## What\n\n- Add `TestTargetOs` and target/host-aware skip helpers while keeping\n`TestEnvironment` internal.\n- Replace topology enum access with remote predicates and a narrow\nDocker accessor.\n- Migrate OS-semantic Wine skips, preserve runner-specific gaps, and\ndocument the skip taxonomy.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p core_test_support`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nremote_test_env_can_connect_and_use_filesystem`\n- `bazel test //codex-rs/core:core-all-wine-exec-test\n--test_output=errors` reached test execution; unrelated existing\nview-image, path, and timing failures remain.\n- `just test -p codex-core` and `just test` reached broad test\nexecution; this checkout has unrelated helper, sandbox, and timing\nfailures.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T21:27:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9a79536e6b22128cd61b842324f7625ae594a901","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9a79536e6b22128cd61b842324f7625ae594a901","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9a79536e6b22128cd61b842324f7625ae594a901/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oa