::CodeModeService (#29716)\n\nMechanical rename of CodeModeService => InProcessCodeModeSession\n\nThis already implements a CodeModeSession as its prime interface to\nCore. The name was vestigial _and_ confusing af when embedded inside\ncore::tools::code_mode::CodeModeService","verified_at":"2026-06-23T21:17:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7b40e3523f6a91e2e99e0ba44dfe6601eaa1ac91","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7b40e3523f6a91e2e99e0ba44dfe6601eaa1ac91","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7b40e3523f6a91e2e99e0ba44dfe6601eaa1ac91/comments","author":{"login":"cconger","id":200563,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMDU2Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/200563?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger","html_url":"https://github.com/cconger","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cconger/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1882719b30b01b50145fbca3772fb1537ed4bb2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1882719b30b01b50145fbca3772fb1537ed4bb2d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1882719b30b01b50145fbca3772fb1537ed4bb2d"}]},{"sha":"1882719b30b01b50145fbca3772fb1537ed4bb2d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDE4ODI3MTliMzBiMDFiNTAxNDVmYmNhMzc3MmZiMTUzN2VkNGJiMmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Owen Lin","email":"owenlin0@gmail.com","date":"2026-06-23T20:57:08Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T20:57:08Z"},"message":"feat(app-server): thread/turns/items/list -> thread/items/list (#29705)\n\n## Description\n\nRename the experimental app-server item pagination API from\n`thread/turns/items/list` to `thread/items/list` and make `turnId`\noptional. Clients can now page persisted items across a thread, or still\nfilter to one turn when needed.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Rename the request/response protocol types and JSON-RPC method to\n`ThreadItemsList*` / `thread/items/list`.\n- Pass optional `turnId` through to `ThreadStore::list_items`.\n- Update app-server docs and focused protocol/app-server tests.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol thread_items_list_round_trips`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server thread_items_list_returns_unsupported`","tree":{"sha":"696ba161db2bf2a9a9f4de349d2e3d96515f2978","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/696ba161db2bf2a9a9f4de349d2e3d96515f2978"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/1882719b30b01b50145fbca3772fb1537ed4bb2d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOvMkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9VAQADGNeErZ4eGzYloX0iMtRIv+\nBWciAuZ0UhvXPDkJ1mxq+MaxIW4+mZvJzXPnd5QrXiQUzkrmXfkdqOSFeE2ilOzI\nyXdWwUt+57/Fl5vLGiNVoOdIj7sheUDp/LJNty33+Gt8fVmm/km176CjNcke8KsP\nlpD/k5QxuDuHzhlHAk2x+V8hjsfXZxL/aO1eeCsXkHlcsoloZ/t9KTpsTv69bjst\n21BZwUJLJ5djBMcYLwmjZROM15/vCMO1iKK6ZpZCrRPq41dwAei3Vleen/tMBuVj\nPeA7E80stK+KxStK0YyyoBquWgbngICed9Jr8Pm3R9uu5SgB0ua8EQwcVIQpQEdL\nemrGTXkJlVW7U1YeSiX5WZjYZ3NS2wK55CbhHuXJFZyQdsCR9aQDgFPYWWOEMOKT\ntmVf+LPu0wEDlTCxdyq2+3OFSr/XSfiqyzCaP4JtZhfqH8SzpwCuOFz9DidzDECL\n+KSaMKfyRi+aID4maws6vJor5TLqrDlkZeF22vw1wQ2sF6yP+gk9KbtW8TFHtrfl\noStwO2z3FghMXys92b/X77nVEVRsg9LkRYwfGYtAX4hpwAKpNFKarl6xBkgx2Z9D\nf/DhX/pAuWxwktwJxtV0fwYIxMxPv05Y9c1L0o01h5QVas7QNWjJAjZIGGDPmjOg\n4ZgdEoeF4Ccg26E9sEoE\n=N53q\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 696ba161db2bf2a9a9f4de349d2e3d96515f2978\nparent 66f0220c56803874b4ac905cf0aaae61d6af6513\nauthor Owen Lin <owenlin0@gmail.com> 1782248228 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782248228 -0700\n\nfeat(app-server): thread/turns/items/list -> thread/items/list (#29705)\n\n## Description\n\nRename the experimental app-server item pagination API from\n`thread/turns/items/list` to `thread/items/list` and make `turnId`\noptional. Clients can now page persisted items across a thread, or still\nfilter to one turn when needed.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Rename the request/response protocol types and JSON-RPC method to\n`ThreadItemsList*` / `thread/items/list`.\n- Pass optional `turnId` through to `ThreadStore::list_items`.\n- Update app-server docs and focused protocol/app-server tests.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-protocol thread_items_list_round_trips`\n- `just test -p codex-app-server thread_items_list_returns_unsupported`","verified_at":"2026-06-23T20:57:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1882719b30b01b50145fbca3772fb1537ed4bb2d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/1882719b30b01b50145fbca3772fb1537ed4bb2d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/1882719b30b01b50145fbca3772fb1537ed4bb2d/comments","author":{"login":"owenlin0","id":947871,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0Nzg3MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/947871?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0","html_url":"https://github.com/owenlin0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/owenlin0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"66f0220c56803874b4ac905cf0aaae61d6af6513","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/66f0220c56803874b4ac905cf0aaae61d6af6513","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/66f0220c56803874b4ac905cf0aaae61d6af6513"}]},{"sha":"66f0220c56803874b4ac905cf0aaae61d6af6513","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY2ZjAyMjBjNTY4MDM4NzRiNGFjOTA1Y2YwYWFhZTYxZDZhZjY1MTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Rasmus Rygaard","email":"rasmus@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T20:39:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T20:39:13Z"},"message":"[codex] Report the exec-server working directory (#29666)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add the exec-server working directory to `environment/info` as an\noptional `PathUri`\n- populate it from the executor process's current directory\n- preserve compatibility with older responses that omit `cwd`\n\n## Why\n\nRemote clients currently have no executor-native default working\ndirectory. This forces callers such as app-server-backend to assume\n`/workspace`, which fails for laptop environments. Reporting the cwd\nalongside the detected shell lets clients use the path convention and\nlocation of the actual executor.\n\n## Impact\n\nThis is backward-compatible: the new response field is optional, and\nclients can continue handling responses from older exec servers. A\nfollow-up app-server-backend change will consume the value for cwd-less\n`command/exec` requests.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server` (275 passed, 2 skipped)","tree":{"sha":"74bf8f0edf5948ce2a74e3feefe28deb2280a3c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/74bf8f0edf5948ce2a74e3feefe28deb2280a3c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/66f0220c56803874b4ac905cf0aaae61d6af6513","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOu7xCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjmcQACWentfeYXi9dSysX09V/MMd\nqDQPNV1kxDBQLlkzNDY6YiNVP9K/w+gdfCbXEzNOt9Qu1RgdAx7RLrKYzEqfkhWi\n0qF5hhIKOzcLA7HusrndgAZSuEjvQtfF2xLEZA4T72MLJT8DH0V5tXEtQyORYtt2\nIEKhvVconWUQjeouzgJBvrvSwp8P2zM1E+VCRKICqcMpHYIiNT4haQyEgM/QV28C\nkNtunI4MuGFwhWplfsLuLeXDrcBBvbZI7GxCZLpaTKa5hzAUHuugd6bap78/vSIT\nn8VTvcygqYGL1QAXCd7LcdxhkZT9op5kRiWiyLWUvVf0ejkDT6LDIe/ZQa+sAoNO\nnce54vr55+oVu+15/Vr7q2rTnMOHRtZSE54deYxrLn6zHqyGAWiWgHQU9JjJxNR+\nJtV9sKOnsrvy6GFhi7TUONPG5NjmfWuTM+RzVCISgRpsNuBoRm9aCL+8DsB8YRyY\nYYexPylmYp+JNT3PfYhxTbZdRyMvvl3DVTu29BvzJN3yNU8sBPniNeRfyQPxrmHk\neC0Z68TRe6BORIPC/UVwG9t5ksuic9tkfJxf/HKLLfR8xmM4eqJ+mxMfgpmNU5O9\n5T6DQy586Xo669Tfpl4ykzYw/JXmZeINfPXlGcM4XHZnsbvb3cVSERnqx2MhD0g/\nQmUG5BE1iGTaj0LZPvu5\n=5y1T\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 74bf8f0edf5948ce2a74e3feefe28deb2280a3c2\nparent f6500886b732ac5e9d90988f9d02ca4b24bf5036\nauthor Rasmus Rygaard <rasmus@openai.com> 1782247153 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782247153 -0700\n\n[codex] Report the exec-server working directory (#29666)\n\n## Summary\n\n- add the exec-server working directory to `environment/info` as an\noptional `PathUri`\n- populate it from the executor process's current directory\n- preserve compatibility with older responses that omit `cwd`\n\n## Why\n\nRemote clients currently have no executor-native default working\ndirectory. This forces callers such as app-server-backend to assume\n`/workspace`, which fails for laptop environments. Reporting the cwd\nalongside the detected shell lets clients use the path convention and\nlocation of the actual executor.\n\n## Impact\n\nThis is backward-compatible: the new response field is optional, and\nclients can continue handling responses from older exec servers. A\nfollow-up app-server-backend change will consume the value for cwd-less\n`command/exec` requests.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server` (275 passed, 2 skipped)","verified_at":"2026-06-23T20:39:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/66f0220c56803874b4ac905cf0aaae61d6af6513","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/66f0220c56803874b4ac905cf0aaae61d6af6513","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/66f0220c56803874b4ac905cf0aaae61d6af6513/comments","author":{"login":"rasmusrygaard","id":949859,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk0OTg1OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/949859?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rasmusrygaard","html_url":"https://github.com/rasmusrygaard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rasmusrygaard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rasmusrygaard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rasmusrygaard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rasmusrygaard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rasmusrygaard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rasmusrygaard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rasmusrygaard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rasmusrygaard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rasmusrygaard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f6500886b732ac5e9d90988f9d02ca4b24bf5036","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f6500886b732ac5e9d90988f9d02ca4b24bf5036","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f6500886b732ac5e9d90988f9d02ca4b24bf5036"}]},{"sha":"f6500886b732ac5e9d90988f9d02ca4b24bf5036","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGY2NTAwODg2YjczMmFjNWU5ZDkwOTg4ZjlkMDJjYTRiMjRiZjUwMzY","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T20:33:59Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T20:33:59Z"},"message":"Decouple plugin manifest path resolution (#29620)\n\n## Why\n\nPlugin manifests use the same schema whether the package lives on the\nhost or in an executor. Only the path representation differs: host\ncallers need native `Path` inputs and `AbsolutePathBuf` outputs, while\nexecutor callers need `PathUri` throughout.\n\nMaintaining separate parsing or resolver implementations would duplicate\nthe manifest rules and allow them to drift. This PR instead makes\nURI-native resolution the single parsing path and keeps host conversion\nat the boundary.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Make `parse_plugin_manifest_uri` the shared manifest parser and\nresolve every path-bearing field as `PathUri`.\n- Keep the existing host entrypoint as a thin adapter: convert its\nnative root and manifest path to `PathUri`, run the shared parser, then\nmap resources back to `AbsolutePathBuf`.\n- Expose `PluginManifest::try_map_resources` so callers can convert the\ngeneric resource type without duplicating manifest construction.\n- Resolve relative manifest paths using the root URI's convention:\nbackslashes are separators for Windows roots and ordinary filename\ncharacters for POSIX roots.\n- Apply lexical containment after URI resolution, rejecting absolute\npaths and parent traversal outside the plugin root.\n- Make encoded backslashes fail containment only for Windows URIs;\nencoded `/` remains unsafe for every convention.\n- Use a host-native synthetic root for marketplace fallback manifests so\nthe host adapter also works on Windows.\n\n```text\nhost Path --------> PathUri --\\\n                              +--> one manifest parser --> PluginManifest<PathUri>\nexecutor PathUri -------------/\n\nhost result: PluginManifest<PathUri> --> PluginManifest<AbsolutePathBuf>\n```\n\nExisting host manifest behavior is preserved; #28918 is the first\nexecutor consumer.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-utils-path-uri`\n- `just test -p codex-plugin`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #29614 — add lexical `PathUri` containment.\n2. **This PR** — share URI-native manifest path resolution.\n3. #28918 — keep selected plugin roots and resources URI-native.\n4. #29626 — load executor skills without host path conversion.\n5. #29628 — resolve executor MCP working directories without host path\nconversion.","tree":{"sha":"ccfc5de974b03c68f6d7d0d7ea395e265a4d0ce8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ccfc5de974b03c68f6d7d0d7ea395e265a4d0ce8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f6500886b732ac5e9d90988f9d02ca4b24bf5036","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOu23CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATPgQAHbuxpL6tMs+uB8cvcy1ryH3\nzn/UWb6dR4H/bm2a5W3Fh13D6M18cJOPthQgJYxxU7I+p8GMkYERMpAdWTSklqU5\nGJ8tm70CBNWpdoOYComSYYikSiiEiOho91bKh3pwhkauso16Hred42bLX/C0IMCx\nnpduokx+fUHpJbYuAxMK3ycVugG0c02zVarNbc4blQPUCMY7Q9TtGGL3wXaGsBvg\nZP7FUPLOuDBi6ATRp7USdKL8wGydZV3uv++CAVyf2D4KuSp+YBtSAQSjn6Bq5Ml3\n0MFn8oza/15MJz9SF7ltNz78drozLjK4KedZkT4vlqiA48PjixcC74N5yajF32Mg\nJ5ZnwCMiP91p7Gu6kL6/7klZJcCOw9J5W8pizZ466uezt4MrP8xkqgILSaKaRxm6\nVAUtOLaYwuJcrYuaMBUFamXddmfkdsBb6wYkSfL0FTTn2mtcVjbaxhkI5CbIykH3\nbMO9XRiexeB+ppznWGlow3K0sSRAwcy1nU39L5UIjUgu2CLGgkTs9KbEILjkM88d\nEGiJ72Cl+PnkaLb7nYfg4VGyYRtzj1WDn2lt9Nl3hKo7Fi/Jb2RHiZW2PXKRpi3l\nVZ5v1+1H8XYXn2euplvglCXnc+KiTBKiHaSjV1lBGlO0gcRd2uMsxolTuqtQZpOA\nppCTp6ocyf83QZqNVe3L\n=4QBl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ccfc5de974b03c68f6d7d0d7ea395e265a4d0ce8\nparent 50eee505a3bbd7a66a73360ae28ea4968f79dd36\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782246839 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782246839 +0000\n\nDecouple plugin manifest path resolution (#29620)\n\n## Why\n\nPlugin manifests use the same schema whether the package lives on the\nhost or in an executor. Only the path representation differs: host\ncallers need native `Path` inputs and `AbsolutePathBuf` outputs, while\nexecutor callers need `PathUri` throughout.\n\nMaintaining separate parsing or resolver implementations would duplicate\nthe manifest rules and allow them to drift. This PR instead makes\nURI-native resolution the single parsing path and keeps host conversion\nat the boundary.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Make `parse_plugin_manifest_uri` the shared manifest parser and\nresolve every path-bearing field as `PathUri`.\n- Keep the existing host entrypoint as a thin adapter: convert its\nnative root and manifest path to `PathUri`, run the shared parser, then\nmap resources back to `AbsolutePathBuf`.\n- Expose `PluginManifest::try_map_resources` so callers can convert the\ngeneric resource type without duplicating manifest construction.\n- Resolve relative manifest paths using the root URI's convention:\nbackslashes are separators for Windows roots and ordinary filename\ncharacters for POSIX roots.\n- Apply lexical containment after URI resolution, rejecting absolute\npaths and parent traversal outside the plugin root.\n- Make encoded backslashes fail containment only for Windows URIs;\nencoded `/` remains unsafe for every convention.\n- Use a host-native synthetic root for marketplace fallback manifests so\nthe host adapter also works on Windows.\n\n```text\nhost Path --------> PathUri --\\\n                              +--> one manifest parser --> PluginManifest<PathUri>\nexecutor PathUri -------------/\n\nhost result: PluginManifest<PathUri> --> PluginManifest<AbsolutePathBuf>\n```\n\nExisting host manifest behavior is preserved; #28918 is the first\nexecutor consumer.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `just test -p codex-utils-path-uri`\n- `just test -p codex-plugin`\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins`\n\n## Stack\n\n1. #29614 — add lexical `PathUri` containment.\n2. **This PR** — share URI-native manifest path resolution.\n3. #28918 — keep selected plugin roots and resources URI-native.\n4. #29626 — load executor skills without host path conversion.\n5. #29628 — resolve executor MCP working directories without host path\nconversion.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T20:34:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f6500886b732ac5e9d90988f9d02ca4b24bf5036","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f6500886b732ac5e9d90988f9d02ca4b24bf5036","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f6500886b732ac5e9d90988f9d02ca4b24bf5036/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"50eee505a3bbd7a66a73360ae28ea4968f79dd36","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/50eee505a3bbd7a66a73360ae28ea4968f79dd36","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/50eee505a3bbd7a66a73360ae28ea4968f79dd36"}]},{"sha":"50eee505a3bbd7a66a73360ae28ea4968f79dd36","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDUwZWVlNTA1YTNiYmQ3YTY2YTczMzYwYWUyOGVhNDk2OGY3OWRkMzY","commit":{"author":{"name":"viyatb-oai","email":"viyatb@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T20:33:44Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T20:33:44Z"},"message":"feat(guardian): include connected account email in app reviews (#27045)\n\n## Why\n\nauto review reviews Codex App tool calls using connector metadata such\nas the app ID, name, and description. That metadata does not identify\nthe account behind the OAuth connection.\n\nFor Google Drive, this means auto review cannot distinguish a Drive\nconnection authenticated as `user@email.com` from a personal Drive\naccount. Uploading work data can therefore look like a transfer to a\npersonal destination even though the connector service already knows the\nauthenticated account email.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Read `_meta._codex_apps.connected_account_email` while resolving\napproval metadata for built-in Codex App tools.\n- Include the connected account email in the structured MCP tool action\nsent to auto review.\n- Trim empty values and omit the field when the connector link has no\naccount email.\n- Update existing auto review request constructors and add coverage for\nrequest construction and JSON serialization.\n\n## Security\n\nOnly metadata from the trusted built-in `codex_apps` MCP server is\naccepted. Custom MCP servers cannot inject a connected account email\ninto auto review reviews; the new regression test verifies that spoofed\nmetadata is ignored.\n\nThe email is used only in auto review's private review request. This\nchange does not add it to model-visible tool descriptions, app-server\napproval events, or auto review assessment/review analytics.","tree":{"sha":"62df041b27e15d95cbd00558efa9d62c44f81e0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/62df041b27e15d95cbd00558efa9d62c44f81e0f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/50eee505a3bbd7a66a73360ae28ea4968f79dd36","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOu2oCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5wEQAGcGJW9qDzHHSn/jxstHox40\nNGoWq1j56YAq35Nl+WGSKbIeIVnhfz6C3cmbIc3ib46az20EU9hC012r9fImlQ4P\n0fAWtdH08sYbNXw3d3pG5u/UNlldxYBMfTSHplwwb7YrnGf7KLbfEUVaukdKv79/\nGHmglwR2w+R2ayzXB74AZBbld2WSEx1Sm0vyNghl0fhsrVLVZ8GbNOn0i1CeYSC4\nkCTomJqjHMsFc6+BZWakX8pRMDQI1b+9mlOj490OTho9cpTSIu70HRTH+oYSRV1G\nLG9i8szrNUV7KSCFMDUF1eZD55fGT9LUwNMDE7leuTis5cD9zhXdaDlAbW7F/ytT\ntDROl+3ZpTTdYFtx401KZR/fyU1iMEowgD/aHdOTdGcFqfOtIh8yo5TCEXwHL2+2\ndw2WL9i7prHzeUnAfyeae+qcfTU+6uK/q+JlKw0JR51fCbX4pvvL+fOCvrlVQ6kx\n6tkW585naNI9qs+IpNuJRVoDNRhWvHPl984Das/wmVrJQWngOEsj3dFP5PYPMzC0\nJYsOz47KenDPx4DjUQlCdyiqDQ0HhjaZcFIFXKnFtGhilzrMuGD+YU3CHpBxV420\nfWtuRcocMjRgploFdlz6GwUfyzZM9gpPT1gcFe37zwKrsO8AXqKfEksslpAVFvJb\ngdJDuN9z7VmEV4GZw8/Y\n=Da/0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 62df041b27e15d95cbd00558efa9d62c44f81e0f\nparent cbcf1f8ca33ea6f683d11232ae485b32d23028c2\nauthor viyatb-oai <viyatb@openai.com> 1782246824 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782246824 +0000\n\nfeat(guardian): include connected account email in app reviews (#27045)\n\n## Why\n\nauto review reviews Codex App tool calls using connector metadata such\nas the app ID, name, and description. That metadata does not identify\nthe account behind the OAuth connection.\n\nFor Google Drive, this means auto review cannot distinguish a Drive\nconnection authenticated as `user@email.com` from a personal Drive\naccount. Uploading work data can therefore look like a transfer to a\npersonal destination even though the connector service already knows the\nauthenticated account email.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Read `_meta._codex_apps.connected_account_email` while resolving\napproval metadata for built-in Codex App tools.\n- Include the connected account email in the structured MCP tool action\nsent to auto review.\n- Trim empty values and omit the field when the connector link has no\naccount email.\n- Update existing auto review request constructors and add coverage for\nrequest construction and JSON serialization.\n\n## Security\n\nOnly metadata from the trusted built-in `codex_apps` MCP server is\naccepted. Custom MCP servers cannot inject a connected account email\ninto auto review reviews; the new regression test verifies that spoofed\nmetadata is ignored.\n\nThe email is used only in auto review's private review request. This\nchange does not add it to model-visible tool descriptions, app-server\napproval events, or auto review assessment/review analytics.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T20:33:45Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/50eee505a3bbd7a66a73360ae28ea4968f79dd36","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/50eee505a3bbd7a66a73360ae28ea4968f79dd36","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/50eee505a3bbd7a66a73360ae28ea4968f79dd36/comments","author":{"login":"viyatb-oai","id":234056686,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNr7g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234056686?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/viyatb-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viyatb-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cbcf1f8ca33ea6f683d11232ae485b32d23028c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cbcf1f8ca33ea6f683d11232ae485b32d23028c2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cbcf1f8ca33ea6f683d11232ae485b32d23028c2"}]},{"sha":"cbcf1f8ca33ea6f683d11232ae485b32d23028c2","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGNiY2YxZjhjYTMzZWE2ZjY4M2QxMTIzMmFlNDg1YjMyZDIzMDI4YzI","commit":{"author":{"name":"stevenlee-oai","email":"stevenlee@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T20:33:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T20:33:23Z"},"message":"Add MCP tool call error metrics (#28976)\n\n[Codex Thread\n019edc37-5345-7272-92c9-bf5494cf3819](https://codex-thread-link.openai.chatgpt-team.site/thread/019edc37-5345-7272-92c9-bf5494cf3819)\n\n## Summary\n\n- count MCP `CallToolResult.isError` responses as failed calls instead\nof successful transport-level calls\n- add `codex.mcp.call.error` with bounded `error_type` and trusted\nplugin-service `error_code` dimensions\n- record the same error classification on MCP tool-call spans while\nkeeping untrusted server error text out of metric labels\n\n## Scope\n\n- no changes to MCP routing, retries, tool behavior, configuration, or\npublic APIs\n- request failures remain grouped as `mcp_request`; separating\nconnection, timeout, protocol, and JSON-RPC failures requires preserving\ntyped errors through the existing flattened error boundary\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core 'mcp_tool_call::tests::'` (75 passed)\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core` (2,676 passed; 80 unrelated environment\nfailures from missing test binaries, sandbox signals, and read-only\npaths)","tree":{"sha":"719e9cb21dddade4dbf67c8148f4be3d782f091e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/719e9cb21dddade4dbf67c8148f4be3d782f091e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/cbcf1f8ca33ea6f683d11232ae485b32d23028c2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOu2TCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADkcQAAaLXL00OOlUFgSPoU+mvrVu\ncCA0/641kybdePCAeAWnaj0Bp3sJv9yC9aEdaN6tiuCrlp+2ctwjlpvd6VIXkjz4\nJtnwPi/byObbAGx3EdBqyUbUCpSfCwTqe6oz7irXYzig9zHgG/UOGAxqLB58YAA4\nbCeDQpABrEGnPZgAzHtEFez4qLoDOmaZ2q6hDRPlKWa9iW5dnVzE7WVpwngZNehe\nwGQAspaX1TEGkzB2Xmo2XG5rUPC4KnHf9PoiMCdTcLHoXRGaFlD9QOfDsYqpirlO\nTycv45gkWIEJd2f6Ww8a6fCgtozcNbApMU7sKojq9lEc8VWxiAD/BNL6xCOHi3wP\nx2HxgVH/rPtWyK9MAPtyv6e+R70dmUnJo2K6qVAz7TpbpIEFcXfI7pJY0ihvVQ7z\n+pZPrbY/Rk7st4NP406sSXmnqbsIqvRvQeZoiU+83U78LCrsKdO4WuLhGD73j6t4\nMVnfgHSEEDF1h0Ako2W5mOLO971/GGITvXwWkHXRJ18yurJ2EcERho+CZvD4Zg/j\npYqWdmNC2Hve/qPRRcGRyLvCm0DBxR8R81qPFn9kx0x/7H4dNEiwJaikrR/V1zuM\nLZey4OnV05aNYrJkBVFsOsH1AgdVkZdNPVElPBBm1fxh4kXxnGxtFthFogV9uQ1o\n3JHalCPnSg6p91P+Kvje\n=Z0Ae\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 719e9cb21dddade4dbf67c8148f4be3d782f091e\nparent 4cc6a4bab5c39021ff28d73ab2f1631721f1d847\nauthor stevenlee-oai <stevenlee@openai.com> 1782246803 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782246803 -0700\n\nAdd MCP tool call error metrics (#28976)\n\n[Codex Thread\n019edc37-5345-7272-92c9-bf5494cf3819](https://codex-thread-link.openai.chatgpt-team.site/thread/019edc37-5345-7272-92c9-bf5494cf3819)\n\n## Summary\n\n- count MCP `CallToolResult.isError` responses as failed calls instead\nof successful transport-level calls\n- add `codex.mcp.call.error` with bounded `error_type` and trusted\nplugin-service `error_code` dimensions\n- record the same error classification on MCP tool-call spans while\nkeeping untrusted server error text out of metric labels\n\n## Scope\n\n- no changes to MCP routing, retries, tool behavior, configuration, or\npublic APIs\n- request failures remain grouped as `mcp_request`; separating\nconnection, timeout, protocol, and JSON-RPC failures requires preserving\ntyped errors through the existing flattened error boundary\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core 'mcp_tool_call::tests::'` (75 passed)\n- `just fix -p codex-core`\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-core` (2,676 passed; 80 unrelated environment\nfailures from missing test binaries, sandbox signals, and read-only\npaths)","verified_at":"2026-06-23T20:33:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cbcf1f8ca33ea6f683d11232ae485b32d23028c2","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/cbcf1f8ca33ea6f683d11232ae485b32d23028c2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/cbcf1f8ca33ea6f683d11232ae485b32d23028c2/comments","author":{"login":"stevenlee-oai","id":213687449,"node_id":"U_kgDODLycmQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/213687449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/stevenlee-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenlee-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4cc6a4bab5c39021ff28d73ab2f1631721f1d847","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4cc6a4bab5c39021ff28d73ab2f1631721f1d847","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4cc6a4bab5c39021ff28d73ab2f1631721f1d847"}]},{"sha":"4cc6a4bab5c39021ff28d73ab2f1631721f1d847","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDRjYzZhNGJhYjVjMzkwMjFmZjI4ZDczYWIyZjE2MzE3MjFmMWQ4NDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T20:21:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T20:21:13Z"},"message":"core: use current step environments for tools (#29547)\n\n## Why\n\nWith deferred executors, an environment can become ready between two\nsampling requests in the same turn. The model-visible environment\nupdate, advertised tools, and eventual tool execution must all describe\nthe same request-time view.\n\nOtherwise, a request built while only environment B is ready can\nadvertise a tool without an `environment_id`; if higher-priority\nenvironment A becomes ready before execution, that call could silently\nrun in A instead.\n\nThis PR is stacked on #29527.\n\n## Design\n\n`run_turn` captures one `Arc<StepContext>` at each sampling-request\nboundary. That step owns the request's `TurnContext` and environment\nsnapshot.\n\n- World-state environment updates and tool planning borrow that same\nstep.\n- `ToolCallRuntime` retains the `Arc` while asynchronous tool calls\nexecute.\n- `ToolInvocation` carries the step to handlers; its temporary `turn`\ncompatibility field is derived from the same object.\n- `ToolRouter` does not retain `StepContext`; it only uses it while\nconstructing the request's tool set.\n- With `DeferredExecutor` disabled, step capture keeps using the\nenvironments frozen at turn start.\n\nSimply: every sampling request gets one consistent picture of its\nenvironments, from what the model sees through where its tool calls run.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Build environment-dependent tool specs from the current request's\n`StepContext`.\n- Use that same step for unified exec, legacy shell, `apply_patch`,\n`view_image`, and `request_permissions` execution.\n- Hide environment-backed tools, including `request_permissions`, while\nno environment is attached.\n- Resolve legacy shell paths and metadata from the selected step\nenvironment instead of the stale turn-start environment.\n- Capture explicit steps at non-turn-loop boundaries such as compaction,\nprompt debug, and startup prewarm.\n- Reconcile prompt-debug history from the same step used to build its\ntools.\n\n## Follow-up\n\n- Bind yielded code-mode cells to the tool runtime that created them, so\nnested calls made after yielding continue to use the originating\nrequest's `StepContext`.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\ndeferred_executor_updates_context_and_tools_after_startup`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nenvironment_count_controls_environment_backed_tools`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nbuild_prompt_input_includes_context_and_user_message`","tree":{"sha":"d9cbda44a7b32413aa3af1b26643d7c05c021a0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d9cbda44a7b32413aa3af1b26643d7c05c021a0c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/4cc6a4bab5c39021ff28d73ab2f1631721f1d847","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOuq5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAouUQAFqe9Ir7mOKxDsSWpVysBk+J\nk6c9Tfl/4/qlmPXgS0AAxmDrSfwsp04qFVm4q8eoFz5OVUmaLG5umg4CRjpNzVnC\n3CYmhgVY+Jq2WR5CYi84L9KHzoHsL1Jp0c72oV8NqvI6xpep1tSUtufT8uprNxiD\neqOAxJfSvLDAR+n6tU3AvrCsABL7bTL0aNeN6/wf8uV3ioUfUXYcqSoqdoicLIPf\nTsbLCiVgMLDmGQUvQ9p9m2oItCOQOUGcK5dBS5jqNNZ7r7+qdiI4cMW3bFARGSde\nN1TbTvRs0RxQeTIN4j+gr47atMd7nCDRjkkwF6E04ucyVrMJ0d6qobO4O86Cttdi\nVrEONlJD5mcAUDFTyLKNlpVnAga+Vn18jXEzeyNnMHe7aXWu/GmT9nz61ffBqz/4\nwfzWqjAJ34fscFA7aoMrenusK2GBKxm0nJv7VGx2ugczmVkfccmOIN1J+tNkUTIE\n5LVpL6gx4nEwyNCYnNvTMyQeQO/oAby8hbJdgn260/Uo2bhSFzn28KUmEhEr6bbK\nZ/cfXotLI4ByTBEqlx/tUO0LelGuKAjOb8/JfclzpUeenaFXQFeslLXV+pjQdxiw\nr206P0oBOXtzWxHjEYubCyRb86Bs1Ch74Vkw+EHT3Y0eI8COL1SJQhcCeFJs4qRZ\nkIx1ZCXpbo6sSFSIrR4R\n=s6tB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d9cbda44a7b32413aa3af1b26643d7c05c021a0c\nparent 7aab4b04bf80d8385b1e33e8b03e3da2100ed9fe\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1782246073 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782246073 +0000\n\ncore: use current step environments for tools (#29547)\n\n## Why\n\nWith deferred executors, an environment can become ready between two\nsampling requests in the same turn. The model-visible environment\nupdate, advertised tools, and eventual tool execution must all describe\nthe same request-time view.\n\nOtherwise, a request built while only environment B is ready can\nadvertise a tool without an `environment_id`; if higher-priority\nenvironment A becomes ready before execution, that call could silently\nrun in A instead.\n\nThis PR is stacked on #29527.\n\n## Design\n\n`run_turn` captures one `Arc<StepContext>` at each sampling-request\nboundary. That step owns the request's `TurnContext` and environment\nsnapshot.\n\n- World-state environment updates and tool planning borrow that same\nstep.\n- `ToolCallRuntime` retains the `Arc` while asynchronous tool calls\nexecute.\n- `ToolInvocation` carries the step to handlers; its temporary `turn`\ncompatibility field is derived from the same object.\n- `ToolRouter` does not retain `StepContext`; it only uses it while\nconstructing the request's tool set.\n- With `DeferredExecutor` disabled, step capture keeps using the\nenvironments frozen at turn start.\n\nSimply: every sampling request gets one consistent picture of its\nenvironments, from what the model sees through where its tool calls run.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Build environment-dependent tool specs from the current request's\n`StepContext`.\n- Use that same step for unified exec, legacy shell, `apply_patch`,\n`view_image`, and `request_permissions` execution.\n- Hide environment-backed tools, including `request_permissions`, while\nno environment is attached.\n- Resolve legacy shell paths and metadata from the selected step\nenvironment instead of the stale turn-start environment.\n- Capture explicit steps at non-turn-loop boundaries such as compaction,\nprompt debug, and startup prewarm.\n- Reconcile prompt-debug history from the same step used to build its\ntools.\n\n## Follow-up\n\n- Bind yielded code-mode cells to the tool runtime that created them, so\nnested calls made after yielding continue to use the originating\nrequest's `StepContext`.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\ndeferred_executor_updates_context_and_tools_after_startup`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nenvironment_count_controls_environment_backed_tools`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nbuild_prompt_input_includes_context_and_user_message`","verified_at":"2026-06-23T20:21:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4cc6a4bab5c39021ff28d73ab2f1631721f1d847","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/4cc6a4bab5c39021ff28d73ab2f1631721f1d847","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/4cc6a4bab5c39021ff28d73ab2f1631721f1d847/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7aab4b04bf80d8385b1e33e8b03e3da2100ed9fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7aab4b04bf80d8385b1e33e8b03e3da2100ed9fe","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7aab4b04bf80d8385b1e33e8b03e3da2100ed9fe"}]},{"sha":"7aab4b04bf80d8385b1e33e8b03e3da2100ed9fe","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDdhYWI0YjA0YmY4MGQ4Mzg1YjFlMzNlOGIwM2UzZGEyMTAwZWQ5ZmU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Boyang Niu","email":"boyang.niu@gmail.com","date":"2026-06-23T20:18:50Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T20:18:50Z"},"message":"[codex] Fix stale approval policy in MCP test (#29704)\n\n## Summary\n\n- replace the removed `AskForApproval::OnFailure` variant in the MCP\nshutdown test with `OnRequest`\n\n## Why\n\n`OnFailure` was removed from `AskForApproval`, but this test fixture\nstill referenced it, causing Rust and Clippy compilation failures.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-mcp shutdown_continues_after_caller_is_aborted`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"568eb675423665cfbbd798e99cf9c5b029d5248e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/568eb675423665cfbbd798e99cf9c5b029d5248e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/7aab4b04bf80d8385b1e33e8b03e3da2100ed9fe","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOuoqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIdkQALG+BcJsKbSQZQxxxpTXt3LG\nPfYFGSgUatByetcR11iaBQSuGMUeoWazBiQNl2DZWYOxjSVy3UskDESTqNQSgrHe\n1KxAMc7EZcgmvrza8K0LxEE3ScAIgv/0jNWxP6qGmNurP1TwWumhXeYR7x3CxU6X\n2866dBPEW2ut1HQCCHG5ywLfd5Zm3+c2xZuqtQSvdI5ouFJDEw0t/+NQlqaEJZ/T\nuUtORFcCm+7P85HSYAcCI+5CsjH3Rlv6U6twsi9QJgBvxe4JG34aiHEX/syjQOlS\nYeDspfuXdLOttW2FqgOnJhtFFs4Yekzcm1Id1Q32fYflImuIR1aqxiS7dhqelbOc\nn/ZY7yoSZahHVizOk9iIcUosVTWvpu4QfBwBNJB7+d8X78aQADulhap2GNxk95Ly\nojQaBrDfUKLgtsCdfa20ip3LGzcnfgvAMK/8tTTxAhmuseU9Ef17wGYuS1wHlEoK\n1afXKYAn7CWpgRnErJALeELzUsg+GChW521vBiSm4oYQVTK34zqIRH9V7hdYPHW2\n+FtbptuOnj7IYw5pmxJ6ZKgTtMaIyb+4HS953HtNpDYCQumypJAgzUufvR26BBoy\n16DML8dQuH9vuT5u4lr5m69HqpqYQX97jU1PlPZClLgF7gqKYYpBDdmkFIIbllUP\ndEBWLsGF0KKWdxtD3kTD\n=Ku/o\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 568eb675423665cfbbd798e99cf9c5b029d5248e\nparent 00dc5ea397713fa51851dad1a574b614dc75a97f\nauthor Boyang Niu <boyang.niu@gmail.com> 1782245930 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782245930 -0700\n\n[codex] Fix stale approval policy in MCP test (#29704)\n\n## Summary\n\n- replace the removed `AskForApproval::OnFailure` variant in the MCP\nshutdown test with `OnRequest`\n\n## Why\n\n`OnFailure` was removed from `AskForApproval`, but this test fixture\nstill referenced it, causing Rust and Clippy compilation failures.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-mcp shutdown_continues_after_caller_is_aborted`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-23T20:18:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7aab4b04bf80d8385b1e33e8b03e3da2100ed9fe","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7aab4b04bf80d8385b1e33e8b03e3da2100ed9fe","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7aab4b04bf80d8385b1e33e8b03e3da2100ed9fe/comments","author":{"login":"kumquatexpress","id":1317457,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTc0NTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1317457?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kumquatexpress","html_url":"https://github.com/kumquatexpress","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kumquatexpress/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kumquatexpress/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kumquatexpress/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kumquatexpress/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kumquatexpress/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kumquatexpress/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kumquatexpress/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kumquatexpress/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kumquatexpress/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"00dc5ea397713fa51851dad1a574b614dc75a97f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/00dc5ea397713fa51851dad1a574b614dc75a97f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/00dc5ea397713fa51851dad1a574b614dc75a97f"}]},{"sha":"00dc5ea397713fa51851dad1a574b614dc75a97f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDAwZGM1ZWEzOTc3MTNmYTUxODUxZGFkMWE1NzRiNjE0ZGM3NWE5N2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T19:56:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T19:56:20Z"},"message":"[codex] Fix stale approval policy in MCP test (#29696)\n\n## Summary\n\n- replace the stale `AskForApproval::OnFailure` reference in the MCP\nconnection manager test with `AskForApproval::OnRequest`\n- restore `codex-mcp` test compilation after `OnFailure` was removed in\n#28418\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe test was added on main after the approval-policy removal branch had\nalready updated the other references, so the newly added call site was\nmissed when #28418 merged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-mcp` (90 passed)\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"568eb675423665cfbbd798e99cf9c5b029d5248e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/568eb675423665cfbbd798e99cf9c5b029d5248e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/00dc5ea397713fa51851dad1a574b614dc75a97f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOuTkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlnIQAIURKCtdO+Icu++HPJmjgwFF\nWhgJQEEQ73mqIZd7ref87yfOAPwwH6qCPoCo11LoJOISYdoiVTFFUbSQ9yuPZwJu\npDEzvLVkaZS3MPx46z5ktKw2wLv1mT9JT2rtg8OP61vKJj7ZcWqPKKcGiStNi0Q/\nKvgEMvmtnwEWpdyFHmrjDdVph4tbBYYXFUM852YfysunKWFuyob8oB+dKPuKAHD3\n3JNKYZOhEpQpBniENOzWnkyXeRe02rczeLuIA8q2o3QOd/Q4BPDQ+OIyM8ZMPqRs\no/5MuprQ6pNf6N9QJw/rBm4RBTJo74hTydilEYziooYMDY9jzNl8v4KyAHkiGZCa\nv+MCB0Lu4+BTsGv5xlvvrTwe3YNa8KLO8MqVKr2BVXxga6dj57SrAAxvAQhWrz36\nZTegBefvuPtzIb1OV7pdtLfl1f4Vg/wrLplnG8CIbjQmY9q7463MHgkUyNU37PbY\nbsr8zr+z3yqK4A/YPaClzBdztFix3YYYBNMu7vOpLTEn6ZU4DmpnoETPZc6SiBEc\nIXYN7CU0pmnmTz6twWdprng5v4s2n068HmKs+5znoGbf1uMMzMsDsd/UpnRTYccG\nB2EjPTIOrCWSM5vWGARvQkqufF+xKCOd9S35T4VnFOHqLD+1XqTjlC/kk1b89mVt\nvBVUXwcCPOQpuDaTAB7V\n=R3br\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 568eb675423665cfbbd798e99cf9c5b029d5248e\nparent 510bce992701635f725391ad8f630cdcbf0a48f5\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1782244580 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782244580 +0000\n\n[codex] Fix stale approval policy in MCP test (#29696)\n\n## Summary\n\n- replace the stale `AskForApproval::OnFailure` reference in the MCP\nconnection manager test with `AskForApproval::OnRequest`\n- restore `codex-mcp` test compilation after `OnFailure` was removed in\n#28418\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe test was added on main after the approval-policy removal branch had\nalready updated the other references, so the newly added call site was\nmissed when #28418 merged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-mcp` (90 passed)\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-23T19:56:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/00dc5ea397713fa51851dad1a574b614dc75a97f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/00dc5ea397713fa51851dad1a574b614dc75a97f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/00dc5ea397713fa51851dad1a574b614dc75a97f/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"510bce992701635f725391ad8f630cdcbf0a48f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/510bce992701635f725391ad8f630cdcbf0a48f5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/510bce992701635f725391ad8f630cdcbf0a48f5"}]},{"sha":"510bce992701635f725391ad8f630cdcbf0a48f5","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDUxMGJjZTk5MjcwMTYzNWY3MjUzOTFhZDhmNjMwY2RjYmYwYTQ4ZjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T19:52:37Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T19:52:37Z"},"message":"core: resolve view_image paths in selected environment (#29526)\n\n## Why\n\nview_image needs to support foreign OS remote executors.\n\n## What\n\n- resolve image paths against the selected environment as `PathUri` and\nread them through that environment's filesystem\n- keep app-server's public path field wire-compatible as\n`LegacyAppPathString`, with purpose-specific UI rendering\n- cover relative and absolute target-native paths in the core\nintegration test and run the full `view_image` suite under wine-exec\nwithout skips","tree":{"sha":"59b068caa723f0ac2869341347b89201045712c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/59b068caa723f0ac2869341347b89201045712c2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/510bce992701635f725391ad8f630cdcbf0a48f5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOuQFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA3LYQAFMh2gixBB5IKek5iOBJiHtA\nlnCyJV9AJW7mi80ITaNmBfD17uRRRz+4Pfk2RiJGHovsNd1Fs44ZeDH9ZdsKC/yU\nK6wu7r117DMM2cnGdkZ1A5tn9mN7XmR5XCTXDJbcvexQ1W66YdqoFCfldiWTq3DA\ndvFq747WNIPy48DBDZjhGtpv9pa2YdecL6NFynD+FcSqKvwsQJFi/9aHszCbknFE\nSGyheygomlzdaUfXQtBzAm2rMeD2ajGnog1srtpAQt4y8yjfWCKxz55FGES2ngrq\nj+CF6yZDt8P5K9JV0PzBSKCSx4Rrus77noyjKqnTcjJV/elgZhobEN2U5wDjpLjw\nkz2Vg0zqW8HipHLAFhGWn3vUh8eFSk2TWYvHUuPR9HvyufSislra6z50G2NnEMwG\nhvESnf5jTf8KaDQ2d/uIC32JYXDIEyXknruwyVerCTnJ/dN/HvHprGfr/waMmOgx\n0ERXBFmHPl71+h2lIah+xb1610WhXgTkhvZZF1NgELYzRjvp/4IXdbrFC1M+A52o\nW51REFPaCMi3Sj0yhF+OosaddOt2SQxoUKuwBllu5Kl2YWhhbeVfWSI/pdN7dame\n284yqIh7lUTpe1IY1zsi6OZtAjd88EP0McKnLM0RP2a6Ssck1yPhMcDfnvRS59Fv\naPrSYZD3EI0LUahatxx2\n=dyOw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 59b068caa723f0ac2869341347b89201045712c2\nparent c660e2b644a5ca75d9fde9947895679906d29c4d\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1782244357 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782244357 +0000\n\ncore: resolve view_image paths in selected environment (#29526)\n\n## Why\n\nview_image needs to support foreign OS remote executors.\n\n## What\n\n- resolve image paths against the selected environment as `PathUri` and\nread them through that environment's filesystem\n- keep app-server's public path field wire-compatible as\n`LegacyAppPathString`, with purpose-specific UI rendering\n- cover relative and absolute target-native paths in the core\nintegration test and run the full `view_image` suite under wine-exec\nwithout skips","verified_at":"2026-06-23T19:52:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/510bce992701635f725391ad8f630cdcbf0a48f5","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/510bce992701635f725391ad8f630cdcbf0a48f5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/510bce992701635f725391ad8f630cdcbf0a48f5/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c660e2b644a5ca75d9fde9947895679906d29c4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c660e2b644a5ca75d9fde9947895679906d29c4d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c660e2b644a5ca75d9fde9947895679906d29c4d"}]},{"sha":"c660e2b644a5ca75d9fde9947895679906d29c4d","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGM2NjBlMmI2NDRhNWNhNzVkOWZkZTk5NDc4OTU2Nzk5MDZkMjljNGQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"richardopenai","email":"richardlee@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T19:40:54Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T19:40:54Z"},"message":"[codex] allow image generation with provider auth (#29513)\n\n## Summary\n\n- allow the native Responses API `image_generation` tool when the active\nprovider carries CCA's non-empty `x-openai-actor-authorization` header\n- preserve the Codex-managed ChatGPT auth path, scoped to providers that\nactually require OpenAI auth\n- keep generic custom providers excluded, including when unrelated\nChatGPT credentials are cached\n- retain the existing feature, provider-capability, and\nimage-input-modality gates\n\n## Why\n\nCCA authenticates its inference requests through the active provider's\n`x-openai-actor-authorization` and `ChatGPT-Account-ID` headers, so it\ndoes not have a Codex-managed login session. The previous gate therefore\nhid the native hosted image-generation tool despite an authenticated\ncodex-backend path.\n\nThis change is intentionally limited to the native hosted tool. It adds\nno extension, MCP, plugin-service, session-source, token plumbing, or\nnew provider configuration surface.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-core\nhosted_tools_follow_provider_auth_model_and_config_gates`\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`\n- `git diff --check origin/main`","tree":{"sha":"3bd7367b48aba3d030ec5b27253d343c94f77f2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3bd7367b48aba3d030ec5b27253d343c94f77f2f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c660e2b644a5ca75d9fde9947895679906d29c4d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOuFGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAO+4QAH+YwCfph2VAmwlIgYuJtDAL\nAL8owljGBjp1rQsNgBFY73tu3IyAbMvDA9ikSzudeLeYJkyLYhm8oDNn4H9pWU3A\npKNVZYx2UnoBKwcyCuWjqDvMF3oLxYiMCYMLqMv4SQcyqtNFGuNE4vmEidJMCv3j\nQuX+FX/HrqXzpGng0kfCb6pQDFX7TjzW0etpTYvWHF/9elrcCKrshuiJc1WwPEfd\nqo7QhF7astFYIFPADAUGmw+i29JDLu8Da9EXMAkC5RLW4b2X5qPT04iPdRvLj0aM\neb/2bCn3qQfWYMqWmwamHnBop//6bJuiDTbkNsXynTAiGpFgBNjvu/dFKleF7Huq\n45C1NHsOsmJs6uz4cpNUU2fW7JxQJYH7u2AOyHBRblio4CKA4AfHm2CF95pxiBae\nOVRUsdgtgjfdwoOXyzXxa60hY2cdXAVIuWHpH0zVbkcdctzyzNgvNCco0AtAfxAs\nFrmCdk9wRmfeNH9FTVD4c1rbDKHlpSvLuAW1E5LddWq5wLGlG4IaVWwHm6ACPDnk\nXqd0SrtlcCvh/+YaawH4W9XiEZfgpH5UvH1hys1lIHpNVoBadk9JJKQ0sKH8ZMwc\nDkkul4b1FiOiDA7a0NEvMdCdK3Wl2yCh3SAH3X9vSgzmFodstR8rOQb8Hl9BKX8U\nQbtxsGErxnvLrgWqY1pp\n=kq4A\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3bd7367b48aba3d030ec5b27253d343c94f77f2f\nparent 18fe1d9fe3fd7b58c8d36763660e915d3b84dd53\nauthor richardopenai <richardlee@openai.com> 1782243654 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782243654 -0700\n\n[codex] allow image generation with provider auth (#29513)\n\n## Summary\n\n- allow the native Responses API `image_generation` tool when the active\nprovider carries CCA's non-empty `x-openai-actor-authorization` header\n- preserve the Codex-managed ChatGPT auth path, scoped to providers that\nactually require OpenAI auth\n- keep generic custom providers excluded, including when unrelated\nChatGPT credentials are cached\n- retain the existing feature, provider-capability, and\nimage-input-modality gates\n\n## Why\n\nCCA authenticates its inference requests through the active provider's\n`x-openai-actor-authorization` and `ChatGPT-Account-ID` headers, so it\ndoes not have a Codex-managed login session. The previous gate therefore\nhid the native hosted image-generation tool despite an authenticated\ncodex-backend path.\n\nThis change is intentionally limited to the native hosted tool. It adds\nno extension, MCP, plugin-service, session-source, token plumbing, or\nnew provider configuration surface.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `cargo test -p codex-core\nhosted_tools_follow_provider_auth_model_and_config_gates`\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`\n- `git diff --check origin/main`","verified_at":"2026-06-23T19:40:54Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c660e2b644a5ca75d9fde9947895679906d29c4d","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c660e2b644a5ca75d9fde9947895679906d29c4d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c660e2b644a5ca75d9fde9947895679906d29c4d/comments","author":{"login":"richardopenai","id":272641442,"node_id":"U_kgDOEEAtog","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/272641442?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai","html_url":"https://github.com/richardopenai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardopenai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"18fe1d9fe3fd7b58c8d36763660e915d3b84dd53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/18fe1d9fe3fd7b58c8d36763660e915d3b84dd53","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/18fe1d9fe3fd7b58c8d36763660e915d3b84dd53"}]},{"sha":"18fe1d9fe3fd7b58c8d36763660e915d3b84dd53","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDE4ZmUxZDlmZTNmZDdiNThjOGQzNjc2MzY2MGU5MTVkM2I4NGRkNTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"iceweasel-oai","email":"iceweasel@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T19:29:46Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T19:29:46Z"},"message":"[codex] Preserve proxy state for filesystem sandbox helpers (#29671)\n\n## Why\n\nFilesystem helpers intentionally run with a minimal environment that\nexcludes proxy variables. After filesystem operations started using the\nWindows sandbox wrapper, the wrapper derived an empty proxy\nconfiguration from that helper environment and compared it with the\npersistent sandbox setup marker. When the marker contained proxy ports,\nevery filesystem operation appeared to require a firewall update, which\ncould launch elevated setup, show a UAC or loader dialog, and fail\noperations such as `apply_patch` with error 1223.\n\nFilesystem helpers do not use network access, so they should preserve\nthe proxy/firewall state established by normal sandboxed process\nlaunches.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add an explicit Windows sandbox proxy-settings mode for reconciling or\npreserving persistent proxy state.\n- Use preserve mode for filesystem helpers while normal process launches\ncontinue to reconcile proxy settings from their environment.\n- Carry the selected proxy state consistently through setup validation,\nelevated setup, and non-elevated ACL refreshes.\n- Cover wrapper argument propagation and marker-derived proxy\npreservation.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo build -p codex-cli --bin codex`\n- `just test -p codex-windows-sandbox\npreserving_proxy_settings_uses_the_existing_marker`\n- `just test -p codex-windows-sandbox windows_wrapper_args_round_trip`\n- `just test -p codex-windows-sandbox\nsetup_request_prefers_explicit_proxy_settings`\n- `just test -p codex-sandboxing transform_for_direct_spawn_windows`\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server fs_sandbox::tests`\n- Ran the same sandboxed `fs/writeFile` reproduction against published\n`0.142.0-alpha.6` and the new CLI. The published CLI launched elevated\nsetup and failed with `ShellExecuteExW ... 1223`; the new CLI completed\nwithout elevation.\n\nRelated to #28359.","tree":{"sha":"f6b6ccc6c001cd3bbcb7df1354d53496892cb5b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/f6b6ccc6c001cd3bbcb7df1354d53496892cb5b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/18fe1d9fe3fd7b58c8d36763660e915d3b84dd53","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOt6qCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKMQQACci5EKeUSTyAw4Hw5tgrVO0\nL9jepDRnLFHjDcpA2ilpQpweYM0si/hWZftqj9d7Dw5mItaHXY0vnZhX5yTRMyIv\ni5LSsPkTTU3C1w70lK6/EETZHeqVAVhjmsIWJ6+38WzcliCPC9P+6MX2HveLH6Dn\nQaPl9e9+0Anz4+ZVlj3nog5GIFHGfGmwSU3LZI3KTV8H1W8DVn0UesP8c8cPk4TB\n2CnIQHImnfEDe2u/ElLBl9j57PwaNwM+bX3JQX1doEgLO3BMUbI9g4aEY5k8VODJ\nDQp86pygmjE97CGXILxMBD0erXqII5jsr4zKNHILNl/4aDQxzX5mYRDx47FTDaot\nqKjIvg6FGpONu6BHfoayU66m2AwxpV+SrRHCfIYGV4O1pq/HeNaXgwPc1WuQ+/mh\ne9QjgrIsH2tlvlpBfvboz7mBhUY+XF4Qc7u4+xhg2u5M4SqIg305Dgfj2gXXMmo0\nitTdH8fzfQpeyCd+rM7WyqWPoaB145jlidH5HCEQ870jns3vPA5Ygo4kdWGO7bZ5\nRbZUPTPnP/XsKjIaps5zsxQWotnOOl1htxp5r4TnjZP63Xb5bw7QLvgSjniOfm7s\nYoFidw9tjpPyLHbDJONOJs5OsdZnLXMfXCgdD/S5dweS/U0VuIV3lJVYi2X1dh7M\nlhT9UslpdQWK+aKFzKiB\n=Z9Gv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f6b6ccc6c001cd3bbcb7df1354d53496892cb5b1\nparent ff50b47dceb151cb08d8ad46e0e35bce8e7abcde\nauthor iceweasel-oai <iceweasel@openai.com> 1782242986 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782242986 -0700\n\n[codex] Preserve proxy state for filesystem sandbox helpers (#29671)\n\n## Why\n\nFilesystem helpers intentionally run with a minimal environment that\nexcludes proxy variables. After filesystem operations started using the\nWindows sandbox wrapper, the wrapper derived an empty proxy\nconfiguration from that helper environment and compared it with the\npersistent sandbox setup marker. When the marker contained proxy ports,\nevery filesystem operation appeared to require a firewall update, which\ncould launch elevated setup, show a UAC or loader dialog, and fail\noperations such as `apply_patch` with error 1223.\n\nFilesystem helpers do not use network access, so they should preserve\nthe proxy/firewall state established by normal sandboxed process\nlaunches.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add an explicit Windows sandbox proxy-settings mode for reconciling or\npreserving persistent proxy state.\n- Use preserve mode for filesystem helpers while normal process launches\ncontinue to reconcile proxy settings from their environment.\n- Carry the selected proxy state consistently through setup validation,\nelevated setup, and non-elevated ACL refreshes.\n- Cover wrapper argument propagation and marker-derived proxy\npreservation.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo build -p codex-cli --bin codex`\n- `just test -p codex-windows-sandbox\npreserving_proxy_settings_uses_the_existing_marker`\n- `just test -p codex-windows-sandbox windows_wrapper_args_round_trip`\n- `just test -p codex-windows-sandbox\nsetup_request_prefers_explicit_proxy_settings`\n- `just test -p codex-sandboxing transform_for_direct_spawn_windows`\n- `just test -p codex-exec-server fs_sandbox::tests`\n- Ran the same sandboxed `fs/writeFile` reproduction against published\n`0.142.0-alpha.6` and the new CLI. The published CLI launched elevated\nsetup and failed with `ShellExecuteExW ... 1223`; the new CLI completed\nwithout elevation.\n\nRelated to #28359.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T19:29:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/18fe1d9fe3fd7b58c8d36763660e915d3b84dd53","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/18fe1d9fe3fd7b58c8d36763660e915d3b84dd53","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/18fe1d9fe3fd7b58c8d36763660e915d3b84dd53/comments","author":{"login":"iceweasel-oai","id":234057055,"node_id":"U_kgDODfNtXw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/234057055?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/iceweasel-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/iceweasel-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ff50b47dceb151cb08d8ad46e0e35bce8e7abcde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ff50b47dceb151cb08d8ad46e0e35bce8e7abcde","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ff50b47dceb151cb08d8ad46e0e35bce8e7abcde"}]},{"sha":"ff50b47dceb151cb08d8ad46e0e35bce8e7abcde","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZmNTBiNDdkY2ViMTUxY2IwOGQ4YWQ0NmUwZTM1YmNlOGU3YWJjZGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"jameswt-oai","email":"jameswt@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T19:27:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T19:27:14Z"},"message":"Separate local and remote plugin analytics IDs (#29495)\n\n## Why\n\nPlugin analytics overloaded `plugin_id`: most events used the Codex\n`<plugin>@<marketplace>` identity, while remote install events used the\nbackend plugin ID. That makes the same field change meaning across event\ntypes and complicates downstream identity resolution.\n\nThis change makes the contract unambiguous:\n\n- `plugin_id`: the local Codex `<plugin>@<marketplace>` identity, when\nresolved\n- `remote_plugin_id`: the backend plugin identity, when available\n\nFor a remote install failure that happens before plugin details resolve,\n`plugin_id` is `null` and `remote_plugin_id` remains populated.\n\n## What changed\n\nAll six plugin analytics events use the same identity contract:\n\n- `codex_plugin_installed`\n- `codex_plugin_install_failed`\n- `codex_plugin_uninstalled`\n- `codex_plugin_enabled`\n- `codex_plugin_disabled`\n- `codex_plugin_used`\n\nRemote identity is resolved from the current installed-plugin snapshot\nfirst, with persisted install metadata as fallback. The telemetry\nmetadata type keeps local identity optional for failures that occur\nbefore remote details are available.\n\nThe app-server test client's manual analytics smokes now find remote\nmutation events through `remote_plugin_id` and validate that `plugin_id`\nremains local.\n\n## Remote uninstall\n\nResolve and capture telemetry metadata before removing the local plugin\ncache, then emit `codex_plugin_uninstalled` after the backend confirms\nsuccess. The event is also emitted when backend uninstall succeeds but\nlocal cache cleanup reports `CacheRemove`.\n\nIf a concurrent remote-cache refresh removes the local bundle before\ntelemetry capture, the already-fetched remote plugin detail supplies\nfallback capability metadata.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-analytics` — 82 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins` — 271 passed\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-test-client` — 5 passed\n- `just test -p codex-plugin` — 3 passed\n- `just test -p codex-app-server plugin_install` — 37 passed\n- `just test -p codex-app-server plugin_uninstall` — 10 passed\n\nThe production app-server install/uninstall flow was also exercised\nagainst `plugins~Plugin_f1b845ac33888191ac156169c58733c2`\n(`build-ios-apps@openai-curated-remote`), and the plugin's original\nuninstalled state was restored.","tree":{"sha":"8b3904fa3b0da0aa90311a7ea25a1ca56bcd6bd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8b3904fa3b0da0aa90311a7ea25a1ca56bcd6bd2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ff50b47dceb151cb08d8ad46e0e35bce8e7abcde","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOt4SCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGy4QAI5usjtho02Xk/LSEe2oM//c\nEpPtv3cbmbsw5spajxL3WAE7DiDPfvQIQvMb06Pd2XrQEyqP2/AAxLNtyMF87Ru9\nup5Njtg4jmGc4/PmYLsC4mMx17MlKf6blb+hZMyCeB1nMfwu8uZbd5VxlTgZJViM\nqcj/mQKpNvwUbSgJ5Engi0gve92c3wLzH26RBM+QzGHEuxKy7qzkYOJC5bEDsCDp\nk2xlI6Fs3gzFCI+ncIYakIKGVU+DqGpBu0LWjce+lLKRsRHLb9hdF5e1B4dwXLhx\nv4ERkb9koTx27TQb12RMBZFdlAq53jFUrqyVSI9UAKFMSkaYWcWFT15mbZIo4J4T\nL4Gx+V3kZuNDpY7d5yWYWO5e3li7V18ncCOvKomcAvajZ8XpCfMrfuz9qrQvPNi4\nzsCC/x4vQHfyjzg1AA/RiEHNJrcN8hH7fri2eFL20ALlU3HUjIrZY78CynFIX8Ja\nuXxJekE1sujyAHtE8Gs+/6a/RoZdKLO8V235LVSBB89mM+KfJF+jBI+4X016TJAU\nbiUzYwSi0IkETwNYkEqRtnoXNVWuc2P+9RjDfHgRPaMcds7/AukUYXeYgWNw1sRF\n4V0Szuoa65Tlc1DB5xVHlNhNaV3H+Q3xiv7b0WpOkNqlMHLxE+byupUIqxGYZqWZ\nNWGIM+pBp0hEvS9XOpfh\n=Jfxg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8b3904fa3b0da0aa90311a7ea25a1ca56bcd6bd2\nparent c5a9a95ab660d54869468ff3282d9d067e66a675\nauthor jameswt-oai <jameswt@openai.com> 1782242834 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782242834 -0700\n\nSeparate local and remote plugin analytics IDs (#29495)\n\n## Why\n\nPlugin analytics overloaded `plugin_id`: most events used the Codex\n`<plugin>@<marketplace>` identity, while remote install events used the\nbackend plugin ID. That makes the same field change meaning across event\ntypes and complicates downstream identity resolution.\n\nThis change makes the contract unambiguous:\n\n- `plugin_id`: the local Codex `<plugin>@<marketplace>` identity, when\nresolved\n- `remote_plugin_id`: the backend plugin identity, when available\n\nFor a remote install failure that happens before plugin details resolve,\n`plugin_id` is `null` and `remote_plugin_id` remains populated.\n\n## What changed\n\nAll six plugin analytics events use the same identity contract:\n\n- `codex_plugin_installed`\n- `codex_plugin_install_failed`\n- `codex_plugin_uninstalled`\n- `codex_plugin_enabled`\n- `codex_plugin_disabled`\n- `codex_plugin_used`\n\nRemote identity is resolved from the current installed-plugin snapshot\nfirst, with persisted install metadata as fallback. The telemetry\nmetadata type keeps local identity optional for failures that occur\nbefore remote details are available.\n\nThe app-server test client's manual analytics smokes now find remote\nmutation events through `remote_plugin_id` and validate that `plugin_id`\nremains local.\n\n## Remote uninstall\n\nResolve and capture telemetry metadata before removing the local plugin\ncache, then emit `codex_plugin_uninstalled` after the backend confirms\nsuccess. The event is also emitted when backend uninstall succeeds but\nlocal cache cleanup reports `CacheRemove`.\n\nIf a concurrent remote-cache refresh removes the local bundle before\ntelemetry capture, the already-fetched remote plugin detail supplies\nfallback capability metadata.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-analytics` — 82 passed\n- `just test -p codex-core-plugins` — 271 passed\n- `just test -p codex-app-server-test-client` — 5 passed\n- `just test -p codex-plugin` — 3 passed\n- `just test -p codex-app-server plugin_install` — 37 passed\n- `just test -p codex-app-server plugin_uninstall` — 10 passed\n\nThe production app-server install/uninstall flow was also exercised\nagainst `plugins~Plugin_f1b845ac33888191ac156169c58733c2`\n(`build-ios-apps@openai-curated-remote`), and the plugin's original\nuninstalled state was restored.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T19:27:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ff50b47dceb151cb08d8ad46e0e35bce8e7abcde","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ff50b47dceb151cb08d8ad46e0e35bce8e7abcde","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ff50b47dceb151cb08d8ad46e0e35bce8e7abcde/comments","author":{"login":"jameswt-oai","id":247462917,"node_id":"U_kgDODr_8BQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247462917?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jameswt-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jameswt-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c5a9a95ab660d54869468ff3282d9d067e66a675","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c5a9a95ab660d54869468ff3282d9d067e66a675","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c5a9a95ab660d54869468ff3282d9d067e66a675"}]},{"sha":"c5a9a95ab660d54869468ff3282d9d067e66a675","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGM1YTlhOTVhYjY2MGQ1NDg2OTQ2OGZmMzI4MmQ5ZDA2N2U2NmE2NzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Winston Howes","email":"winston@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T19:20:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T19:20:51Z"},"message":"Keep managed MITM CA private keys in proxy memory (#29013)\n\n## Why\n\nThe managed MITM trust bundle must be readable by sandboxed commands.\nPersisting its sibling CA private key under `$CODEX_HOME/proxy`\ntherefore requires a deny-read sandbox rule, but the Windows unelevated\nbackend rejects deny-read paths and WSL1's legacy Landlock path cannot\nenforce that rule.\n\nA persistent OS credential store also does not provide the same\ncross-platform boundary from other processes running as the same user.\nKeeping the signer inside the network proxy process avoids both\nproblems: ordinary sandbox setup stays independent of CA-key state, and\nno private signing key is exposed through the filesystem or a persistent\ncredential record.\n\n## What\n\n- generate one managed CA per proxy process and retain its private\nsigner only in proxy memory\n- emit only content-addressed public CA certificates and trust bundles\nunder `$CODEX_HOME/proxy`\n- hold a cross-process lease for each active public certificate and\nprune artifacts from inactive proxy processes\n- keep all CA ownership in `codex-network-proxy`; no `codex-core` or\nsandbox-policy changes\n- validate generated trust-bundle paths by their content hash\n- keep the public bundle readable by sandboxed commands on Windows,\nWSL1, macOS, and Linux\n\nThe independent startup custom-CA follow-up is #29014.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `CODEX_HOME=/private/tmp/codex-test-home-network-proxy just test -p\ncodex-network-proxy` (179 tests)\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- `just fix -p codex-network-proxy`\n- `just fmt`\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: viyatb-oai <viyatb@openai.com>","tree":{"sha":"6f336db8a7082aabd0c25a8524377a78ffb71e05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/6f336db8a7082aabd0c25a8524377a78ffb71e05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c5a9a95ab660d54869468ff3282d9d067e66a675","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOtyTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYp4QAEjeTkAZGVBXxhyhsPWqJqTf\nhSj3yfZ+55c9+uxPLtYfwPWEthzyos9Ck/GwLodNGassz+87krP4wY1+zCU89cTs\nOde7J3sEvdVNuu6GPJRgcdDPTdWEqjNnLwlHZfxi7gJ9DEsQcoOPEaczQsGeoBYt\nkN3FdVb5N+0IXl5dbuUfq1tMZ6C8ZdldWpJF79dlFhP2qW8zu55nyBy1hwpiuyzt\nAcBBuXRT/+ZtvvhhOtw76E0kpkup6QtK19K6H+pAF5TP/Wydgq7yYb4vDr4f54p7\n+s9nWHIaKe1h0A26lzb0rgeldTvkw87Qx3HVldgNGtM3ScJBbdGMQVIW2Gh0bnMW\nELvfUN2UxTdx/qEBmK81nIvaaSd8dwF0V7FQGWsgIiApi/bFHVK7flR+k9LCAAA3\nYmMFJ9Bl+slNK7Ll9BjkviCWYPPpsDrhaSNOsW9x+eklHfiY0etcbruBGk4x0paB\n2fTULOe+pmnfQtJZNuN3f5hNZRFBnKQr/IZ5uUYWL/Nvp5bEIKj1//L0+jcF2s1c\nVZTG0aYD0RM0ihNSngzOLZfCVE0jQpqIpeXPt9u0d41cVbwfFnWUt5jVdfM8kJ7l\n8+4ND76szCFPxq3gGmHBlvtGxOj/UniniIo63ztM0JAGfgrNq+EiiYyrWALOB3fu\nEWQ9J4Pk8MHOqkjuz+2K\n=WdSq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6f336db8a7082aabd0c25a8524377a78ffb71e05\nparent 354807920e0b21e4c1691d5c08f2152a4e972409\nauthor Winston Howes <winston@openai.com> 1782242451 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782242451 -0700\n\nKeep managed MITM CA private keys in proxy memory (#29013)\n\n## Why\n\nThe managed MITM trust bundle must be readable by sandboxed commands.\nPersisting its sibling CA private key under `$CODEX_HOME/proxy`\ntherefore requires a deny-read sandbox rule, but the Windows unelevated\nbackend rejects deny-read paths and WSL1's legacy Landlock path cannot\nenforce that rule.\n\nA persistent OS credential store also does not provide the same\ncross-platform boundary from other processes running as the same user.\nKeeping the signer inside the network proxy process avoids both\nproblems: ordinary sandbox setup stays independent of CA-key state, and\nno private signing key is exposed through the filesystem or a persistent\ncredential record.\n\n## What\n\n- generate one managed CA per proxy process and retain its private\nsigner only in proxy memory\n- emit only content-addressed public CA certificates and trust bundles\nunder `$CODEX_HOME/proxy`\n- hold a cross-process lease for each active public certificate and\nprune artifacts from inactive proxy processes\n- keep all CA ownership in `codex-network-proxy`; no `codex-core` or\nsandbox-policy changes\n- validate generated trust-bundle paths by their content hash\n- keep the public bundle readable by sandboxed commands on Windows,\nWSL1, macOS, and Linux\n\nThe independent startup custom-CA follow-up is #29014.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `CODEX_HOME=/private/tmp/codex-test-home-network-proxy just test -p\ncodex-network-proxy` (179 tests)\n- `just bazel-lock-check`\n- `just fix -p codex-network-proxy`\n- `just fmt`\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: viyatb-oai <viyatb@openai.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T19:20:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c5a9a95ab660d54869468ff3282d9d067e66a675","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c5a9a95ab660d54869468ff3282d9d067e66a675","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c5a9a95ab660d54869468ff3282d9d067e66a675/comments","author":{"login":"winston-openai","id":177672674,"node_id":"U_kgDOCpcR4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177672674?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/winston-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://ap