hub.com/openai/codex/commit/b539e3e72bbc8f7282d2dd4ac7bc1ab891e85738"}]},{"sha":"b539e3e72bbc8f7282d2dd4ac7bc1ab891e85738","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGI1MzllM2U3MmJiYzhmNzI4MmQyZGQ0YWM3YmMxYWI4OTFlODU3Mzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Winston Howes","email":"winston@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T18:06:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T18:06:07Z"},"message":"Handle additional tools in rollout persistence metrics (#29669)\n\n## Why\n\nThe rollout persistence metrics added on current `main` exhaustively\nmatch `ResponseItem`, but omit `ResponseItem::AdditionalTools`. That\nprevents `codex-rollout` and downstream targets from compiling across\nCargo and Bazel builds.\n\n## What\n\nMap `ResponseItem::AdditionalTools` to the `response.additional_tools`\nmetric label, consistent with the existing exact-variant labels.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-rollout` (76 passed)\n- `just fix -p codex-rollout`","tree":{"sha":"30bb6092f90991a150ecbe79f15fc1ff01986dda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/30bb6092f90991a150ecbe79f15fc1ff01986dda"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b539e3e72bbc8f7282d2dd4ac7bc1ab891e85738","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOssPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqrIQAK5Zws/CsTjvezI7a/jO/UDr\nL02NtCX91H6zsL0za1gjy7qNUfHM0q5iGh1tyNQAh9Wy3AMyBPMQqvdHTiG2TmtF\nc9KMLT8sDtAWcqcvK3B5xzGWGq6+2btIp47yKFEla9YYjIdmBVuIHWbXk1m1MZLW\nNTQullJ+yhq1ihmpTvncqwHJR3oNkKbHHbURR7Y0vGpccLb+7t2KObGnY2gIlAQG\ncDhfOdt+QjL0I9C7Yc4CXyADVT2yR8jhZj3ZFppiKxU+u1vlfVgNUgoKJfbaydOD\nAEFr34WCkCGXBO/sfkX/moZFhZKYgn6MqNsug+bAiNPWwbIU39fae2DyLcDxKbci\nJK04NVdZLwVVXjiSzaFwHCUgHoYtC6+VToiCV7ptr4+oi8q56HwaAWfDcXZ2qfuW\nJB1ojYo7+Jf/GybIBqAK5c1iXNSqu41xofmWCWIAwyx0QIomeEwwD1RLQTrXrcBd\nip9JSquiXx5utBDoFkbAIEr1/PahkRynIHthpI6J5y8IzJqvC7L6pBN5K0h3Bzrn\ndf7x9yOtjXRWmRQs+IobkWkUnCItTMZWdki9sV7LTv4NOCK0pg0mA4PhB32T7W9C\nUtmwo/HljI8R+9m9ZTnpawlbdZ7ZM2jQx8ghxgedmmduH+46nplS68Yzulb7aUfI\nZ21dtzyNsQjn3OHOeSyY\n=Dkzh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 30bb6092f90991a150ecbe79f15fc1ff01986dda\nparent 39ee1b96b009439f1914bd85f3b2e71fda33a1de\nauthor Winston Howes <winston@openai.com> 1782237967 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782237967 -0700\n\nHandle additional tools in rollout persistence metrics (#29669)\n\n## Why\n\nThe rollout persistence metrics added on current `main` exhaustively\nmatch `ResponseItem`, but omit `ResponseItem::AdditionalTools`. That\nprevents `codex-rollout` and downstream targets from compiling across\nCargo and Bazel builds.\n\n## What\n\nMap `ResponseItem::AdditionalTools` to the `response.additional_tools`\nmetric label, consistent with the existing exact-variant labels.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-rollout` (76 passed)\n- `just fix -p codex-rollout`","verified_at":"2026-06-23T18:06:08Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b539e3e72bbc8f7282d2dd4ac7bc1ab891e85738","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b539e3e72bbc8f7282d2dd4ac7bc1ab891e85738","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b539e3e72bbc8f7282d2dd4ac7bc1ab891e85738/comments","author":{"login":"winston-openai","id":177672674,"node_id":"U_kgDOCpcR4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177672674?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/winston-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"39ee1b96b009439f1914bd85f3b2e71fda33a1de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/39ee1b96b009439f1914bd85f3b2e71fda33a1de","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/39ee1b96b009439f1914bd85f3b2e71fda33a1de"}]},{"sha":"39ee1b96b009439f1914bd85f3b2e71fda33a1de","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDM5ZWUxYjk2YjAwOTQzOWYxOTE0YmQ4NWYzYjJlNzFmZGEzM2ExZGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T18:03:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T18:03:35Z"},"message":"[codex] Handle additional tools in rollout persistence metrics (#29672)\n\n## Summary\n\nHandle `ResponseItem::AdditionalTools` in rollout persistence metrics.\n\nThe persistence metrics match was added after the `AdditionalTools`\nvariant and omitted it, causing release builds to fail with a\nnon-exhaustive pattern error. This assigns the item the\n`response.additional_tools` metrics label.\n\nRelease failure:\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/28043786727/job/83016608475\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout` (76 passed)","tree":{"sha":"e5d383034bbcda6021df1ebfed7ed78893f79ee1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e5d383034bbcda6021df1ebfed7ed78893f79ee1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/39ee1b96b009439f1914bd85f3b2e71fda33a1de","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOsp3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATtoQACxwu03a7dWabWCpmCgc6CM+\nC0qIVpPWADxkheGD08c+Lvdvnrtwsb2dUsfQPrzg1oXzyCCmn5Z8f43EEuYFSojQ\nBIOAJoH9wCqItmHk6HzQ3UQI6BwBnS5Brcd3wnyJbggrH+9q9UB3JXVzGcixxLnt\nkPdLe7k9mQgEwMwo5KbPIur0/m9u9X2porlLu2sVqo1cQZLNNBaFK7T3tHo+DOi7\nGhXhSWYStiVFje+vKDnOY0cv/v5QT1wh4djpkN6fppyQSJbQpdTPP/IGYberLLDA\nFWauyXEwr5lcrxYpZwAErh5raL6IT9ioFec6GFvgmg/45r+IzDftJTrDU56YV5Bi\ngdmFhIxmh4JugtG05OkNXWnWMwuFpQYJbv0MPh3EOcUnZaw/o+Ge1C1hAHHRhZDI\n7AwyB5QOutSMj5utqPBPlnLWRpnCGM1Wzuu3svZ3b0QqupT2X8LyZLEOHqmsno7v\nSNySZS6EhaJWWhT8b6R3W94fUNvz94H7oJtxl545ID26UGCdPt24nf8md0EDBjVs\n9zDC4xc9ZLF+o5dHA/YeixvDyBP97grJP08Q+dRCpGtVH8dubGPcLVO8VXXRMy7h\nlFuwD2eX03YkCKNwO5tcdVTg21fm8e5dlgqXTPL/nby/2vppr7Hxs7c/g61bMIaH\n+Zy0HLTZDbOBhfn7GkvH\n=ZfL3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e5d383034bbcda6021df1ebfed7ed78893f79ee1\nparent d1d11cac0556ce678750b791e49e45162ab4fb05\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1782237815 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782237815 +0000\n\n[codex] Handle additional tools in rollout persistence metrics (#29672)\n\n## Summary\n\nHandle `ResponseItem::AdditionalTools` in rollout persistence metrics.\n\nThe persistence metrics match was added after the `AdditionalTools`\nvariant and omitted it, causing release builds to fail with a\nnon-exhaustive pattern error. This assigns the item the\n`response.additional_tools` metrics label.\n\nRelease failure:\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/actions/runs/28043786727/job/83016608475\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just fmt`\n- `just test -p codex-rollout` (76 passed)","verified_at":"2026-06-23T18:03:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/39ee1b96b009439f1914bd85f3b2e71fda33a1de","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/39ee1b96b009439f1914bd85f3b2e71fda33a1de","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/39ee1b96b009439f1914bd85f3b2e71fda33a1de/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d1d11cac0556ce678750b791e49e45162ab4fb05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d1d11cac0556ce678750b791e49e45162ab4fb05","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d1d11cac0556ce678750b791e49e45162ab4fb05"}]},{"sha":"d1d11cac0556ce678750b791e49e45162ab4fb05","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQxZDExY2FjMDU1NmNlNjc4NzUwYjc5MWU0OWU0NTE2MmFiNGZiMDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"sayan-oai","email":"sayan@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T17:33:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T17:33:19Z"},"message":"core: use turn-owned world state for inline compaction (#29527)\n\n## Why\n\nFollow-up to #29249 and its [compaction review\nthread](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29249#discussion_r3455055101).\n\nDuring a turn, environment readiness can change between sampling\nrequests. Inline compaction must render the same model-visible\n`WorldState` used by the request it follows. Rebuilding that state\nduring compaction can observe a newer environment, make replacement\nhistory disagree with what the model saw, and suppress the next\nenvironment update.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Make `run_turn` own the current `Arc<WorldState>` and replace it only\nbetween sampling requests.\n- Build each state from an explicitly chosen environment snapshot, diff\ndeferred-executor steps against the turn-owned state, and retain the\nlatest state in `ContextManager` only for cross-turn and resume\ntracking.\n- Pass the exact turn-owned state into inline compaction and explicit\nnew-context-window replacement.\n- Carry that state with\n`InitialContextInjection::BeforeLastUserMessage`, so replacement context\nand its stored baseline cannot come from different snapshots.\n- Remove obsolete state-recapture helpers and ambiguous TurnContext-only\nWorldState builders.\n- Add an integration test that moves an environment from starting to\nready during a paused turn, triggers compaction, and verifies the next\nrequest receives the readiness update exactly once.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\ndeferred_executor_compaction_preserves_then_updates_environment_once`\n- `just test -p codex-core process_compacted_history`\n- `just test -p codex-core mid_turn_continuation_compaction`\n- `just test -p codex-core build_initial_context`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nignores_session_prefix_messages_when_truncating`","tree":{"sha":"0a98bbd53f88010b62de50141bd062cea8ec0a6c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/0a98bbd53f88010b62de50141bd062cea8ec0a6c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d1d11cac0556ce678750b791e49e45162ab4fb05","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOsNfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAL8gQAG0gg3IGxyeEvErs6wQq+o+y\n3GRyfHVUgnPzXDOQ4QhEf1rvyGdFUMzISt01CSj37PeKBS/V8b2oEN31n5pqMY4W\n5hz+Ynq0j+9BED428dWcjoChH0OY5GOwXLq5OQ/dVKqrtn6m1KW2zzq8DKNZHjOt\nRoyMLE4NUq8V9pG14pTmFRKk/W5vkd5qfYl/ppVA2fyh1QU2zYJDmLB5kc2eLBxx\nfgbOQeoTxpxi8Vr9KiNYEci268/vwDUNKcOHSgXug8IbvgWqFRuvt7GBwaSubQjp\n08gd06dmtsJNpPAIYng/RVUBSa7pTYE4pUpVveSpvlpR+96C5YzRUP/72eD+pBFj\nz/N5Zat3kH92gAM6as9XfOh4CN+Z768VVCHn4f68QUoso6bjiokG5dsFutr/VNIP\ncNNV8h9UOx7r5N3VbGAN8upiE0W4PC5pEwZ1c8TiyN9NcrYa4apSVMK3H1XwBPW+\nMF3lmE92Li1FIk3FlU3Oked6NunRILVAbU2Jhi0wUVS8RqkQlFmtxCOYNuZpQQTv\nXVEE3nzILxm1n3PRlARfqNRNCiGRhC/Z1MEuEMEwWlx5DjbLfvRmUI3ZF+Ru47Bt\nGpW2xOTyc30dmry64vjXTipkB0ABLr5gVz+4jQ6VmmDSNDwbqx7l+h9gMHJ5X/x1\noL9KuJEFJBjJkqp+r9tg\n=9IEz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0a98bbd53f88010b62de50141bd062cea8ec0a6c\nparent 8751fd3fcb8031d42b62670a6131872074635c9b\nauthor sayan-oai <sayan@openai.com> 1782235999 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782235999 -0700\n\ncore: use turn-owned world state for inline compaction (#29527)\n\n## Why\n\nFollow-up to #29249 and its [compaction review\nthread](https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29249#discussion_r3455055101).\n\nDuring a turn, environment readiness can change between sampling\nrequests. Inline compaction must render the same model-visible\n`WorldState` used by the request it follows. Rebuilding that state\nduring compaction can observe a newer environment, make replacement\nhistory disagree with what the model saw, and suppress the next\nenvironment update.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Make `run_turn` own the current `Arc<WorldState>` and replace it only\nbetween sampling requests.\n- Build each state from an explicitly chosen environment snapshot, diff\ndeferred-executor steps against the turn-owned state, and retain the\nlatest state in `ContextManager` only for cross-turn and resume\ntracking.\n- Pass the exact turn-owned state into inline compaction and explicit\nnew-context-window replacement.\n- Carry that state with\n`InitialContextInjection::BeforeLastUserMessage`, so replacement context\nand its stored baseline cannot come from different snapshots.\n- Remove obsolete state-recapture helpers and ambiguous TurnContext-only\nWorldState builders.\n- Add an integration test that moves an environment from starting to\nready during a paused turn, triggers compaction, and verifies the next\nrequest receives the readiness update exactly once.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\ndeferred_executor_compaction_preserves_then_updates_environment_once`\n- `just test -p codex-core process_compacted_history`\n- `just test -p codex-core mid_turn_continuation_compaction`\n- `just test -p codex-core build_initial_context`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nignores_session_prefix_messages_when_truncating`","verified_at":"2026-06-23T17:33:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d1d11cac0556ce678750b791e49e45162ab4fb05","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d1d11cac0556ce678750b791e49e45162ab4fb05","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d1d11cac0556ce678750b791e49e45162ab4fb05/comments","author":{"login":"sayan-oai","id":244841968,"node_id":"U_kgDODpf98A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244841968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/sayan-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sayan-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8751fd3fcb8031d42b62670a6131872074635c9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8751fd3fcb8031d42b62670a6131872074635c9b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8751fd3fcb8031d42b62670a6131872074635c9b"}]},{"sha":"8751fd3fcb8031d42b62670a6131872074635c9b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDg3NTFmZDNmY2I4MDMxZDQyYjYyNjcwYTYxMzE4NzIwNzQ2MzVjOWI","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T17:29:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T17:29:27Z"},"message":"Shut down superseded MCP managers on refresh (#29608)\n\n## Summary\n\nMCP refresh replaced the published connection manager without shutting\ndown the manager it superseded. If another task retained that old\nmanager, its stdio MCP processes stayed alive and accumulated across\nrefreshes.\n\nAtomically swap in the refreshed manager, then explicitly shut down the\nexact manager returned by the swap. Add a process-level regression test\nthat retains the old manager during refresh and verifies its stdio\nprocess exits while the replacement remains available.\n\n## Context\n\nExplicit cleanup was lost when manager publication moved to `ArcSwap`.\nDropping the old manager is not a reliable shutdown boundary because\nactive callers can retain its `Arc` and underlying client process\nhandles.","tree":{"sha":"4fccafd583d76d78125187727e1e2ebdbffba1d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/4fccafd583d76d78125187727e1e2ebdbffba1d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/8751fd3fcb8031d42b62670a6131872074635c9b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOsJ3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhrMQAA1/W68kj+sjs67SqBYVXQIc\nI8nEoiZGHDnB21U3gFo6Ql4swYhLUS+3O+cHRcFD9ER4EbvhJoec2vr5LcfWn9f9\nctOGaZXsW5gQkIkCt1IGxzpLJ3oGif0fpMBdDxh5VUEnCpc6DJa0bUqMXONF4W+T\nuFyunlcopmtA4gNi/ESamcNm3rCLUrOmC6bF7yDv0F6v0wngWtJK4sxI/eUskq5t\nMmuhAbSbfsmifHt1AVWM25+MakybrCBqYndTx7OqVYaLbtYkaJ+R26eo9VjHFLow\n/3xhEQ1xSnEgwS//fy3BDm0brG/8pyNM/ZLV+V6rtfk8OWZGkOJ0rqRfrrVIGQuT\nDjt8MIORjwaCgFH+50sXFf1MwLRKSrJ2cUnACznhiK0aNmXiUeCTFJxBwoHJdFk8\nOb3k1/SWofzdhQGApSbGfn8V51T/kO/SgqwkOTAvr+1EO0ZepmQJwilYSVEGapMk\ngnJwTb6EYRpjvdzOrzfWEfIBBpMgUhNQgPqibSHDLw24PXy+idxjuDttYo2gL2Tp\nnC2nGI72jNNxmqRmzaMqPMoiv3800/5fK2Xo5DODf6iwapXfhMDeZQnTVyeRYVG/\nojtXzTqgZvV/bZDxhjxb4cY+0576S712ebPV/f65eeezPE5faJg9FUoIqFHKzSax\nE8FeALPu3aeQBf8l4YcX\n=p6hH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 4fccafd583d76d78125187727e1e2ebdbffba1d8\nparent 9fe689783deba43105a241facb312626bec1a383\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782235767 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782235767 +0100\n\nShut down superseded MCP managers on refresh (#29608)\n\n## Summary\n\nMCP refresh replaced the published connection manager without shutting\ndown the manager it superseded. If another task retained that old\nmanager, its stdio MCP processes stayed alive and accumulated across\nrefreshes.\n\nAtomically swap in the refreshed manager, then explicitly shut down the\nexact manager returned by the swap. Add a process-level regression test\nthat retains the old manager during refresh and verifies its stdio\nprocess exits while the replacement remains available.\n\n## Context\n\nExplicit cleanup was lost when manager publication moved to `ArcSwap`.\nDropping the old manager is not a reliable shutdown boundary because\nactive callers can retain its `Arc` and underlying client process\nhandles.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T17:29:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8751fd3fcb8031d42b62670a6131872074635c9b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/8751fd3fcb8031d42b62670a6131872074635c9b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/8751fd3fcb8031d42b62670a6131872074635c9b/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9fe689783deba43105a241facb312626bec1a383","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9fe689783deba43105a241facb312626bec1a383","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9fe689783deba43105a241facb312626bec1a383"}]},{"sha":"9fe689783deba43105a241facb312626bec1a383","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDlmZTY4OTc4M2RlYmE0MzEwNWEyNDFmYWNiMzEyNjI2YmVjMWEzODM","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T17:13:27Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T17:13:27Z"},"message":"[core] debounce current-time reminders by elapsed time (#29659)\n\n## Summary\n- rename `reminder_interval_model_requests` to\n`reminder_interval_seconds`\n- read the configured time provider before every model request and\ninject a reminder only after the configured number of seconds has\nelapsed\n- preserve immediate first delivery and forced delivery after compaction\nchanges the context window\n\n## Tests\n- `just test -p codex-core current_time_reminder`","tree":{"sha":"3f546c12780780ae6f668fa3736f6f3aeda25c49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3f546c12780780ae6f668fa3736f6f3aeda25c49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/9fe689783deba43105a241facb312626bec1a383","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOr63CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABWAQAAczN0wzg2/ucwDAMQCIk7Ga\nY+yYF1hYo9cI1hus4eYTBKlZhX8fTZWKN3MZBCYNkO8hQAg4OK/iegk4BaJ1/1TA\nNbu8+BQJZv1jepDjPK0Ch4pIy0/8B4VDAPZWB0KbqIFCJXERXoeTb0HWApk++TBr\ndefxcgi7zdMLTvT8JAY+5ui0wArz9/JlWMNcaQJWybiFXsA2i5hLpA4eqgC2KiVH\nzxl09TKVDlEiSX9b0h1lZR714gNk/1WiVlMGyZ2PeOSdG5JI80jnxpYgMBEVUxem\nVfxI31QNHH2LKX1jEx/YsV5MjcMaKSCw8azMoMV2iP975sbitWhMlkNbymbqhdBw\nk/mYs0MKzM7ih0RBGd9CKp7A+1Rby28LpM73d1QkLCogYRwvNUPwLZZvtg6jo1Lg\nh/+HaIASdscX86KsxK3b3nRIQRtaZvXF3OavmcjSHM5tjYbF4ppuPBLcly8JVPa0\nZ4vq0Q/0RnOC4ET6HUI+raOzlip4rhrR9f0+711UkXazhV/gj6llDbcphk0119t0\nYW9w0aADB9Hmt1ulXAEI+L6bnIcH68g3qR18n2Yym0bELg/qMQVCkF0mgDU0QNI3\nIThm2Evn+LAldRIMn/3GNmfe79k11DjxOr6NTwuJ0gpeM6QQtEgKOJqPMEx+lMKh\n4Uvu1Zr0rmMqbO4UDR5B\n=AzEQ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3f546c12780780ae6f668fa3736f6f3aeda25c49\nparent 02c326f646f80065bdb574d2fad50a86f93a98d7\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1782234807 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782234807 -0700\n\n[core] debounce current-time reminders by elapsed time (#29659)\n\n## Summary\n- rename `reminder_interval_model_requests` to\n`reminder_interval_seconds`\n- read the configured time provider before every model request and\ninject a reminder only after the configured number of seconds has\nelapsed\n- preserve immediate first delivery and forced delivery after compaction\nchanges the context window\n\n## Tests\n- `just test -p codex-core current_time_reminder`","verified_at":"2026-06-23T17:13:28Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9fe689783deba43105a241facb312626bec1a383","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/9fe689783deba43105a241facb312626bec1a383","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/9fe689783deba43105a241facb312626bec1a383/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"02c326f646f80065bdb574d2fad50a86f93a98d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/02c326f646f80065bdb574d2fad50a86f93a98d7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/02c326f646f80065bdb574d2fad50a86f93a98d7"}]},{"sha":"02c326f646f80065bdb574d2fad50a86f93a98d7","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDAyYzMyNmY2NDZmODAwNjViZGI1NzRkMmZhZDUwYTg2ZjkzYTk4ZDc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Tom","email":"wiltzius@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T16:26:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T16:26:30Z"},"message":"[codex] Instrument rollout persistence bytes (#29498)\n\n- Add 1%-sampled rollout persistence metrics that report per-item and\nper-thread JSON byte totals before and after filtering when metrics\nexport is enabled.\n- Tag each item with its exact response or event variant, including\nnested turn-item kinds for conditionally persisted completion events, so\naggregate cloud-storage impact can be estimated by policy choice.","tree":{"sha":"a782cdbebb27007d4ceeb0453dc468098a9bf437","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/a782cdbebb27007d4ceeb0453dc468098a9bf437"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/02c326f646f80065bdb574d2fad50a86f93a98d7","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOrO2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjsEQAHhcKiw5/SZE5UAfZD69+fbK\nxj1eeX5F/7Cnl7njNXQBjo7WVuwppUEoobuS0ghCTkx+kNjo7Ft+Lo4tjPO5zfzC\n8euBtnAwNjZyFeLoUastX2khKuIfTai+6pMnfutymzhMBPwlKeHbusMLB07CJOv0\nv2iuYaeKg2uZ9bmohOJB/3Mk4GOhqccmGJSon8h+t1TY+t0qwxwF69eYZRct8ZW7\nzg4XRwTEcoHJJaIqHbTwojvJt/dltAI9C/EDNdCYI7p18V30AVKi8r9KYXIql0QF\nPB6C2yk5+stOJDT0lP2CqGP6e2ldYMT1p8HPUNugNgeN7JKnLYyEHzfxljcAlgdH\nePgHZf2bC6J9az4YAav5lCnrxY28d7emCv5O9Xh/8umRfE0bHP2GFbroyR60wYuJ\nyfYgz+HnF+kG7hsF2e6fIcc+fXGDDNA/YwbzL4iW+tJiMedCu408oDrB+CoNXmGe\ngYfIV9ZZOhnM1BViy5NMgpfZL4HHOembA7VWyJYZtmiioDeacuU2PxAWV++/2UuB\nuTcGrcP9LWIjBx/PrtZJDBmg4QArlT+VcxTI48TqkqYcux8J7Mh2Qv2PrI69XSjo\nMKhQSWACObfwmfFzJrpfFhgw+aznB0+4Gk5KV8xnqbDK2r4O4Drsuv1LiwbMqj38\nXRktKBOnQWh/7BbrkCYN\n=TVR6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a782cdbebb27007d4ceeb0453dc468098a9bf437\nparent c553cea9eae2648d74342e21ce68233893e81d2c\nauthor Tom <wiltzius@openai.com> 1782231990 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782231990 -0700\n\n[codex] Instrument rollout persistence bytes (#29498)\n\n- Add 1%-sampled rollout persistence metrics that report per-item and\nper-thread JSON byte totals before and after filtering when metrics\nexport is enabled.\n- Tag each item with its exact response or event variant, including\nnested turn-item kinds for conditionally persisted completion events, so\naggregate cloud-storage impact can be estimated by policy choice.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T16:26:30Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/02c326f646f80065bdb574d2fad50a86f93a98d7","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/02c326f646f80065bdb574d2fad50a86f93a98d7","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/02c326f646f80065bdb574d2fad50a86f93a98d7/comments","author":{"login":"wiltzius-openai","id":176426546,"node_id":"U_kgDOCoQOMg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176426546?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai","html_url":"https://github.com/wiltzius-openai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wiltzius-openai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c553cea9eae2648d74342e21ce68233893e81d2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c553cea9eae2648d74342e21ce68233893e81d2c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c553cea9eae2648d74342e21ce68233893e81d2c"}]},{"sha":"c553cea9eae2648d74342e21ce68233893e81d2c","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGM1NTNjZWE5ZWFlMjY0OGQ3NDM0MmUyMWNlNjgyMzM4OTNlODFkMmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T15:19:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T15:19:19Z"},"message":"Update vulnerable Hono and fast-uri dependencies (#29650)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Pin `hono` to 4.12.25, the first patched release for the recent Hono\nsecurity advisories.\n- Pin `fast-uri` to 3.1.1 to fix the percent-encoded path traversal\nvulnerability.\n- Refresh `pnpm-lock.yaml` with only those dependency updates.\n\n`hono` 4.12.25 is used instead of the newer 4.12.27 because the\nrepository requires dependencies to be at least seven days old.","tree":{"sha":"e0d3c010c4e57aa5745d8debc4e3fc7b12d492bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/e0d3c010c4e57aa5745d8debc4e3fc7b12d492bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/c553cea9eae2648d74342e21ce68233893e81d2c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOqP3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbd8QAI4jqhEjAuEolf/iT2/SY6XD\nJCE1DIIlRO6eKJ4Cxpj6JkB1dIOcbHcPpA4xIpnQaz/c7dJeUtvcsYmzlECyvezX\nM4WLBWMvasQsI33b9xi7xxaRcm4crkBcObeuduL+6d0hOl0tWZQYU9RQGGwFkC+n\n1O3bBKo0AoboUsybT9N05l6MH+SEfQrY7qnLjnRG3kb9OCzb78xyOmItK/GyrSLF\nuekTnDcz2gtJDItvU83+8J7MdbxObqosysiInxRA020fSIccktVx2Z1xMvn7RItV\nW9iA3/Kd02aXwGmI2Vrvfvq2eUZ2bk4S0O7cQS/TPAImOF5xx7wSgE0zzh0EPeN2\n2g7QcO51pLMOiWK7luqb0zDN+7y9Ns6J9JG3KjRbijnyXl5pfOxMgofuhB6wpoYm\nnemiUEdj++3jIFnjP0f10WAZQTtN40aLMq2VyB9oGlT9v1zuXV2Vp2kmgTJz2ifq\nzrjcEuf6m6Bb3/s1+XUiTCAC3tr9FJTZ3UrKrbLd/JXIhROvBA+kTjLX3dqudgv8\nQz0ghq/RXILnqW9jQCPoMs38eYGJMCmS4jQu/so8pGiSP3lPPWW+dCXde63WtFpo\nIUlIP0MMyKPdtc5hc/daeajsuf/St/Icx87xcmRr2gfMeJN2wAAaWRi+8ljfSIN4\nI2Swp55FadY8XRPuyGaJ\n=UX3C\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e0d3c010c4e57aa5745d8debc4e3fc7b12d492bb\nparent bbe100689073815876d330e56a200217a96a9e35\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782227959 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782227959 +0100\n\nUpdate vulnerable Hono and fast-uri dependencies (#29650)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Pin `hono` to 4.12.25, the first patched release for the recent Hono\nsecurity advisories.\n- Pin `fast-uri` to 3.1.1 to fix the percent-encoded path traversal\nvulnerability.\n- Refresh `pnpm-lock.yaml` with only those dependency updates.\n\n`hono` 4.12.25 is used instead of the newer 4.12.27 because the\nrepository requires dependencies to be at least seven days old.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T15:19:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c553cea9eae2648d74342e21ce68233893e81d2c","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/c553cea9eae2648d74342e21ce68233893e81d2c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/c553cea9eae2648d74342e21ce68233893e81d2c/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bbe100689073815876d330e56a200217a96a9e35","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bbe100689073815876d330e56a200217a96a9e35","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bbe100689073815876d330e56a200217a96a9e35"}]},{"sha":"bbe100689073815876d330e56a200217a96a9e35","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGJiZTEwMDY4OTA3MzgxNTg3NmQzMzBlNTZhMjAwMjE3YTk2YTllMzU","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T14:25:28Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T14:25:28Z"},"message":"Update rmcp to 1.8.0 (#29634)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Update `rmcp` and `rmcp-macros` from 1.7.0 to 1.8.0.\n- Adapt to the new shared `peer_info` return type.\n- Box OAuth status discovery at the MCP boundary to keep the expanded\nfuture type from overflowing Rust's trait recursion limit.\n\nThis brings in custom OAuth HTTP client support from\n[modelcontextprotocol/rust-sdk#908](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/rust-sdk/pull/908).","tree":{"sha":"7e63360c579fbc4c2490209a362dcc40d1ffa289","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/7e63360c579fbc4c2490209a362dcc40d1ffa289"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/bbe100689073815876d330e56a200217a96a9e35","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOpdYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHXgQAKAxpmi+TzhAUTgN+HBvKTwi\nlQvwJPXGQB4LP8XP+xHDdkAccRxV422xIlzkOtAAj0rddfZHHpeE2XhihkiYbSIt\nFKzMqbSGn5zN8Rrbb/adBoBW3WpF/H+YUa5f4UpZHgzBYXBoTeOFpcdTCDdIxppG\n4608qC2DFB1WGA9HzIDgIPwzyJrs8Avq6b6+zSmWBrEfvPG8uyT9TTeX4sVtOmmA\nNHIgh4Yr7aYLJOwWeDSPP7KZ9Wvd44Iz9AN0PZI02YOtNd9uDVCWQ9l0SVLnK5dq\nNWfFovEXv33DgYlWEuqsiQ88DFNrtv3XiulE3r44m4IGOgmb78QuAhmOlbCfZVFX\n2gniq24PWU0Wz02Wajhg5WQkOvdAymLW4sn5AzyzVvdfKua6bq85r3BcXRde7A8I\nrSQQ3WKTPwHQqRNHplayFrtyJHDDRmQBUprMdJQq+OMS5gv64ejVDRR1nM/qy43/\nSKdexXD3Y0teeW2vSRkzNfud/TAwFc5Iey1YphTAAzi7MP6ZYZnQI5xrDhFuwrYC\nuznDkLXoT6e5Bnqzs33avbr3R2FUhAjYjWrBzp5VwYRkfdQKtup4CWp6Xc23/EB+\nlv5pAEQBoceybaRawp7v6YIG0NJ1KRHOwiwysY+dnBNuJw6VUAQQqWwqIg/HZk1g\ndqzYsSwzYn1q+5aCo3V3\n=L8Yb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7e63360c579fbc4c2490209a362dcc40d1ffa289\nparent 330ae6a516009e127db01843f5049497d3c46805\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782224728 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782224728 +0100\n\nUpdate rmcp to 1.8.0 (#29634)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Update `rmcp` and `rmcp-macros` from 1.7.0 to 1.8.0.\n- Adapt to the new shared `peer_info` return type.\n- Box OAuth status discovery at the MCP boundary to keep the expanded\nfuture type from overflowing Rust's trait recursion limit.\n\nThis brings in custom OAuth HTTP client support from\n[modelcontextprotocol/rust-sdk#908](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/rust-sdk/pull/908).","verified_at":"2026-06-23T14:25:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bbe100689073815876d330e56a200217a96a9e35","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/bbe100689073815876d330e56a200217a96a9e35","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/bbe100689073815876d330e56a200217a96a9e35/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"330ae6a516009e127db01843f5049497d3c46805","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/330ae6a516009e127db01843f5049497d3c46805","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/330ae6a516009e127db01843f5049497d3c46805"}]},{"sha":"330ae6a516009e127db01843f5049497d3c46805","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDMzMGFlNmE1MTYwMDllMTI3ZGIwMTg0M2Y1MDQ5NDk3ZDNjNDY4MDU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Charlie Marsh","email":"charliemarsh@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T14:23:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T14:23:25Z"},"message":"Share resumed rollout history (#28426)\n\n## Summary\n\nResuming a persisted thread currently deep-clones its complete rollout\nhistory several times. `InitialHistory` is retained for the app-server\nresponse, copied into thread persistence, and copied again by read-only\naccessors. These copies scale with the complete rollout rather than the\nbounded model context and add measurable latency for large sessions.\n\nThis change stores resumed rollout history in `Arc<Vec<RolloutItem>>`.\nRollout loading wraps the parsed vector once, while app-server response\nconstruction, session initialization, and thread persistence share it\nthrough inexpensive `Arc` clones. Read-only history access now returns a\nborrowed slice, and fork paths use `Arc::unwrap_or_clone` where they\ngenuinely need mutable ownership. Rollout reconstruction also consumes\nits temporary context instead of cloning the reconstructed model\nhistory.\n\nThe serialized representation remains unchanged. In an artificial 123 MB\nrollout benchmark, sharing resumed history reduced cold resume latency\nby roughly 9–10%. The affected crates compile with their test targets,\nall 80 thread-store tests pass, and the Bazel dependency lock remains\nvalid.","tree":{"sha":"c7a54d56b5fef4260088b04d288c7087c6363707","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c7a54d56b5fef4260088b04d288c7087c6363707"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/330ae6a516009e127db01843f5049497d3c46805","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOpbdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAW+AQABAezSzCbJqS6UsMD1YPALui\ngIVmZAAPrI+XY6RnPXEOFvOn9OOzVKRadTHw3z2zhsD/vReE1H+w2Z9v7JbzUf2+\nIfEZZcuFbFHlIVjZEkpDc4JZ6zQO1Oih43QSpB6km25QQZ6F175PjHE9ILeVeGsw\nTAFnFHPg5yQsdGHwWCBI6vOGgp8ydsi6wkeqR6bW5qGaIdSxm/Vs72JXTN84I8SW\nn5EacHYqG+dXZNiy1jgFkup/t06xYyO5G9nC+zcSZESCZI4Yw2aZu9a9tmGxJqTZ\nzH1pYMt1LzGCXmCjbFVqU6k/RgGu1tlcdRj3BAl2zeVHoGZDffCA0L1VdPLAE+Jo\nZBxSIxZwzMAfRvEKMMes2zxrlGEwAVtcx3VnPM/mG9eONRW5Uy/fpCdohI8tfBno\nsPOs3Lw2qKtOY1nKbcfviPpoEyy6vvjF95jACDB96TXtnk+JJcbckB7r1ZtHB4RK\nq2QGJ6OJYR1vLCPwTOTz3Ikfbv+6D8W8UBh346LCwXHtEi15Xwy5TauzErtrNUkG\nujoFDtiuxr+JdkNFghyNR+DXbh6YE1HLRDp3zOKpPh+e77Jt0Tmxv2qZ8KBhzilj\nMHK7F5wQq9qV05+DU//vhfk4e2C1JpZL/dQiJt84zbvg1jXYlJz4M/qgX1Xi1pMc\n+5JvVrikTOgTFdjreyjm\n=rALq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c7a54d56b5fef4260088b04d288c7087c6363707\nparent 414782450952a196bbb64b1605a458c2531c47b6\nauthor Charlie Marsh <charliemarsh@openai.com> 1782224605 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782224605 -0400\n\nShare resumed rollout history (#28426)\n\n## Summary\n\nResuming a persisted thread currently deep-clones its complete rollout\nhistory several times. `InitialHistory` is retained for the app-server\nresponse, copied into thread persistence, and copied again by read-only\naccessors. These copies scale with the complete rollout rather than the\nbounded model context and add measurable latency for large sessions.\n\nThis change stores resumed rollout history in `Arc<Vec<RolloutItem>>`.\nRollout loading wraps the parsed vector once, while app-server response\nconstruction, session initialization, and thread persistence share it\nthrough inexpensive `Arc` clones. Read-only history access now returns a\nborrowed slice, and fork paths use `Arc::unwrap_or_clone` where they\ngenuinely need mutable ownership. Rollout reconstruction also consumes\nits temporary context instead of cloning the reconstructed model\nhistory.\n\nThe serialized representation remains unchanged. In an artificial 123 MB\nrollout benchmark, sharing resumed history reduced cold resume latency\nby roughly 9–10%. The affected crates compile with their test targets,\nall 80 thread-store tests pass, and the Bazel dependency lock remains\nvalid.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T14:23:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/330ae6a516009e127db01843f5049497d3c46805","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/330ae6a516009e127db01843f5049497d3c46805","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/330ae6a516009e127db01843f5049497d3c46805/comments","author":{"login":"charliemarsh-oai","id":282065134,"node_id":"U_kgDOEM_47g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/282065134?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/charliemarsh-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charliemarsh-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"414782450952a196bbb64b1605a458c2531c47b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/414782450952a196bbb64b1605a458c2531c47b6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/414782450952a196bbb64b1605a458c2531c47b6"}]},{"sha":"414782450952a196bbb64b1605a458c2531c47b6","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQxNDc4MjQ1MDk1MmExOTZiYmI2NGIxNjA1YTQ1OGMyNTMxYzQ3YjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T13:59:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T13:59:39Z"},"message":"path-uri: add lexical containment (#29614)\n\n## Why\n\nExecutor-owned paths must stay portable while the orchestrator reasons\nabout them. Converting a Windows or remote path to the orchestrator\nhost's native path just to check containment breaks that boundary.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add lexical containment to `PathUri`.\n- Compare URI authorities and complete path segments, so `plugin-other`\nis not treated as a child of `plugin`.\n- Fail closed for encoded path separators and opaque fallback URIs.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nfile:///C:/plugins/foo/assets/icon.svg\n  is below file:///C:/plugins/foo\n\nfile:///C:/plugins/foo2/icon.svg\n  is not below file:///C:/plugins/foo\n```\n\nThis is the shared foundation for keeping executor-owned plugin\nresources URI-native without consulting the orchestrator filesystem.","tree":{"sha":"c5295fc0db1ea8177cabec8f84aea1a875e32a65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/c5295fc0db1ea8177cabec8f84aea1a875e32a65"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/414782450952a196bbb64b1605a458c2531c47b6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOpFLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAi0cQAEXBQXjgQxd46CQMFIHJ6RYI\nqczxpMvJyj2hwt+194nttBwSLBfFRSmpxUDHk5gPROLmnPpSyAwHT05tjhBfh3KQ\nQKD7iUaIJqEcFMysk+Tr5d6U0ii1E3Z6An3Dz4pM8gZ9iyr9ClusIBNCduG3wQEG\nNcgHjPfhh4tEEDyN1aLaLbelk9rAPC4XpLZt2r52pFVmhcvi28AGP6jCvB17RBe1\nf8vxq4/7ihONt+yhRCDjUcFD3C9VMGi0HjZB7vjULiq0mdJIqNgtajWjJiKAcju5\ng+9RCjr01C/ivCXKMme3WsrOsFrd7vPRNmsX5AzS27/BMyOvnLZ7lnsZpBXH5GLq\nzQyJBFtyZlTrkeIOa0VnfGTQK5wUkrmx5Z3dyRqMDXvB5x21+UMnTtPC9C6/MbxF\n/fbPIgtb6lv84821eAhM/WgHoEFhwBK/o+s0TpCJtcT8qt2gn2AlHWKaBi8cVzPp\n6SNRIxAjn0uU+JpliBZAji9LviWyDJMNLZgt79+vXkK4pZcyWUCa2R6oOV0fNo3t\nVgwpgk+Y99tpJy9/tNXn8OxRNl0HmprpM4vVQn6maRYy+1zAwbF5poCn4FYzUKeV\nlozEQkzLi3lY637HV/dMloy2zkXyngn9JBBaVdgByW6FKtnlWClZJ3Xmw7RXZf94\nCsHCxHwNRoLtHK+kYPrW\n=nlg6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c5295fc0db1ea8177cabec8f84aea1a875e32a65\nparent 49614a0391d83eec442ffeca1d4aa0fdeb119818\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782223179 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782223179 +0100\n\npath-uri: add lexical containment (#29614)\n\n## Why\n\nExecutor-owned paths must stay portable while the orchestrator reasons\nabout them. Converting a Windows or remote path to the orchestrator\nhost's native path just to check containment breaks that boundary.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add lexical containment to `PathUri`.\n- Compare URI authorities and complete path segments, so `plugin-other`\nis not treated as a child of `plugin`.\n- Fail closed for encoded path separators and opaque fallback URIs.\n\nFor example:\n\n```text\nfile:///C:/plugins/foo/assets/icon.svg\n  is below file:///C:/plugins/foo\n\nfile:///C:/plugins/foo2/icon.svg\n  is not below file:///C:/plugins/foo\n```\n\nThis is the shared foundation for keeping executor-owned plugin\nresources URI-native without consulting the orchestrator filesystem.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T13:59:40Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/414782450952a196bbb64b1605a458c2531c47b6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/414782450952a196bbb64b1605a458c2531c47b6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/414782450952a196bbb64b1605a458c2531c47b6/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"49614a0391d83eec442ffeca1d4aa0fdeb119818","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/49614a0391d83eec442ffeca1d4aa0fdeb119818","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/49614a0391d83eec442ffeca1d4aa0fdeb119818"}]},{"sha":"49614a0391d83eec442ffeca1d4aa0fdeb119818","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDQ5NjE0YTAzOTFkODNlZWM0NDJmZmVjYTFkNGFhMGZkZWIxMTk4MTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T12:15:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T12:15:20Z"},"message":"Namespace multi-agent v2 tools under collaboration (#29067)\n\n## Summary\n\nMulti-agent v2 tools now use the fixed `collaboration` namespace when\nnamespace tools are available. This keeps the model-visible hint and the\nactual tool surface aligned around `functions.collaboration.*`, without\nexposing an unshipped namespace knob to users.\n\nThe PR also removes the old `features.multi_agent_v2.tool_namespace`\nconfig/schema surface, updates the MAv2 test fixtures for namespaced\ncalls, and fixes stale `TurnContext.features` references that were\nbreaking `codex-core` builds.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Expose MAv2 tools under `collaboration` instead of relying on a\nconfigurable namespace.\n- Remove `tool_namespace` from MAv2 TOML config, resolved config,\nvalidation, schema, and tests.\n- Update tool-planning and integration fixtures to assert or emit\nnamespaced MAv2 tool calls.\n- Read feature state through `TurnContext.config.features` in the\nmulti-agent mode context paths.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just write-config-schema`\n- `just test -p codex-features`","tree":{"sha":"971b836466adadd009ff4cee0772536d0cf172d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/971b836466adadd009ff4cee0772536d0cf172d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/49614a0391d83eec442ffeca1d4aa0fdeb119818","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOnjYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzb8QAGEX4892ujQFjuXWH4wa6AHc\nn37rs4yTh4iGRwd9n8ytDlLCF3/e6qDk8y51xzQ92otJ/M9GqMMavZ509K8unqSF\nsqLXC1e60UfTBBjJC2y+Xf47bv5mt7f5Od9h9A4BpWWFep6RJ7iDUkI3M3T+Sr0c\nnwEs+SOOoyesAUP2RIzWbFhRaXK6006OoJN11vQ9H5yKMd6df8da5Q3KYk3WlVQs\nO7LA/bPw3TbMdTsOdGeWoDec6j/rYEyk1oTD9Kr/wE93jsaGsXKc/MmMihPtpnka\n9IffvVVbzumBa1CLe8I4GQO2JqUys/YKm57SxImuAPdpTweU5lEYSsRxG8SybRmn\nmjWdMb/HVeAcYwWw/iQkU0wg5Wb/1DfkDEMuraWXnfnCOK3qblu5GcCtL+1/38uu\n6VH6Sqe8ONEGEDPiU4BNRs6dMWCTzBLoLn9vXpZdaw0i7zdAHlGM7CqFMC0ueTmu\n/CPdBRsengN6caQ/qK330m+8lU9EREkQ5Ey7XOFquKJYCH/8h3tKLlIziKh8+7ip\nSit75i5x14jZ+anzrFPIh8NcLG+jU2nRR/XHKBsz7FpoIq4Xe6cNJB6IkgfkrK3o\nBS+mDvWid7Hy0UW70XOTfN9nx0AOWUG9WSKCaLALRKuvA231AV+qVnvpI/c9aVac\nu8sVHJJ4FfvN7IhsrCA2\n=+dBH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 971b836466adadd009ff4cee0772536d0cf172d3\nparent 55bc38a22bc6b75f51ca7d3a4bd3e634979af479\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782216920 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782216920 +0200\n\nNamespace multi-agent v2 tools under collaboration (#29067)\n\n## Summary\n\nMulti-agent v2 tools now use the fixed `collaboration` namespace when\nnamespace tools are available. This keeps the model-visible hint and the\nactual tool surface aligned around `functions.collaboration.*`, without\nexposing an unshipped namespace knob to users.\n\nThe PR also removes the old `features.multi_agent_v2.tool_namespace`\nconfig/schema surface, updates the MAv2 test fixtures for namespaced\ncalls, and fixes stale `TurnContext.features` references that were\nbreaking `codex-core` builds.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Expose MAv2 tools under `collaboration` instead of relying on a\nconfigurable namespace.\n- Remove `tool_namespace` from MAv2 TOML config, resolved config,\nvalidation, schema, and tests.\n- Update tool-planning and integration fixtures to assert or emit\nnamespaced MAv2 tool calls.\n- Read feature state through `TurnContext.config.features` in the\nmulti-agent mode context paths.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just write-config-schema`\n- `just test -p codex-features`","verified_at":"2026-06-23T12:15:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/49614a0391d83eec442ffeca1d4aa0fdeb119818","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/49614a0391d83eec442ffeca1d4aa0fdeb119818","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/49614a0391d83eec442ffeca1d4aa0fdeb119818/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"55bc38a22bc6b75f51ca7d3a4bd3e634979af479","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/55bc38a22bc6b75f51ca7d3a4bd3e634979af479","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/55bc38a22bc6b75f51ca7d3a4bd3e634979af479"}]},{"sha":"55bc38a22bc6b75f51ca7d3a4bd3e634979af479","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDU1YmMzOGEyMmJjNmI3NWY1MWNhN2QzYTRiZDNlNjM0OTc5YWY0Nzk","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T11:45:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T11:45:42Z"},"message":"Fix Codex Apps auth elicitation hang (#29615)\n\n## Summary\n- Require the reserved Codex Apps MCP server name to be present in the\nconnection manager before treating it as host-owned.\n- Update auth elicitation tests to model an installed host-owned Codex\nApps server without sending startup events to the test session.\n\n## Why\nPR #29518 replaced the old host-owned flag with a name-only check. That\nmade non-host-owned tests with the reserved codex_apps name enter auth\nelicitation and wait forever for a response.","tree":{"sha":"03d24773d49c926bd7da77df1c246c4bff0c3a7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/03d24773d49c926bd7da77df1c246c4bff0c3a7a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/55bc38a22bc6b75f51ca7d3a4bd3e634979af479","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOnHmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAs68QAFK07O3i7f15iOsCg+t+NM+K\nwqjiQK521mFWKQbTzXjPbdk/n0EMw2CFU49dbj061BidID5bhjtuO+2w8jwPxWdy\ntE5nM9qrCoNsyrT4KlJxf/kv1CokYCBI+tgP1dAHvJc77oCD2wGx32Lxrq89Bn8o\nJRbPgzZDQsYyrMrz9GzdhC+ULBQVVku6AaVq5HabrfgzueSQK/tKWBCX//BGqy8+\nm1EqpAqcT22e+5ocmnt6pRqcEFSRjFuWEOGymdUqCcRhydpcwawxxew1mCKgJVhL\neN14TEhquW981maDZMbwPbjLQJJfPSSj5/wCCtBF4mZlQ8feEalepJyKYGFegeCh\nWCm+chQaROpOmOiZfhOTa6gIVfHUhlvcFGn0CPyhN77kL0z27CXX/Us7fr3Hoy4T\nyjsicFhMJRyBRC2naUN6fJpR2agI9Z8LzTWkJhom/0UqCVZVBjf/dFbphsaGV4ny\n+phPaONhKK+2a8kxiNKGezjZIN21RwcoX2LzSLIRy3+aP4Rz/keXjqD3/lgSi8ja\nG4rzMSGf3ilXWanIkXNxcTVocA/d6HthRkbOmg6FNmcNKAfJCYelRLeIwIzylEnb\n5v1DWSPz4nh/1ASntjQzofW1/040D4KAuRJwSXWrwGA53STO9c3AP8AasDTYLfTf\nClWRSfIAMa2fa/oV7sai\n=eUdv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 03d24773d49c926bd7da77df1c246c4bff0c3a7a\nparent 63f8f547c0b95800f3c61ee172a2a833b75faf3f\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782215142 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782215142 +0200\n\nFix Codex Apps auth elicitation hang (#29615)\n\n## Summary\n- Require the reserved Codex Apps MCP server name to be present in the\nconnection manager before treating it as host-owned.\n- Update auth elicitation tests to model an installed host-owned Codex\nApps server without sending startup events to the test session.\n\n## Why\nPR #29518 replaced the old host-owned flag with a name-only check. That\nmade non-host-owned tests with the reserved codex_apps name enter auth\nelicitation and wait forever for a response.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T11:45:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/55bc38a22bc6b75f51ca7d3a4bd3e634979af479","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/55bc38a22bc6b75f51ca7d3a4bd3e634979af479","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/55bc38a22bc6b75f51ca7d3a4bd3e634979af479/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"63f8f547c0b95800f3c61ee172a2a833b75faf3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/63f8f547c0b95800f3c61ee172a2a833b75faf3f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/63f8f547c0b95800f3c61ee172a2a833b75faf3f"}]},{"sha":"63f8f547c0b95800f3c61ee172a2a833b75faf3f","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDYzZjhmNTQ3YzBiOTU4MDBmM2M2MWVlMTcyYTJhODMzYjc1ZmFmM2Y","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T10:18:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T10:18:25Z"},"message":"Stop persisting bridged log events (#29599)\n\n## Why\n\nThe 0.142.0 persistent-log filter disables target=log, but bridged log\nrecords are filtered using their original dependency target before\ntracing-log emits them as target=log. This allowed high-volume\ndependency TRACE events to keep reaching SQLite.\n\nThis is a follow-up to #28224.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Reject bridged target=log events inside the SQLite sink before\nformatting or queueing them.","tree":{"sha":"8e80b5949e2b3887418343491a8d42a2c869d4cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/8e80b5949e2b3887418343491a8d42a2c869d4cc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/63f8f547c0b95800f3c61ee172a2a833b75faf3f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOl1xCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU1UQADN4VzztJOfRBqYYdSTF/8hn\nopsdsA4ItwNUP5M0lATv+LFXkXWcHI1TUj/ubQQWJ+eIn4/Nz/dOV6IiDVg0T+we\nrjPwPcxjAd5LhzZcQPsa4KN3+WnVs4JkGrsHDAtgMx8+/moapUwjDqcxe9UeVRBr\nIHL7GnTLftNHK4vCPrKJR//4ILNDpzp6kKQ9PAisQRts79edP4ROnPgsqKSjT+L0\nb+bAtbiFXcpIswNlkMbfYZyFPvMV4MzDpsflofePn79pvRceZQK+weD6lWNrslmO\n+v90qxNxCff1g2BHvYbgK2iN6IUo9JoW9pKz1d/1gUKw1CpUETMXTmBcqF8MLfZ3\nXM1F8PsjiGFsrbd5qutN4J//DjzLUruWZdtjosqZ0/krYMKmQ7waS7Mg0u6+Nc1V\n7QQgsKaMV6Qb92H5B+4nT6q17F+kjDRyuktfsMwXbYaNjkLsftkVJI1F//w2ba5p\nwFuBnAWMlZMIgUe1YebuwqKxN7AaB7QXdcmb1DeP6JKxwPjLz2941kxAyO88yW6T\nbkkEDcOMfpVhqTTddl91GdSoG/4UC6ToW2ScV0L5/MJ6hrBSmTaauko1S0OqBtqi\nHokl3HNSunFBYjT/J/a7u0jD4af1fXoO+wAYeoQsKt5di7jt+B15Rv4YxXFH/3GS\nC3XL7Xp2eNi3WlQmwZlB\n=Fu42\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8e80b5949e2b3887418343491a8d42a2c869d4cc\nparent d2484697b1f9ce33d1d818ccad859ca3a4d721c6\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782209905 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782209905 +0200\n\nStop persisting bridged log events (#29599)\n\n## Why\n\nThe 0.142.0 persistent-log filter disables target=log, but bridged log\nrecords are filtered using their original dependency target before\ntracing-log emits them as target=log. This allowed high-volume\ndependency TRACE events to keep reaching SQLite.\n\nThis is a follow-up to #28224.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Reject bridged target=log events inside the SQLite sink before\nformatting or queueing them.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T10:18:25Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/63f8f547c0b95800f3c61ee172a2a833b75faf3f","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/63f8f547c0b95800f3c61ee172a2a833b75faf3f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/63f8f547c0b95800f3c61ee172a2a833b75faf3f/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d2484697b1f9ce33d1d818ccad859ca3a4d721c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d2484697b1f9ce33d1d818ccad859ca3a4d721c6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d2484697b1f9ce33d1d818ccad859ca3a4d721c6"}]},{"sha":"d2484697b1f9ce33d1d818ccad859ca3a4d721c6","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGQyNDg0Njk3YjFmOWNlMzNkMWQ4MThjY2FkODU5Y2EzYTRkNzIxYzY","commit":{"author":{"name":"jif","email":"jif@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T08:17:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T08:17:52Z"},"message":"Allow codex sandbox to consume MCP sandbox state (#29358)\n\n## Summary\n\n- let `codex sandbox` accept the JSON value from\n`codex/sandbox-state-meta`\n- require the payload `permissionProfile` instead of falling back to\nambient permissions\n- reuse the existing macOS, Linux, and Windows launch paths, treating\nexternal sandbox state conservatively as read-only\n- let opaque forwarders add runtime read roots and disable direct\nnetwork access without decoding the payload\n\nBuilds on #29113, which is now on `main`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `just test -p codex-cli debug_sandbox::tests`\n- `cargo build -p codex-rmcp-client --bin test_stdio_server`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nstdio_mcp_tool_call_includes_sandbox_state_meta`\n- `just test -p codex-mcp`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"1b1d5ddb3189e3b9dfa9f554631de2de375b8f3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/1b1d5ddb3189e3b9dfa9f554631de2de375b8f3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/d2484697b1f9ce33d1d818ccad859ca3a4d721c6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOkEwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAG8oQAKasVYQoBMulQaJ3l7igE81j\nP2mHxGOuZqZAMdVBUTQaKGue8dGBD17GhCabICRCAinWuAiatXBhHqxNs5frMSy7\nNmAxGPJrNEpOKbpZc5RflbNl0Xsj+MTJUD5JXFwh+j99eyVUyZIcYE4cQzY9uP8M\nXsPsEw3rOox/GNBuyplKP/pXInh5n4P3DeWXe54xrpMtNXgbglKN0L45Ym/KTJi/\nSw60zxul4Cg3GGnalsA05IhDQvTWLWFhv/0qQWeeI/kDAJH5me0IfNH/SfjpuAzq\nNbz2P8rnHPsh7e5WcWK4SV7Yd3ZOytXEk76nWFDLl7xzxBZ/Zt3OCUIlgz0/Lksf\nzqbiVWhpRf764lSRo0l2WYqMDyliFQ+E33hBRpHcGwS2uNotemT97WnPUa2fa7ai\ncjc8hMTmZF4+8b4iVAMMIpC/P/yOHSe6xnEAUEYMjRKiy1YQ77CenKwcF6S8WEbe\nzV5q8NjuslJJww+qgQrAGXNHzU2rvfQzKpim/aC3/jorZqD03l912ukBCow/cdaL\nf12kBM4GWdGSwEh+hNDuA1H8qM2VIgkrd2zaDDO3Ee3AO7dBWr7t2KCFlk9IR6SA\nRBv0u6P/v7UFcGDjUjZJLFon60bRNmYPtuStlHF0Q+fLcoL7BOCg+Agr3+C9bDth\nC6E392mFDfQbwqkMcHyx\n=/+0e\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1b1d5ddb3189e3b9dfa9f554631de2de375b8f3b\nparent 266dcbfe5b1972c027a4c04728e45949ccc1e820\nauthor jif <jif@openai.com> 1782202672 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782202672 +0200\n\nAllow codex sandbox to consume MCP sandbox state (#29358)\n\n## Summary\n\n- let `codex sandbox` accept the JSON value from\n`codex/sandbox-state-meta`\n- require the payload `permissionProfile` instead of falling back to\nambient permissions\n- reuse the existing macOS, Linux, and Windows launch paths, treating\nexternal sandbox state conservatively as read-only\n- let opaque forwarders add runtime read roots and disable direct\nnetwork access without decoding the payload\n\nBuilds on #29113, which is now on `main`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `just test -p codex-cli debug_sandbox::tests`\n- `cargo build -p codex-rmcp-client --bin test_stdio_server`\n- `just test -p codex-core\nstdio_mcp_tool_call_includes_sandbox_state_meta`\n- `just test -p codex-mcp`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-23T08:17:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d2484697b1f9ce33d1d818ccad859ca3a4d721c6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/d2484697b1f9ce33d1d818ccad859ca3a4d721c6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/d2484697b1f9ce33d1d818ccad859ca3a4d721c6/comments","author":{"login":"jif-oai","id":230027070,"node_id":"U_kgDODbXvPg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/230027070?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/jif-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jif-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"266dcbfe5b1972c027a4c04728e45949ccc1e820","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/266dcbfe5b1972c027a4c04728e45949ccc1e820","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/266dcbfe5b1972c027a4c04728e45949ccc1e820"}]},{"sha":"266dcbfe5b1972c027a4c04728e45949ccc1e820","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDI2NmRjYmZlNWIxOTcyYzAyN2E0YzA0NzI4ZTQ1OTQ5Y2NjMWU4MjA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T07:53:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T07:53:17Z"},"message":"Group Codex Apps client setup (#29583)\n\n## Why\n\n`McpConnectionManager::new` classified the Codex Apps server twice: once\nto create its tools cache context and again to select its runtime\nauthentication provider. Keeping those decisions separate makes it\nharder to see that they belong to the same server-specific setup path.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Group Codex Apps cache and authentication setup under one explicit\nbranch.\n- Keep regular MCP server setup in the corresponding `else` branch.\n- Limit environment bearer-token inspection to the Codex Apps path where\nit affects runtime authentication.","tree":{"sha":"0535bf844d058761a1bfd9efbe2742ab71e595b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/0535bf844d058761a1bfd9efbe2742ab71e595b7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/266dcbfe5b1972c027a4c04728e45949ccc1e820","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOjttCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjTEQAAm9QHTfOGCcxQm3x3DXwv9g\nxob/Tp/BKJqBnSLziAZV0itBP8FS9tPBq1t+RlYpvngKA61d7FCjmzrfJpsfXRkE\nzQ1lz0SwjhJ4kVfvriTbh2R8iX7fa3GNdsl1qmzsrw92j8TfdeL/2r8W32ljplSo\nC4zrNkK98VfRB6hPuRR2l2/Dlj3UnEP64eh2+Jnlyu6t7ppiyHAErBTmkgWnrKHg\nuNCzkrDT65L1tUC6drgT4BMNtLhAvTJ+gpw6oeE2/BatdnXlvVNsai0vq30yQFu1\nEoZd6dcmMCFQEP7DalI2+NMOUL8sw0ljCUNq7Q5dyO8fEGVUKXl/SrCtTokrljT6\n9KrDW8lY2RfW4tgiNK1fHD7xDlViZ8xyuUhXOn7rYcG+i074ivW22olq8I8GJuQP\n7lq1zM4dWUAOsCZIwWnu3P47OQOlAOWJ79dOlZeEb+JLJ7nHRVYdRmXwrY4dl4cp\nSzpOG0V2B9Re72Tt2Z5nNUWyXjmsGgAaZadfpv3/T4SV//tn0pMoI4Ypm8BqPBgK\nUtDT15R9QQ5fQDt4fTo5QCe0ORbxOjGWA7ojMaI9tkwHjY2nxAUv2A1eDUdr4QWq\nEBa4rw7gc2G04gLAJysh69RaCyJEOWFGP31mgXigtVCG2c84jBaCHXurzm1ccohp\niwYEjJSpNQGzq90S7ISK\n=7Imo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0535bf844d058761a1bfd9efbe2742ab71e595b7\nparent 83c4934e45d22dab962c55817fdbdc134e98dca6\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1782201197 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782201197 -0700\n\nGroup Codex Apps client setup (#29583)\n\n## Why\n\n`McpConnectionManager::new` classified the Codex Apps server twice: once\nto create its tools cache context and again to select its runtime\nauthentication provider. Keeping those decisions separate makes it\nharder to see that they belong to the same server-specific setup path.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Group Codex Apps cache and authentication setup under one explicit\nbranch.\n- Keep regular MCP server setup in the corresponding `else` branch.\n- Limit environment bearer-token inspection to the Codex Apps path where\nit affects runtime authentication.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T07:53:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/266dcbfe5b1972c027a4c04728e45949ccc1e820","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/266dcbfe5b1972c027a4c04728e45949ccc1e820","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/266dcbfe5b1972c027a4c04728e45949ccc1e820/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"83c4934e45d22dab962c55817fdbdc134e98dca6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/83c4934e45d22dab962c55817fdbdc134e98dca6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/83c4934e45d22dab962c55817fdbdc134e98dca6"}]},{"sha":"83c4934e45d22dab962c55817fdbdc134e98dca6","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDgzYzQ5MzRlNDVkMjJkYWI5NjJjNTU4MTdmZGJkYzEzNGU5OGRjYTY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T07:31:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T07:31:56Z"},"message":"Remove redundant Codex Apps cache guard (#29575)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex Apps cache writes are already restricted to Codex Apps call paths:\nstartup invokes the helper only from the Codex Apps branch, and hard\nrefresh operates on the reserved Codex Apps server directly. Rechecking\nthe server name inside the cache helper duplicates that classification\nand leaves the helper with an argument that cannot change valid\nbehavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Remove the redundant server-name check and parameter from the cache\nwriter.\n- Rename the helper to `write_codex_apps_tools_cache` to reflect its\nnarrower contract.\n- Update production and test callsites to use the simplified API.","tree":{"sha":"adc389593e86fdddb7e1b665c9b9203bfb91103d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/adc389593e86fdddb7e1b665c9b9203bfb91103d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/83c4934e45d22dab962c55817fdbdc134e98dca6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOjZsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANWkQADKg0mY9YQy4U+IvVCo+AxFE\nXiLg0TLXt+6oSC8I559jAYOndwwoNSJSxFBAlb2+lg+bEPGa5tZWB7rE38GnEmYi\neqlXmSEzEbmSQqZcijTYPHNgfqPVrqklV35JSDF7yW2v2pVthTu44fis5wzab5al\n8dugdlILM0VK73doNAbqi9ga+jui9F2IFHPCoO40v86YydD6fs+9+95xulHiZOZ2\nmfyfd9S6HH0c2FvBhoXq8X1o+ch53D7MAXAPpzDD+izQr1Y06x/PhidGuoXT3blA\nzMfSaYzkwdqOZzxHJh0V44yjhQUtrvPva89F8bArabdOC6Sx8JiaUX2ZyZVYEhSy\n/cZa1q79HTUPMBmdSSxBSVzc/1++FSJXff4UL6OjXCl/x+V2imwV+haoJ5NFjrtm\nh3hGm5yF/fsaa7PAahV2a2lOIknoRKCN1mVydu+965w8jtMQUG7HWXVrwnKg/Eik\ns0xv406nOXjmYfK2DLDKXKrK2K3dp4gdiOEga3mBt7Z3qHm+j8HWS3V48a7xEyHr\n2GzlzXHsQxBgo7TqmsRbViirFdaPV57kJceXMKzauwJifK2JEpmTpCi6N+shkUef\nS8lmQRS3k+MabAWK5Kv1pdH/G8/Wu0GBQ0MSWTD0RWHd3+bCFwO78p1eJ8VRkPvC\nBYwezSUyBr0C6oazUl77\n=6H6v\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree adc389593e86fdddb7e1b665c9b9203bfb91103d\nparent 6e0c8b45170eb295cfbba514a4e8aca00efb43aa\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1782199916 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782199916 -0700\n\nRemove redundant Codex Apps cache guard (#29575)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex Apps cache writes are already restricted to Codex Apps call paths:\nstartup invokes the helper only from the Codex Apps branch, and hard\nrefresh operates on the reserved Codex Apps server directly. Rechecking\nthe server name inside the cache helper duplicates that classification\nand leaves the helper with an argument that cannot change valid\nbehavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Remove the redundant server-name check and parameter from the cache\nwriter.\n- Rename the helper to `write_codex_apps_tools_cache` to reflect its\nnarrower contract.\n- Update production and test callsites to use the simplified API.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T07:31:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/83c4934e45d22dab962c55817fdbdc134e98dca6","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/83c4934e45d22dab962c55817fdbdc134e98dca6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/83c4934e45d22dab962c55817fdbdc134e98dca6/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"6e0c8b45170eb295cfbba514a4e8aca00efb43aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6e0c8b45170eb295cfbba514a4e8aca00efb43aa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6e0c8b45170eb295cfbba514a4e8aca00efb43aa"}]},{"sha":"6e0c8b45170eb295cfbba514a4e8aca00efb43aa","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDZlMGM4YjQ1MTcwZWIyOTVjZmJiYTUxNGE0ZThhY2EwMGVmYjQzYWE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T07:20:23Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T07:20:23Z"},"message":"Handle additional tools in image URL validation (#29577)\n\n## Why\n\n`ResponseItem::AdditionalTools` was added without updating app-server\nimage URL validation. The exhaustive match therefore prevents app-server\nand downstream targets from compiling on `main`.\n\n## What changed\n\nTreat `AdditionalTools` like the other response items that cannot\ncontain input-image URLs.","tree":{"sha":"fc831e6cfa4a318774e4bb2b9161cf943fa05da1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/fc831e6cfa4a318774e4bb2b9161cf943fa05da1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/6e0c8b45170eb295cfbba514a4e8aca00efb43aa","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOjO3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOZ4QAD450uXByz6aD/Zl6M75b7MT\n1Oxp3z2GEgcmubOrDk5JwpVgI4jWWAsqma2Ofx1365IQDJpT4H8SzCAb2PcVWJg/\nuvXedWac9KO/xsjvsUaZdOytdjXgrQ1Z5Tu6QHGVtr1Kh2WNBE/UAmx/IXU8g+iw\n4eqyFk4AThGODumuiiZoz1U3wIyMUeE/TqgwNAQGUHocLrb91pazZnywpSzzlHeI\nSJB9BugM6KdE+IQlBhAnV2QcMKyuF7v53a4uKqgyRUPfpZruhIGiyxCL7lx8WoV1\n4XhLKG5A3lNX0se1VuUGCsgtqybv35qp9tiuHc1hAKl/XuN2HGpIx+jCKWKJ4pc8\nPYYj3QJYB77FXIFN2pnRXQuqo8sh17Q9WVsss0zszr0sXKO/Qkq7T1WQvotT1Bho\nKzgFREEiAHO+Kpcgs6sfjnUQgRRrLYOkfNU236oXjAe/7keKO8G+HG6968xPIVRD\nSsEOvu34+5An7J78aBN8OXeNGgkz4dGIpGTQA/tRbSr8DYtJYYUJbPk7+KGARDFM\nhuwfszNvgpfSaQuOkOTEzuiyqlL9V/2BOY9aBHsnVW8LThERD0eR9Hm8C8/q4DU3\nDnfrcfd7Ixh3Jc4s9B6bjAEs0+58GtXsm1hPAHwxEhDZDp6Cy8m/NlJLQ072PV2m\nsiStIXBgF3xIUwW0YTgG\n=2/M6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree fc831e6cfa4a318774e4bb2b9161cf943fa05da1\nparent f0ad028a740f1fe6295cec38a0b5cfd0a909683a\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1782199223 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782199223 -0700\n\nHandle additional tools in image URL validation (#29577)\n\n## Why\n\n`ResponseItem::AdditionalTools` was added without updating app-server\nimage URL validation. The exhaustive match therefore prevents app-server\nand downstream targets from compiling on `main`.\n\n## What changed\n\nTreat `AdditionalTools` like the other response items that cannot\ncontain input-image URLs.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T07:20:24Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6e0c8b45170eb295cfbba514a4e8aca00efb43aa","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/6e0c8b45170eb295cfbba514a4e8aca00efb43aa","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/6e0c8b45170eb295cfbba514a4e8aca00efb43aa/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f0ad028a740f1fe6295cec38a0b5cfd0a909683a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f0ad028a740f1fe6295cec38a0b5cfd0a909683a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f0ad028a740f1fe6295cec38a0b5cfd0a909683a"}]},{"sha":"f0ad028a740f1fe6295cec38a0b5cfd0a909683a","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGYwYWQwMjhhNzQwZjFmZTYyOTVjZWMzOGEwYjVjZmQwYTkwOTY4M2E","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T07:00:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T07:00:25Z"},"message":"Centralize Codex Apps client handling (#29528)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex Apps-specific behavior is currently distributed across cache\nhelpers, startup, tool conversion, and model-visible annotation. Each\nlayer independently checks the reserved server name, which obscures the\nboundary between trusted host-owned connector metadata and regular MCP\nserver data.\n\nClassifying the server once when `AsyncManagedClient` is created gives\nthe client a single source of truth and makes the two processing paths\nexplicit.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Record whether an `AsyncManagedClient` represents the Codex Apps\nserver at construction time.\n- Route startup cache loading, cache persistence, and cache telemetry\nthrough the Codex Apps branch.\n- Split uncached tool conversion between Codex Apps normalization and\nregular MCP metadata sanitization.\n- Split model-visible schema and plugin provenance handling along the\nsame boundary.\n- Remove redundant server-name guards from helpers that are now called\nonly from the Codex Apps branch.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Preserve behavioral coverage that verifies Codex Apps connector\nmetadata and the complete converted `ToolInfo` shape.\n\n## Stack\n\nDepends on #29518.","tree":{"sha":"3c139b086e8a72ed91c6c9a92beee2a5cc25ce33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3c139b086e8a72ed91c6c9a92beee2a5cc25ce33"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/f0ad028a740f1fe6295cec38a0b5cfd0a909683a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOi8JCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA62IQAAQ3nfoMApl9deeOlSnnw5bx\nWaRkQLwAohFwSMbQw1QRwBgPZ8fsnD/zp2vCdhJRIipMZc0719vHHhTYk3yiB6nu\n1UIJXAK9N2lh1tn7fVEL1sAu2LWxAnOgawTIQ51b9LmcY4EENEnqQsLzaxwHs9th\nBVgbQFz+EVHK/9DKVKO54poNBvU5GMjt5FfP6Ax1I8cn1lvjwj2ilX5Sy/kLg4XJ\n6WeQMiLPBvih0j4I1BSFYd7S7AMEjJ8lovSaINqdC6dxlIMFiHnNhuWi5tTO11Nc\nFUJnkynb7mwjvYAUbTBYE1SQbOxsoD4tXMPV8XZeLoN6TTAIirRaQITGBpqUlHRb\nU43ONmU6WD1VPkpbYH0ZmYNfM8Gd62I+z38MEuzDl6S3jjbtQxa2ektbRRV5x4Nw\nYW0xKVp0yK5R0ylK/bE++d2ztA4hWU260S+9bf+9QCBRcRCV1XoKF5Oid8j4to/q\nVD+HIHL7UW+MLRZGZU+pBNU34MHXBKX6Vrqm0RuNnNMG4HSDFfnvwiUlexArIeMh\n8xDo5NhL+szYLco5JBl4e50/j2MpeS+gx3QZUo4wAyfdNdzQmpCs6YuBheAGaTDs\n7+xJbMnxmTnd520MtlcBwsNf2YdFf/uTcV2n514aPLVACHlYz3W8YRqgwl5HH/yZ\ne+dhe2RfzlafecK+on+9\n=BAlp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3c139b086e8a72ed91c6c9a92beee2a5cc25ce33\nparent 33cc928d339307795d4f5987337c7c4607f70338\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1782198025 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782198025 -0700\n\nCentralize Codex Apps client handling (#29528)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex Apps-specific behavior is currently distributed across cache\nhelpers, startup, tool conversion, and model-visible annotation. Each\nlayer independently checks the reserved server name, which obscures the\nboundary between trusted host-owned connector metadata and regular MCP\nserver data.\n\nClassifying the server once when `AsyncManagedClient` is created gives\nthe client a single source of truth and makes the two processing paths\nexplicit.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Record whether an `AsyncManagedClient` represents the Codex Apps\nserver at construction time.\n- Route startup cache loading, cache persistence, and cache telemetry\nthrough the Codex Apps branch.\n- Split uncached tool conversion between Codex Apps normalization and\nregular MCP metadata sanitization.\n- Split model-visible schema and plugin provenance handling along the\nsame boundary.\n- Remove redundant server-name guards from helpers that are now called\nonly from the Codex Apps branch.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Preserve behavioral coverage that verifies Codex Apps connector\nmetadata and the complete converted `ToolInfo` shape.\n\n## Stack\n\nDepends on #29518.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T07:00:26Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f0ad028a740f1fe6295cec38a0b5cfd0a909683a","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/f0ad028a740f1fe6295cec38a0b5cfd0a909683a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/f0ad028a740f1fe6295cec38a0b5cfd0a909683a/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"33cc928d339307795d4f5987337c7c4607f70338","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/33cc928d339307795d4f5987337c7c4607f70338","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/33cc928d339307795d4f5987337c7c4607f70338"}]},{"sha":"33cc928d339307795d4f5987337c7c4607f70338","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDMzY2M5MjhkMzM5MzA3Nzk1ZDRmNTk4NzMzN2M3YzQ2MDdmNzAzMzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T06:56:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T06:56:16Z"},"message":"[codex] Use input items for Responses Lite tools (#27946)\n\nWhen using Responses Lite, we should all use `additional_tools` and a\ndeveloper item instead of the top level tools array & instructions\nfield. This keeps things 1-to-1.\n\nForced namespacing for _all_ tools will land in a following PR after\nsome coordination & fixes in Responses API (around collisions & return\nitems).\n\nThe goal is to eventually expand the scope of this to _all_ requests\nfrom codex, but that will require larger coordination across providers &\nslower rollout.","tree":{"sha":"ee0642398cfc66e5b56ecaa34daee9799664fe4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/ee0642398cfc66e5b56ecaa34daee9799664fe4f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/33cc928d339307795d4f5987337c7c4607f70338","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOi4QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA340QAAVZUatqG3WUQMwhwfJpSZzw\nF9dSxd2ppW/JkDOZBQCYhlM37gpaD7eHUyor9ZJk4W4mL5pgocqke5fqwWXXrCkb\nrwpOBYrGTRMn1OV1o4zKxBsmI9tGn8sETzqNcB3gNjowEAamjFkeVQsfrSZ0+kp7\nP9WgEayORjWc17Qzi5pR9UOcWQVEW5uk3jt2BItvdTRJ8+wSgax/OHaMiG/ezKgE\nrZsoM3fJ2tVi9tYrVK621hL8WJkyLmoCnDxn5KVRGgaKUGMaAr+GvjOTGD3fOvAC\nT833Tlp9D1lEg9cNSn9WnhHUiss2OnCq+yQWYhnh4EaBCKv2OOsaRxjWO60KduPL\nJ3VWwPDrTblqK2o1ucOttC0vqWQCc7MAxEUA6UiYMaY4VBa4wvvSsOxz/wmFQ8EB\ns1U/gUyC5zbwqaXRnmWoZf8Ltp09uUZ9y5WkM3vOPfKUM0jAzUBnqV35fCRHXTOs\n/ZWiMXCgJUwRqHwYAlKIJhiioGMBWNdm8V8ME+jL3/mYqkw8se4Fd/Uy0lR1YtED\nTgugfizZAK95lwqGUct45DS3n8J8Pk5AlcDyZcrq3XPOyoaGbpTpbl+rmJip2OmT\nxkgeGve0D9JXzGyTvAMUbt0CYzzaEnjG7phz8V45GxQAVSvvzLXmEb+IvUo4482l\nEFWm2bTwPYbRCsOlcKPl\n=hQix\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ee0642398cfc66e5b56ecaa34daee9799664fe4f\nparent a22e3d0b8295550b6b8630cdaf4291af18aa4de1\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1782197776 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782197776 -0700\n\n[codex] Use input items for Responses Lite tools (#27946)\n\nWhen using Responses Lite, we should all use `additional_tools` and a\ndeveloper item instead of the top level tools array & instructions\nfield. This keeps things 1-to-1.\n\nForced namespacing for _all_ tools will land in a following PR after\nsome coordination & fixes in Responses API (around collisions & return\nitems).\n\nThe goal is to eventually expand the scope of this to _all_ requests\nfrom codex, but that will require larger coordination across providers &\nslower rollout.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T06:56:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/33cc928d339307795d4f5987337c7c4607f70338","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/33cc928d339307795d4f5987337c7c4607f70338","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/33cc928d339307795d4f5987337c7c4607f70338/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a22e3d0b8295550b6b8630cdaf4291af18aa4de1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a22e3d0b8295550b6b8630cdaf4291af18aa4de1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a22e3d0b8295550b6b8630cdaf4291af18aa4de1"}]},{"sha":"a22e3d0b8295550b6b8630cdaf4291af18aa4de1","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGEyMmUzZDBiODI5NTU1MGI2Yjg2MzBjZGFmNDI5MWFmMThhYTRkZTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Ahmed Ibrahim","email":"aibrahim@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T06:19:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T06:19:42Z"},"message":"Remove redundant Codex Apps manager flag (#29518)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex Apps server admission is already decided before\n`McpConnectionManager` is constructed. `effective_mcp_servers` and\n`effective_mcp_servers_from_configured` remove the server when the apps\nfeature or required authentication is unavailable, so storing the same\ndecision on the manager duplicates state that can drift from the\neffective server map.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Remove `host_owned_codex_apps_enabled` from `McpConnectionManager` and\nits constructor.\n- Identify the host-owned Codex Apps server by its reserved server name\nonce it is present in the effective server map.\n- Remove the now-unused flag calculations and constructor arguments from\nproduction and test callsites.","tree":{"sha":"88294f785f5cc98bcd9d450e2d44f0209f95938b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/88294f785f5cc98bcd9d450e2d44f0209f95938b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/a22e3d0b8295550b6b8630cdaf4291af18aa4de1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOiV+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeoMQAK7R/tOm1S0mWySPI8a0WQq8\n4Tue4WZlkA7gspHigCvB+FPcrhwWC9ZLPfUKHaqKJ0tFXPGyC0OmgXFqDcKINJef\nTTRbVlgxoVl6WO89xXeLZ2Mu5zwD8RMIXBbuv49crpO6AZ2x9+IKXiX8QOGk2fO7\ncbRRqlbPL1aKgr0uzXe/7NCobNxCJ6ZXkX4xZ0HBZVCT7OW3NWHjnqo7Kbo8szUc\n8N6Spmue4IAaElCW+5qwgfuYB8hbr8quWfmXl73WrYRZTKscvxrBfjhFUl82Hcn5\n0si01l1i1NJHXoJktGFv2YV0vrFBBdUJO5oopLF/zygy/MFOkIA+gplBkgksi8kw\nvyOtEC49ku7QtrmqNKq1ITALthEV+w4x8LpFA5uz0H/6NoI+AOXcUhE0AfnkyHd3\ny5zgDG4TaSa00V4iAHYj45QG7is+ez2r6xLq06XhAywH19/gpwFYoV7s7XgqPcyK\nQaykDd/BpBLZCSspLZNkmm7Dfm0xdr1sJTSGHA/APFVN1HEimRj2JPVSANl04dNs\n1rLh296hexdV/LLswOQpt1dCdQWiA/VkXf4wbeA37c5Md8OvXoX5wZttlXzyrj7t\nXaL2xKfJZtZA9mzkWKS/nS2N8gyp8lSDuQdoc+0AiAmqKRUL4JlWEocYGhISoeKr\nkW7CaRCH3cnqr8xUo78m\n=HWvm\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 88294f785f5cc98bcd9d450e2d44f0209f95938b\nparent 802c98cab4b65c3faa689a4d7962d28469f0d659\nauthor Ahmed Ibrahim <aibrahim@openai.com> 1782195582 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782195582 -0700\n\nRemove redundant Codex Apps manager flag (#29518)\n\n## Why\n\nCodex Apps server admission is already decided before\n`McpConnectionManager` is constructed. `effective_mcp_servers` and\n`effective_mcp_servers_from_configured` remove the server when the apps\nfeature or required authentication is unavailable, so storing the same\ndecision on the manager duplicates state that can drift from the\neffective server map.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Remove `host_owned_codex_apps_enabled` from `McpConnectionManager` and\nits constructor.\n- Identify the host-owned Codex Apps server by its reserved server name\nonce it is present in the effective server map.\n- Remove the now-unused flag calculations and constructor arguments from\nproduction and test callsites.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T06:19:43Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a22e3d0b8295550b6b8630cdaf4291af18aa4de1","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/a22e3d0b8295550b6b8630cdaf4291af18aa4de1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/a22e3d0b8295550b6b8630cdaf4291af18aa4de1/comments","author":{"login":"aibrahim-oai","id":219906144,"node_id":"U_kgDODRuAYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/219906144?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/aibrahim-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aibrahim-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"802c98cab4b65c3faa689a4d7962d28469f0d659","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/802c98cab4b65c3faa689a4d7962d28469f0d659","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/802c98cab4b65c3faa689a4d7962d28469f0d659"}]},{"sha":"802c98cab4b65c3faa689a4d7962d28469f0d659","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDgwMmM5OGNhYjRiNjVjM2ZhYTY4OWE0ZDc5NjJkMjg0NjlmMGQ2NTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T06:17:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T06:17:12Z"},"message":"[codex] stylistic changes (#29068)\n\n## Summary\n\n- express remote compaction result handling as an exhaustive match\n- preserve the special `TurnAborted` path without emitting a generic\ncompaction error\n- rely on the standard `test_codex` provider setup in the compaction\nbudget test\n\nFollow-up to review feedback on #28707.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncompaction_budget_exhaustion_aborts_without_error_or_retry`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"2634e4f79dee3b01f4aff6b7fb707018d83a7750","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/2634e4f79dee3b01f4aff6b7fb707018d83a7750"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/802c98cab4b65c3faa689a4d7962d28469f0d659","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOiToCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAcqYQADNu0QpRijqqVBTLopeVdEFg\n+Gy0Sv/6J5wTUJ1HwZokxReuM4F+WWsHzLKO8L2rrMCHKCIcI6YqHPAiexmMSXER\nFitnyz9sKtNROAZO8c2iS26QBfm7plyVgllb4SPAggJ875kKKKI8XeBVRlj+5oE0\n5uxYnkf+0x06aB8Aaq8MsVR7+PfzTVAL1FYxNvgbIPvUX2U+Hcdmb3arbSqs0YSv\nXyTw+dTrkgr9/yrXMBNO0hYMS9TyTlzBEwj7WQUljAwppH+c9zd/TqblQnFAhO3j\nyDOe4hL3Tq/M68YqJG7/3/0kBT5fwV8b8ZaigVhfrOntad4mYPpXL6tTyUI/7/kI\n+eF6mYN14vR4lcLIzQmNhZQ6hbhk3L7XfW+kDHI1H7OjbfTkzv47P2aSMHCY+EFP\nBNJ/HHyZy2jsmZ+g8NG5NqF5v1F6R799TgFHXMsLL2esc3mTj00etVHVxi4kHcVo\nEgJmuyhcZD9kDFNfqZWMUvXtIXQeEt87CuZxX06frIzS8Xpw5pBQYHHVhop67bkI\nkHc6Psfg6/5IJ7OB1RCQptwl6FHKp31nqGuiV3YWlIp5pYdYBoHu7prheih37IW8\nRqNgHErjwCRq2/B3VNch0/QQD2enKAdN78tjtZ6vFlEjftHxQ1QQIpDwAQ89GY6B\nlC2cgPYLFWcAWygcFmD8\n=vt9d\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2634e4f79dee3b01f4aff6b7fb707018d83a7750\nparent e0ac5d3c1552b4eb2c11d1f7e215bb933c78ad99\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1782195432 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782195432 -0700\n\n[codex] stylistic changes (#29068)\n\n## Summary\n\n- express remote compaction result handling as an exhaustive match\n- preserve the special `TurnAborted` path without emitting a generic\ncompaction error\n- rely on the standard `test_codex` provider setup in the compaction\nbudget test\n\nFollow-up to review feedback on #28707.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-core\ncompaction_budget_exhaustion_aborts_without_error_or_retry`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-23T06:17:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/802c98cab4b65c3faa689a4d7962d28469f0d659","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/802c98cab4b65c3faa689a4d7962d28469f0d659","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/802c98cab4b65c3faa689a4d7962d28469f0d659/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e0ac5d3c1552b4eb2c11d1f7e215bb933c78ad99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e0ac5d3c1552b4eb2c11d1f7e215bb933c78ad99","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e0ac5d3c1552b4eb2c11d1f7e215bb933c78ad99"}]},{"sha":"e0ac5d3c1552b4eb2c11d1f7e215bb933c78ad99","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGUwYWM1ZDNjMTU1MmI0ZWIyYzExZDFmN2UyMTViYjkzM2M3OGFkOTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"daniel-oai","email":"daniels@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T03:44:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T03:44:48Z"},"message":"[codex] Expose service tier and reasoning effort in OTEL (#29155)\n\n## Summary\n\nNVIDIA asked to measure Fast mode usage and reasoning effort from Codex\nCLI OTEL logs. Add the finalized `service_tier` and\n`model_reasoning_effort` to the existing `codex.sse_event`\n`response.completed` record.\n\nThis intentionally reuses the existing completion event and leaves\ntransport APIs and shared telemetry plumbing unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `cargo build -p codex-cli --bin codex`\n- `just test -p codex-core responses_api_emits_api_request_event`\n- End-to-end with the built CLI and a local OTLP/HTTP collector:\n- Fast/high emitted `service_tier=priority` and\n`model_reasoning_effort=high` with token usage.\n- Standard/low omitted `service_tier` and emitted\n`model_reasoning_effort=low` with token usage.","tree":{"sha":"9a3789c1b389e1eae1e6fad8138f0902f13b4a5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/9a3789c1b389e1eae1e6fad8138f0902f13b4a5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e0ac5d3c1552b4eb2c11d1f7e215bb933c78ad99","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOgEwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAH74QAEd1tnSIpPWh+E7H9MQXQURa\nREcHOQOaTq7mz0g9u7P8iBccwQ6kuED0oDe1LeHg5w1gG/P8+fbrJx9Fbu1lMeKE\nAV6jSH0kADXgYa+UGezzbnA22oWFbIUqiEokb3ds1McD8eGht5m5gzfwrbLsOTCg\noYlMK1z0tHNLlSntti4o74VHiga1T7zfy1C3xqlkk2Bm4+0Mem7q4g2H9iJawTFS\nmiYf5WIQ4vjTpMBMTpr3TBBFijLN9hDi6HGIQgqnbOIeurKLoFsCmuOAoMhjAhbk\nSIjOIL1lpGParlpkeDkut98+eL9+dQKuj6E11SEqI1GfL0zrsgywiVUNS52YFfLo\nsX817XG1SMzwrYaeBBxQ76qkMWXFoF2FDNeVCOCqKZ8YcVG5rD2BBHzrZwje3Q7r\n4kdSLgklHkpSO/Ox0eP1PHW9ujHGyqrOSeQY2CqIMPkOnsrQ0ImQoe4XUcc55H77\nu/fRumKxJXy/Itym7a7ZwTszcjD2VQXHuofpx7416Jc8VQ3ToCaW7C5WIsinCRUn\nDIK/6wtrfgSTKyWgQzHb7IhnpQkHYgqvh1K5kowO6VD3idz0SggvHZma2FS2Gg7K\nhmsRmQ4L3Xk8k7o48P8ey6Ys3ZozUOtQmc/j141FJUDButpFSseZOrHsdwKL8ln/\nNJt7Jwi/z1de01GJdyFj\n=5em1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9a3789c1b389e1eae1e6fad8138f0902f13b4a5d\nparent 27f22b54aef4d7e5eb6c564e969c961c74605461\nauthor daniel-oai <daniels@openai.com> 1782186288 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782186288 -0700\n\n[codex] Expose service tier and reasoning effort in OTEL (#29155)\n\n## Summary\n\nNVIDIA asked to measure Fast mode usage and reasoning effort from Codex\nCLI OTEL logs. Add the finalized `service_tier` and\n`model_reasoning_effort` to the existing `codex.sse_event`\n`response.completed` record.\n\nThis intentionally reuses the existing completion event and leaves\ntransport APIs and shared telemetry plumbing unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `cargo build -p codex-cli --bin codex`\n- `just test -p codex-core responses_api_emits_api_request_event`\n- End-to-end with the built CLI and a local OTLP/HTTP collector:\n- Fast/high emitted `service_tier=priority` and\n`model_reasoning_effort=high` with token usage.\n- Standard/low omitted `service_tier` and emitted\n`model_reasoning_effort=low` with token usage.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T03:44:48Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e0ac5d3c1552b4eb2c11d1f7e215bb933c78ad99","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e0ac5d3c1552b4eb2c11d1f7e215bb933c78ad99","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e0ac5d3c1552b4eb2c11d1f7e215bb933c78ad99/comments","author":{"login":"daniel-oai","id":257632403,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1sokw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257632403?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/daniel-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"27f22b54aef4d7e5eb6c564e969c961c74605461","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/27f22b54aef4d7e5eb6c564e969c961c74605461","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/27f22b54aef4d7e5eb6c564e969c961c74605461"}]},{"sha":"27f22b54aef4d7e5eb6c564e969c961c74605461","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDI3ZjIyYjU0YWVmNGQ3ZTVlYjZjNTY0ZTk2OWM5NjFjNzQ2MDU0NjE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Chris Bookholt","email":"bookholt@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T03:09:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T03:09:20Z"},"message":"[codex] Reject unlowered PowerShell AST regions (#24092)\n\n## Why\n\nOn Windows, Codex uses a PowerShell safe-command classifier to decide\nwhether a command is read-only enough to run without additional\napproval. The classifier lowers `EndBlock.Statements` into argv-like\ncommand words and checks those words against a safelist.\n\nPowerShell can execute code stored elsewhere in the AST. Parameter\ndefaults, named blocks, `using` preambles, and top-level `trap` handlers\nare not represented in the lowered statement list. Ignoring those\nregions can make a side-effecting script look like a read-only command.\n\n## What\n\nFail closed whenever a PowerShell script contains executable AST content\nthat the current lowering does not represent.\n\n## How\n\n- Return `unsupported` for parameter, dynamic-parameter, begin, process,\nand clean blocks.\n- Return `unsupported` for `using module` and `using assembly`\npreambles.\n- Return `unsupported` for non-empty `EndBlock.Traps` collections.\n- Preserve compatibility with Windows PowerShell 5.1 by looking up\n`CleanBlock` dynamically.\n- Treat `unsupported` as a failure to prove that the command is safe,\nrouting it through the normal approval path.\n- Add parser-level and end-to-end regressions for parameter blocks,\nnamed blocks, using statements, and trap handlers.\n\nThis does not make these PowerShell forms invalid or prevent them from\nrunning. It prevents automatic safe-command approval when the classifier\ncannot account for all executable behavior.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-shell-command`\n- Windows CI exercises the parser and end-to-end safe-command\nregressions against a real PowerShell installation.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: viyatb-oai <viyatb@openai.com>","tree":{"sha":"498d8e943ff97cb160900b0fca0541dbc430624b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/498d8e943ff97cb160900b0fca0541dbc430624b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/27f22b54aef4d7e5eb6c564e969c961c74605461","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOfjgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHygQAG+43fRk3YWGvMbg3QaqNMgi\nnBIv8yHe/kg8AvGcBfOGmuUJapFty69wXP/hiXCVmqv05P0gOMxUO4PD2551FJB0\n9U3opjvwYRjbwPuWzdmeWKUknkKN8Vu8PTG5Iy5GLRHgujBFZyKnc4vnLbrEBM3Y\n9QD2C3wAX0CcQCUPykSymoN5a17t7lvxgVKgC9k9CvbT6bMitoTO57OurYj3CpSk\nsOln9qfkwgQ7c/nVFMRc0pllDTzxG3+YtAWBna99ttGfeGIqgK8lvmjYL97P+hdE\n0wK2aK1jIfdCdqoVP1OnXc4WcCQC8sI9w9AsIo2SRRMMipDpKjx7kM/fAL8PL89s\nWW3La0RyY+p6i89e9145ADOnl4KhGhfNrj4F65Ri7xEhnd5nFoPfy8CrP0bC4/Vv\nqbjneVAsXbnJfvMJPcmpWJjawYfLSsviKlEXOJfn6WvvJYsZtxp0HAxPcbC5rasD\nsvbe9OywWFrGdp8s+AGYJFy7wpebBs2XDDql3sYYLbZHZiNmXqI7lFfLQuxh9QBj\n0dPDhD0ggOcX06F6OEHRgUBNx1+odyzf0Dy3l7JABcEgYFveqKzuz0Uy5POrreqB\nxi6rK27Zv+fPqKQ89De3+VRsXxQF6asA4J2FH/p5epD0xCuN4/LydESA1CxGFzh0\nNrfTVxkJ8boejJ7n2wyY\n=Tqwr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 498d8e943ff97cb160900b0fca0541dbc430624b\nparent 7c22d376e510e5f596e000260714d24b5b8f0783\nauthor Chris Bookholt <bookholt@openai.com> 1782184160 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782184160 +0000\n\n[codex] Reject unlowered PowerShell AST regions (#24092)\n\n## Why\n\nOn Windows, Codex uses a PowerShell safe-command classifier to decide\nwhether a command is read-only enough to run without additional\napproval. The classifier lowers `EndBlock.Statements` into argv-like\ncommand words and checks those words against a safelist.\n\nPowerShell can execute code stored elsewhere in the AST. Parameter\ndefaults, named blocks, `using` preambles, and top-level `trap` handlers\nare not represented in the lowered statement list. Ignoring those\nregions can make a side-effecting script look like a read-only command.\n\n## What\n\nFail closed whenever a PowerShell script contains executable AST content\nthat the current lowering does not represent.\n\n## How\n\n- Return `unsupported` for parameter, dynamic-parameter, begin, process,\nand clean blocks.\n- Return `unsupported` for `using module` and `using assembly`\npreambles.\n- Return `unsupported` for non-empty `EndBlock.Traps` collections.\n- Preserve compatibility with Windows PowerShell 5.1 by looking up\n`CleanBlock` dynamically.\n- Treat `unsupported` as a failure to prove that the command is safe,\nrouting it through the normal approval path.\n- Add parser-level and end-to-end regressions for parameter blocks,\nnamed blocks, using statements, and trap handlers.\n\nThis does not make these PowerShell forms invalid or prevent them from\nrunning. It prevents automatic safe-command approval when the classifier\ncannot account for all executable behavior.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `just test -p codex-shell-command`\n- Windows CI exercises the parser and end-to-end safe-command\nregressions against a real PowerShell installation.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: viyatb-oai <viyatb@openai.com>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T03:09:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/27f22b54aef4d7e5eb6c564e969c961c74605461","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/27f22b54aef4d7e5eb6c564e969c961c74605461","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/27f22b54aef4d7e5eb6c564e969c961c74605461/comments","author":{"login":"bookholt-oai","id":250040491,"node_id":"U_kgDODudQqw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/250040491?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bookholt-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/bookholt-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bookholt-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bookholt-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bookholt-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bookholt-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bookholt-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bookholt-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bookholt-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bookholt-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bookholt-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"7c22d376e510e5f596e000260714d24b5b8f0783","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7c22d376e510e5f596e000260714d24b5b8f0783","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7c22d376e510e5f596e000260714d24b5b8f0783"}]},{"sha":"7c22d376e510e5f596e000260714d24b5b8f0783","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDdjMjJkMzc2ZTUxMGU1ZjU5NmUwMDAyNjA3MTRkMjRiNWI4ZjA3ODM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Francis Chalissery","email":"fc@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T02:51:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T02:51:03Z"},"message":"Propagate safety buffering treatment metadata (#29473)\n\n## Summary\n\n- read the request-scoped safety-buffering treatment from HTTP response\nheaders and per-turn WebSocket metadata through one shared header parser\n- combine that treatment with Responses API safety-buffering signals\n- propagate `showBufferingUi` and nullable `fasterModel` through the\nexisting `model/safetyBuffering/updated` app-server notification\n- update the app-server documentation and generated JSON and TypeScript\nschemas\n\nThe public implementation contains no model mapping or real model\nidentifier. Tests and protocol examples use generic `current-model` and\n`faster-model` placeholders only.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- server-side treatment evaluation:\nhttps://github.com/openai/openai/pull/1060247\n- initial Responses API safety-buffering propagation:\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29371\n- Codex App UI: https://github.com/openai/openai/pull/1057789\n\n## Validation\n\n- Codex API tests: 129 passed\n- focused Codex core safety-buffering integration test passed\n- app-server protocol tests passed after regenerating schema fixtures\n- Clippy fix and repository formatting completed successfully\n\nThe broader app-server run compiled all changed crates and completed\nwith 1,269 passing tests. Its remaining failures were unrelated\nenvironment limitations: macOS sandbox application was denied, one\nexpected test binary was unavailable, and several existing subprocess\ntests timed out as a result.","tree":{"sha":"1d6a998f5f5f8e4e7967a4dc1693d7b9c2336d0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/1d6a998f5f5f8e4e7967a4dc1693d7b9c2336d0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/7c22d376e510e5f596e000260714d24b5b8f0783","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOfSXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGaAQAF7mUetXI2UL0t1g7y80ZlSq\nt0GNTVtVGl5uOrZYGZ8jsGnt7RRUwvjRcCWMlKhCl/hz9gPfJ85dELZeTwg2ZjdL\nGm6bQbW+qPvP3LkbVt6lIVmN4WLgi1kXdfXkvZdD2ZJccohImBqwMd9BIyydBOb+\nqyBTCaFp0oWFrctUS+KLfnas7SCogKSEg0b3sbVl33LUNVMBpnMhXM/rHYa45qCH\nZWSoYtMGInFStLgEJWW72VcZOpORL/ih6EDXMR2Wxplm4w2QAefq4Edfl/eJTAy5\nCPLAXY4q/eoquxpk6+2Ei4vSj5r/GMbezA/nlFggX0FfOcIV/tY1F2MJib+8Kbd1\nqifA3vVs14GMkyi0yAZukEyOC97nvsMt/ZlUa2g2fYwFs9KTYtt6zpGrvz6q1CMc\nFMWbeY6gsslnQHjq3Xj4COffuNF/zgFubHxfm7cbNdIOmZno3gaQNTqm1AKp2dmO\njH3H15VHs1KtCD7hlRes8g05CL6lQksiMn306bjK9a1z8r3EOzoJqbz3pFma44tY\nrM4ge1Evvj18kRhPa5sEEl0VA99Gu6sbYTwIGjo+UMlus1dGCmSP858U1sxmfwXV\n4407tWAbIowdpBURD9lDlG2ejbRu8Gq3i6rb6QBgOru8GTrEufJzfVita6Gl2pIR\nFjQIHtRzbmJl1CSoXiOl\n=dr0I\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1d6a998f5f5f8e4e7967a4dc1693d7b9c2336d0d\nparent 67009bc53ffc684eaf235c6186df890d35259240\nauthor Francis Chalissery <fc@openai.com> 1782183063 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782183063 -0700\n\nPropagate safety buffering treatment metadata (#29473)\n\n## Summary\n\n- read the request-scoped safety-buffering treatment from HTTP response\nheaders and per-turn WebSocket metadata through one shared header parser\n- combine that treatment with Responses API safety-buffering signals\n- propagate `showBufferingUi` and nullable `fasterModel` through the\nexisting `model/safetyBuffering/updated` app-server notification\n- update the app-server documentation and generated JSON and TypeScript\nschemas\n\nThe public implementation contains no model mapping or real model\nidentifier. Tests and protocol examples use generic `current-model` and\n`faster-model` placeholders only.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- server-side treatment evaluation:\nhttps://github.com/openai/openai/pull/1060247\n- initial Responses API safety-buffering propagation:\nhttps://github.com/openai/codex/pull/29371\n- Codex App UI: https://github.com/openai/openai/pull/1057789\n\n## Validation\n\n- Codex API tests: 129 passed\n- focused Codex core safety-buffering integration test passed\n- app-server protocol tests passed after regenerating schema fixtures\n- Clippy fix and repository formatting completed successfully\n\nThe broader app-server run compiled all changed crates and completed\nwith 1,269 passing tests. Its remaining failures were unrelated\nenvironment limitations: macOS sandbox application was denied, one\nexpected test binary was unavailable, and several existing subprocess\ntests timed out as a result.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T02:51:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7c22d376e510e5f596e000260714d24b5b8f0783","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/7c22d376e510e5f596e000260714d24b5b8f0783","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/7c22d376e510e5f596e000260714d24b5b8f0783/comments","author":{"login":"fc-oai","id":269039706,"node_id":"U_kgDOEAk4Wg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/269039706?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/fc-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fc-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"67009bc53ffc684eaf235c6186df890d35259240","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/67009bc53ffc684eaf235c6186df890d35259240","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/67009bc53ffc684eaf235c6186df890d35259240"}]},{"sha":"67009bc53ffc684eaf235c6186df890d35259240","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKDY3MDA5YmM1M2ZmYzY4NGVhZjIzNWM2MTg2ZGY4OTBkMzUyNTkyNDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T01:33:51Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T01:33:51Z"},"message":"mcp: accept foreign absolute cwd for remote stdio (#29493)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote stdio MCP servers can run in an environment whose path convention\ndiffers from the Codex host. A Windows cwd such as\n`C:\\Users\\openai\\share` is absolute for the executor but was rejected by\na POSIX orchestrator.\n\nBuilt on #29501, now merged, which only clarifies the host-native\n`PathUri` constructor name.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Deserialize MCP cwd values as `LegacyAppPathString` so config does not\napply host path rules.\n- Interpret that spelling as host-native for local launches and convert\nit to `PathUri` at executor launch.\n- Skip host filesystem and command resolution checks for remote stdio in\n`codex doctor`.\n- Add host-independent config and executor-boundary coverage using the\nforeign path convention for each test platform.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-utils-path-uri -p codex-config -p codex-mcp -p\ncodex-rmcp-client` (408 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-cli -p codex-rmcp-client` (372 passed)\n- `cargo check --workspace --tests`\n- `just test` (11,311 passed; 43 unrelated environment/timing failures)\n- `just fix -p codex-cli -p codex-config -p codex-core -p codex-mcp -p\ncodex-mcp-extension -p codex-rmcp-client -p codex-tui`","tree":{"sha":"3f5cf4a51b8386537ffbe834f9945f9fafee4d09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/3f5cf4a51b8386537ffbe834f9945f9fafee4d09"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/67009bc53ffc684eaf235c6186df890d35259240","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOeJ/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQh8QAI78J+XCUwwofHRqlDta68vz\n+Iv9NFdhsXQ8pt19ZDwEywI93ZRJ+KRcUYSO9EPXaVuA5EptcKKhsEQSGjAQxq3n\nkpYuX3zBvvK7iHVOIs8GEGnAPhi+rW17aJlZhmkGbsXyViRaJ5krMYEtQxE8lSEh\nC4e9aah5k3PcvxkJsFUVS6klvzk1yfF7GXLRgf4aesPxgT0toMl/AX8HkP6b3ODN\nzFffHyRUXUCtM5Pe/PXw0oqfOuc2t12IQHWgTlElBGpc59FeZWFxvbEmoRkiKT1l\nAlnjWRnAK8wT7iqHUObIh7l5kuJjStTA2lqX2KW9qdDA1C/jJDeJSqWZCtrHAGty\nUTOB2vQGuMHsH0ihAWEoQrBkr2bKdUC5lqxvGl1S0+lch3H5nhOc+kA5qUFgGt81\nr/vvnrhkgU6jk0gvH8v+Ogqmr7XQK2lNmgAhJexfeDp4Oe5teH1XpC8OkBPpeWFM\nkYsWvLHcFI11p3kHRPpKik5GfULugSBDHfuO2u+RD6wYKoncJCpLkiRz+xXVLZOQ\nbrUGT568yqHJylZXwZookL2j4Il8aiIvAFoG9zGP3v7mybBAyL47vCpySytVoDn6\nSdvIbNlct553NMymK3uuJ5T3zp0WdTNXK7K3Nroqjnw6GGbJ2laCO3SxjF/bXJF9\nH5Zgu4WC5RM9xMi55BM9\n=ikPK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3f5cf4a51b8386537ffbe834f9945f9fafee4d09\nparent 3310fc8ae5d56b2c2a617dff0800abf0ef3be16b\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1782178431 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782178431 +0000\n\nmcp: accept foreign absolute cwd for remote stdio (#29493)\n\n## Why\n\nRemote stdio MCP servers can run in an environment whose path convention\ndiffers from the Codex host. A Windows cwd such as\n`C:\\Users\\openai\\share` is absolute for the executor but was rejected by\na POSIX orchestrator.\n\nBuilt on #29501, now merged, which only clarifies the host-native\n`PathUri` constructor name.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Deserialize MCP cwd values as `LegacyAppPathString` so config does not\napply host path rules.\n- Interpret that spelling as host-native for local launches and convert\nit to `PathUri` at executor launch.\n- Skip host filesystem and command resolution checks for remote stdio in\n`codex doctor`.\n- Add host-independent config and executor-boundary coverage using the\nforeign path convention for each test platform.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just test -p codex-utils-path-uri -p codex-config -p codex-mcp -p\ncodex-rmcp-client` (408 passed)\n- `just test -p codex-cli -p codex-rmcp-client` (372 passed)\n- `cargo check --workspace --tests`\n- `just test` (11,311 passed; 43 unrelated environment/timing failures)\n- `just fix -p codex-cli -p codex-config -p codex-core -p codex-mcp -p\ncodex-mcp-extension -p codex-rmcp-client -p codex-tui`","verified_at":"2026-06-23T01:33:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/67009bc53ffc684eaf235c6186df890d35259240","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/67009bc53ffc684eaf235c6186df890d35259240","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/67009bc53ffc684eaf235c6186df890d35259240/