}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3310fc8ae5d56b2c2a617dff0800abf0ef3be16b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/3310fc8ae5d56b2c2a617dff0800abf0ef3be16b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/3310fc8ae5d56b2c2a617dff0800abf0ef3be16b/comments","author":{"login":"celia-oai","id":209693228,"node_id":"U_kgDODH-qLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209693228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/celia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b16d2858f56a9f3928ac0150250a176b04dde92b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b16d2858f56a9f3928ac0150250a176b04dde92b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b16d2858f56a9f3928ac0150250a176b04dde92b"}]},{"sha":"b16d2858f56a9f3928ac0150250a176b04dde92b","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGIxNmQyODU4ZjU2YTlmMzkyOGFjMDE1MDI1MGExNzZiMDRkZGU5MmI","commit":{"author":{"name":"canvrno-oai","email":"kbond@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T00:56:04Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T00:56:04Z"},"message":"PAC 4 - Add macOS system proxy resolver (#26709)\n\n## Summary\n\nStacked on #26708.\n\nAdds the macOS implementation of the shared system-proxy contract. This\nallows Codex-owned auth clients to use the route macOS selects for each\nauth URL through SystemConfiguration and CFNetwork, including PAC and\nWPAD results.\n\nThe `respect_system_proxy` feature is disabled by default, so existing\nclient behavior remains unchanged unless explicitly enabled.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Adds the macOS-only `system-configuration` dependency to\n`codex-client`.\n- Dispatches system-proxy resolution to `outbound_proxy/macos.rs` on\nmacOS.\n- Reads system proxy settings from `SCDynamicStore` and resolves the\ntarget URL with `CFNetworkCopyProxiesForURL`.\n- Executes PAC URLs and inline PAC JavaScript through a bounded run loop\nwith a five-second timeout.\n- Handles `DIRECT`, HTTP proxies, and CFNetwork HTTPS entries using HTTP\nCONNECT; unsupported SOCKS entries map to `UnsupportedProxyScheme`.\n- Builds concrete proxy URLs from host and port entries, including IPv6\nhost bracketing.\n- Maps results into the shared `SystemProxyDecision::{Direct, Proxy,\nUnavailable}` contract.\n- Hashes URL-specific cache keys so PAC decisions remain distinct\nwithout retaining raw request URLs or query strings.\n\n## End-user behavior\n\n- Disabled/default: existing client behavior is unchanged.\n- Enabled with `[features.respect_system_proxy]`:\n  - macOS auth clients honor system proxy configuration, PAC, and WPAD;\n  - valid OS/PAC `DIRECT` decisions use a direct connection;\n- unavailable system resolution falls back to explicit environment proxy\nvariables, then `DIRECT`, through the shared contract from #26707.\n- Unsupported proxy schemes are not silently translated into another\nroute.\n- Custom CA handling remains separate from proxy selection.\n- Known limitation: only the first supported system/PAC candidate is\nused. Subsequent proxy or `DIRECT` candidates are not attempted after a\nconnection failure. This matches the current Windows behavior and leaves\nroom for future ordered-fallback support.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `just test -p codex-client` — 34 tests passed.\n- `just clippy -p codex-client`\n- `just fmt`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`","tree":{"sha":"d3fa0a66ccb2ef0d65fa2849285dff64b1b5042b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/d3fa0a66ccb2ef0d65fa2849285dff64b1b5042b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b16d2858f56a9f3928ac0150250a176b04dde92b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOdmkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyS0QAHeQT69n8glCoA8f/axHRDp8\nJTnfP+tvnpC+knGVD6BjJcZdQaivFNg0z2chI9/wB5xXM48QtIhRpNRHujeNzFel\nDRrV7uBAE15NAwcZ9pm4UFbnWaBaHeUFg+pma8btrItN/pUjekbgvqACZ7tmlTG3\nJjEMslZ2NJYl7sIJa3vTHirTQ01Elhm3ApAadRc6Bx2AKYA58Cm+fUhVoZBYdXKg\nYc2jJ9Y5iVt9fi9bNbiiywDHRrJFtEN/brUK/UCdGZcRlA5Pv56dIRELkTyyhhHB\ntUCin4py8PppSX6Q4VHpvKmq9qulTEQi+eZvZmR7UBn3GvzUu8NY1eIebGNm9LiI\ndJmDPYJw9hkPfc+M8E86tfnaUzincF3tvTv2//kIU8E1t0mI6l6Ah4HmwpmpWfdq\nzKGpbvYgU+1fak0r04ubeCfjiMQqnivMHKuhzUX54EtsouI+hUgtMHykr1lh/rkw\ne2BJ910y7HdW7us68onb6Mt7/h7QlMqJLJv0ClBh9eJu6+11BZWsLEe3U0r7pqII\nu+1GBW7oEQvDfPWHDGvcs7jYVHesJIfttawyVR/2pa5uCIeLkkfSBamQa3ov95KE\nwTNCyAzlOVth9Zlmjqdw3MeKCCbHfDgCOR5tq8b52RFj2IiHrgw8+K7q2EEt0dI/\nsZf0+hNcBeZ6qxCwtjHp\n=4d1P\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d3fa0a66ccb2ef0d65fa2849285dff64b1b5042b\nparent ff31ba8d0a75f0a51644359265e194b93848a023\nauthor canvrno-oai <kbond@openai.com> 1782176164 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782176164 -0700\n\nPAC 4 - Add macOS system proxy resolver (#26709)\n\n## Summary\n\nStacked on #26708.\n\nAdds the macOS implementation of the shared system-proxy contract. This\nallows Codex-owned auth clients to use the route macOS selects for each\nauth URL through SystemConfiguration and CFNetwork, including PAC and\nWPAD results.\n\nThe `respect_system_proxy` feature is disabled by default, so existing\nclient behavior remains unchanged unless explicitly enabled.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Adds the macOS-only `system-configuration` dependency to\n`codex-client`.\n- Dispatches system-proxy resolution to `outbound_proxy/macos.rs` on\nmacOS.\n- Reads system proxy settings from `SCDynamicStore` and resolves the\ntarget URL with `CFNetworkCopyProxiesForURL`.\n- Executes PAC URLs and inline PAC JavaScript through a bounded run loop\nwith a five-second timeout.\n- Handles `DIRECT`, HTTP proxies, and CFNetwork HTTPS entries using HTTP\nCONNECT; unsupported SOCKS entries map to `UnsupportedProxyScheme`.\n- Builds concrete proxy URLs from host and port entries, including IPv6\nhost bracketing.\n- Maps results into the shared `SystemProxyDecision::{Direct, Proxy,\nUnavailable}` contract.\n- Hashes URL-specific cache keys so PAC decisions remain distinct\nwithout retaining raw request URLs or query strings.\n\n## End-user behavior\n\n- Disabled/default: existing client behavior is unchanged.\n- Enabled with `[features.respect_system_proxy]`:\n  - macOS auth clients honor system proxy configuration, PAC, and WPAD;\n  - valid OS/PAC `DIRECT` decisions use a direct connection;\n- unavailable system resolution falls back to explicit environment proxy\nvariables, then `DIRECT`, through the shared contract from #26707.\n- Unsupported proxy schemes are not silently translated into another\nroute.\n- Custom CA handling remains separate from proxy selection.\n- Known limitation: only the first supported system/PAC candidate is\nused. Subsequent proxy or `DIRECT` candidates are not attempted after a\nconnection failure. This matches the current Windows behavior and leaves\nroom for future ordered-fallback support.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `just test -p codex-client` — 34 tests passed.\n- `just clippy -p codex-client`\n- `just fmt`\n- `just bazel-lock-check`","verified_at":"2026-06-23T00:56:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b16d2858f56a9f3928ac0150250a176b04dde92b","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b16d2858f56a9f3928ac0150250a176b04dde92b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b16d2858f56a9f3928ac0150250a176b04dde92b/comments","author":{"login":"canvrno-oai","id":257630656,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1shwA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257630656?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/canvrno-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ff31ba8d0a75f0a51644359265e194b93848a023","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ff31ba8d0a75f0a51644359265e194b93848a023","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ff31ba8d0a75f0a51644359265e194b93848a023"}]},{"sha":"ff31ba8d0a75f0a51644359265e194b93848a023","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZmMzFiYThkMGE3NWYwYTUxNjQ0MzU5MjY1ZTE5NGI5Mzg0OGEwMjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Adam Perry @ OpenAI","email":"anp@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T00:55:49Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T00:55:49Z"},"message":"Make formatter output quiet on success (#29467)\n\n## Why\n\n`just fmt` is quite noisy even on successful runs.\n\n## What\n\nOnly print output when a formatter fails.\n\n- Buffer output from each formatter and print only a failed command and\nits diagnostics.\n- Prefix the `justfile` driver invocations with `@` so Just does not\necho the command itself.\n- Retain rustfmt stderr on failure and cover silent-success and\nfailure-reporting behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Confirmed `just fmt` and `just fmt-check` both exit successfully with\nempty stdout and stderr.","tree":{"sha":"b2d100cb74be8cd86ab1a20adc832998986ecef4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/b2d100cb74be8cd86ab1a20adc832998986ecef4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/ff31ba8d0a75f0a51644359265e194b93848a023","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOdmVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACcwQAGzYm8awy9UlB9WN9uf9PypM\n6HMaotQOusJE03H2rNHQnwXwIYjzfh2tGBIgRx77kYBYt0kLZLkpSpiydv4FqXXX\n+opkdsGkvWuE+gg3oXEjhSmuH9cKEpPKzpAOztBLw/S3n+j+uPaN6dPvQpGXyZd5\nj2eqOqyjnDl+4fXCVjXrJRkfmNs4N/12mdsNkTW5gWg2Mtzj9CGxYzqVtnHPQjRa\nt/m6yi3rPB2kC9aIgiC3ufH2oPWX4+ydokndz4qXtvHsEMBf61dAHUTPvoQX/uaN\nIys+Yf/0mCYNP/Dtc/9OX4r7+eIWJrcV7ptpyftenbINb7NKSO7EMEW7JlW88pnW\nJh6oFajWU7n6oTQdmakNC8PezLcdVYiaeNYsNGY2+Qusgxrio1ZALyiR+QvZpLie\nKgT+2I1NhsTZvIN/lyUNcKlYzIV5ErywuwV+Icyet/k9bfSzIV05HZgg++sRKQ/M\n+ITqvOMwcjCCOx/p60Vq91C94I6AQHGtV7QOXXirrDH+SciZPtx4FrXe7kxQl8YT\nK1khEBCV0gR9P2LZGduDk/kICgvYeOI8vn+SgL47P28RAXVSRCyM+FQ+OS353nkF\nlvxbXV8VWD4lBsHD7Xnl8YuDqB1Q/hZdYKtrsGVW97bEPOOKcLv4ipc7hPQR9L9J\n3p7Lo8WfHOZv6teB1Cnt\n=6EUF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b2d100cb74be8cd86ab1a20adc832998986ecef4\nparent e65e480e0d67ce5a32667ff3e89143be035a0606\nauthor Adam Perry @ OpenAI <anp@openai.com> 1782176149 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782176149 +0000\n\nMake formatter output quiet on success (#29467)\n\n## Why\n\n`just fmt` is quite noisy even on successful runs.\n\n## What\n\nOnly print output when a formatter fails.\n\n- Buffer output from each formatter and print only a failed command and\nits diagnostics.\n- Prefix the `justfile` driver invocations with `@` so Just does not\necho the command itself.\n- Retain rustfmt stderr on failure and cover silent-success and\nfailure-reporting behavior.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Confirmed `just fmt` and `just fmt-check` both exit successfully with\nempty stdout and stderr.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T00:55:50Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ff31ba8d0a75f0a51644359265e194b93848a023","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/ff31ba8d0a75f0a51644359265e194b93848a023","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/ff31ba8d0a75f0a51644359265e194b93848a023/comments","author":{"login":"anp-oai","id":286154589,"node_id":"U_kgDOEQ5fXQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286154589?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/anp-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anp-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e65e480e0d67ce5a32667ff3e89143be035a0606","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e65e480e0d67ce5a32667ff3e89143be035a0606","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e65e480e0d67ce5a32667ff3e89143be035a0606"}]},{"sha":"e65e480e0d67ce5a32667ff3e89143be035a0606","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGU2NWU0ODBlMGQ2N2NlNWEzMjY2N2ZmM2U4OTE0M2JlMDM1YTA2MDY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Celia Chen","email":"celia@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T00:53:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T00:53:09Z"},"message":"chore: improve expired Bedrock credential errors (#28992)\n\n## Why\n\nAmazon Bedrock returns a `401 Unauthorized` response containing\n`Signature expired:` when an AWS credential, including a short-lived\n`AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK`, has expired. Codex currently surfaces that\nresponse as a generic `unexpected status` error, which does not explain\nhow to recover.\n\nEnvironment-provided bearer tokens cannot be refreshed automatically, so\nthe error should direct users to refresh their AWS credentials or\nreplace or remove the environment token and restart Codex. This\nclassification belongs to the Amazon Bedrock provider so similar\nresponses from other providers retain their existing behavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a synchronous `ModelProvider::map_api_error` hook that defaults to\nthe existing provider-neutral API error mapping, and route model\nrequest, stream, WebSocket, and terminal unauthorized errors through the\nactive provider.\n- Override the hook for Amazon Bedrock. After preserving the structured\nstatus, body, URL, and request metadata, recognize `401` responses\ncontaining `Signature expired:` and attach actionable credential\nguidance.\n- Keep `codex-protocol` provider-neutral by representing the guidance as\nan optional `user_message`. Error rendering prefers this message while\ncontinuing to append the URL, request ID, Cloudflare ray, and\nauthorization diagnostics.\n- Add model-provider coverage for expired signatures and negative cases,\ncore coverage for provider dispatch after unauthorized recovery, and a\nTUI snapshot for the rendered error.\n\n## Testing\nTested with a real request with expired bedrock key:\n<img width=\"962\" height=\"126\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-22 at 3 56 51 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7e21cc7c-798e-4662-8467-7f304a2f2b59\"\n/>","tree":{"sha":"46865ec3a749946dfeb7f4cb05a4745c99434b3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/46865ec3a749946dfeb7f4cb05a4745c99434b3f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/e65e480e0d67ce5a32667ff3e89143be035a0606","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOdj1CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaNIQAJWvCljJOUON0KCyeWy3pHAS\nkwekXQH1px3+hv0rRpEVm7nWq1WJOnLbm2nnV55D+4rNzJzvxxrP44TwApyx1mYC\nQAe530nT8KbrYxa3bxc4DDWozTvVtbw/wLXZzz2BNcf753dWkO2DO5EiM+NSoeoz\n6Dnv8wuCzmkg98C/bydmYSdhC+xa3XGDnBW8Ng8SJXsaol7wm/zcTymRXkDkLOoA\nE9Z15ULhAVvoT3GJFxy++c0gUGcDOaguzt13oROBjOW1ZUsjSHUZEKGxWmfvZRbr\nPIujp9XusetZeRaEOaxOYFIHkBLzJnz5bytV7fzHTvpZxg8v7BYNkVno9XFbeP71\nxlFcjFhnK3pKMsUgQeHI+F9TvVQAXOKrtw44u7Fp223akWZG0S/HQVz/KL820YSj\nQt5vyXuHgVHplXqin+lNMQ9eiwBFA6h4mbQgp8JD9q3q8b1lYvst/x8IrERufl1s\nX5v0RHGY3EwJi6caBsyEvwNiQymQ1deql0CBsWO1VPFfhNwNSNzl6f941PJYAlP/\nBJ8xpBKOz6tfAXMJeJeIuirygweSmvvj3RgskPWuz8CqkTpmmDNZTr07D/0mjOHv\nq02EDbC+DuU96dyu3HdFXcY1Jc5YwRPLU+pI/arJpomXT7K12Dh1NwaoJ9vjGiow\nbgPyE7D8+k6EBuOccRqT\n=2acp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 46865ec3a749946dfeb7f4cb05a4745c99434b3f\nparent b294638bb557afe3e8bd1d82aa3ea9f459b2747e\nauthor Celia Chen <celia@openai.com> 1782175989 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782175989 +0000\n\nchore: improve expired Bedrock credential errors (#28992)\n\n## Why\n\nAmazon Bedrock returns a `401 Unauthorized` response containing\n`Signature expired:` when an AWS credential, including a short-lived\n`AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK`, has expired. Codex currently surfaces that\nresponse as a generic `unexpected status` error, which does not explain\nhow to recover.\n\nEnvironment-provided bearer tokens cannot be refreshed automatically, so\nthe error should direct users to refresh their AWS credentials or\nreplace or remove the environment token and restart Codex. This\nclassification belongs to the Amazon Bedrock provider so similar\nresponses from other providers retain their existing behavior.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Add a synchronous `ModelProvider::map_api_error` hook that defaults to\nthe existing provider-neutral API error mapping, and route model\nrequest, stream, WebSocket, and terminal unauthorized errors through the\nactive provider.\n- Override the hook for Amazon Bedrock. After preserving the structured\nstatus, body, URL, and request metadata, recognize `401` responses\ncontaining `Signature expired:` and attach actionable credential\nguidance.\n- Keep `codex-protocol` provider-neutral by representing the guidance as\nan optional `user_message`. Error rendering prefers this message while\ncontinuing to append the URL, request ID, Cloudflare ray, and\nauthorization diagnostics.\n- Add model-provider coverage for expired signatures and negative cases,\ncore coverage for provider dispatch after unauthorized recovery, and a\nTUI snapshot for the rendered error.\n\n## Testing\nTested with a real request with expired bedrock key:\n<img width=\"962\" height=\"126\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-06-22 at 3 56 51 PM\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7e21cc7c-798e-4662-8467-7f304a2f2b59\"\n/>","verified_at":"2026-06-23T00:53:09Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e65e480e0d67ce5a32667ff3e89143be035a0606","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/e65e480e0d67ce5a32667ff3e89143be035a0606","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/e65e480e0d67ce5a32667ff3e89143be035a0606/comments","author":{"login":"celia-oai","id":209693228,"node_id":"U_kgDODH-qLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209693228?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/celia-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/celia-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b294638bb557afe3e8bd1d82aa3ea9f459b2747e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b294638bb557afe3e8bd1d82aa3ea9f459b2747e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b294638bb557afe3e8bd1d82aa3ea9f459b2747e"}]},{"sha":"b294638bb557afe3e8bd1d82aa3ea9f459b2747e","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGIyOTQ2MzhiYjU1N2FmZTNlOGJkMWQ4MmFhM2VhOWY0NTliMjc0N2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"rka-oai","email":"rka@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T00:43:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T00:43:56Z"},"message":"[codex] reject remote images at app-server ingress (#29419)\n\n## Stack\n\nStacked on #29417. Review and land that PR first.\n\n## Summary\n\n- reject HTTP(S) image URLs in the handlers for `turn/start` and\n`turn/steer`\n- validate `thread/inject_items` after its existing\nJSON-to-`ResponseItem` conversion, so each item is deserialized once\n- turn invalid dynamic-tool image responses into the existing\nunsuccessful text fallback; the model receives the validation message as\nthe function output\n- leave `thread/resume.history` compatible with legacy history; #29417\nreplaces remote images before model input\n- continue accepting inline data URLs and `localImage` inputs\n- keep this policy in app-server; this PR does not add a shared protocol\nAPI or change core image preparation\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server -E\n'test(/request_handlers_reject_remote_image_urls|dynamic_tool_remote_image_response_becomes_model_visible_error|dynamic_tool_call_round_trip_sends_content_items_to_model|turn_start_tracks_turn_event_analytics|standalone_image_edit_uses_recent_pathless_image/)'`\n(5 passed)\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server`\n- `just fmt`","tree":{"sha":"81533a58edbed63aeafee225cde921a4cba8147d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/81533a58edbed63aeafee225cde921a4cba8147d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/b294638bb557afe3e8bd1d82aa3ea9f459b2747e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOdbMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXV4QABS/Xs/3OkxhRIQRWyu9INiJ\nGBdR7vo3u4d4kqOiq4AZwzKrX4NoYerzhZxaCNZchDtTAIUOEg31IxIwv8qwR9W8\nNNq9LVOW94MNTCcqyR+b0iH2FJhRzhtxT7tcBBHhtsoZM0pmy/15SLlWqCGpgJYP\nGaFzYKP+MF2gcj+cbdCQLePSBv1uJyV7XubFN9CrztmL0HQoNUqO6skPvyZpFhlH\nBRdWiqIE/GIaWs4ENBAdm2loCELZKH13u3R2Sen080F93OZsDC/DKVYsifVJ9hwf\nkiEGiQKQzM8dv5vXWVYBLE8kUHIlfT/J8MYeMViUEZIzSYYmv2vq6Sk4ZGDCFas/\ndDhLvvkIQW3r1JgbeAPjY6rH+BsNe41WH1SH5nOvWkUA6e+GzyFHLqfvsk0owXm6\nchVQeuzzxB6NY7b+bHhdbPQx5Pq9KDBznYi0NqW/pRmvA0ryv3VZn3J4Yf+LZvlI\n2azDTwv6yiJS0i+iyf5yv+tK4l0FlGEjlDw4n077I+4tdOCMNYwhtPs2nT8luh3X\nBE+hUdE3v/jZQ3t2WhJonAYSHIoIihFgDe/iH+Y85rZ7lpUZ+dCi0hxD8pSsyrev\nt8C7gRzkLQWeU5O7qtW0BtiL0K85gT6AFx5aBqKdLV5sx3yRxCsCf+IFI5rNqXz8\nVajw/samvCKy9IxT8BjE\n=ymKC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 81533a58edbed63aeafee225cde921a4cba8147d\nparent fbd575ab4a8f786a535223856e4b8fd8beb29458\nauthor rka-oai <rka@openai.com> 1782175436 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782175436 +0000\n\n[codex] reject remote images at app-server ingress (#29419)\n\n## Stack\n\nStacked on #29417. Review and land that PR first.\n\n## Summary\n\n- reject HTTP(S) image URLs in the handlers for `turn/start` and\n`turn/steer`\n- validate `thread/inject_items` after its existing\nJSON-to-`ResponseItem` conversion, so each item is deserialized once\n- turn invalid dynamic-tool image responses into the existing\nunsuccessful text fallback; the model receives the validation message as\nthe function output\n- leave `thread/resume.history` compatible with legacy history; #29417\nreplaces remote images before model input\n- continue accepting inline data URLs and `localImage` inputs\n- keep this policy in app-server; this PR does not add a shared protocol\nAPI or change core image preparation\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `just test -p codex-app-server -E\n'test(/request_handlers_reject_remote_image_urls|dynamic_tool_remote_image_response_becomes_model_visible_error|dynamic_tool_call_round_trip_sends_content_items_to_model|turn_start_tracks_turn_event_analytics|standalone_image_edit_uses_recent_pathless_image/)'`\n(5 passed)\n- `just fix -p codex-app-server`\n- `just fmt`","verified_at":"2026-06-23T00:43:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b294638bb557afe3e8bd1d82aa3ea9f459b2747e","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/b294638bb557afe3e8bd1d82aa3ea9f459b2747e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/b294638bb557afe3e8bd1d82aa3ea9f459b2747e/comments","author":{"login":"rka-oai","id":240799229,"node_id":"U_kgDODlpN_Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/240799229?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/rka-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rka-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"fbd575ab4a8f786a535223856e4b8fd8beb29458","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fbd575ab4a8f786a535223856e4b8fd8beb29458","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fbd575ab4a8f786a535223856e4b8fd8beb29458"}]},{"sha":"fbd575ab4a8f786a535223856e4b8fd8beb29458","node_id":"C_kwDOOYsS4doAKGZiZDU3NWFiNGE4Zjc4NmE1MzUyMjM4NTZlNGI4ZmQ4YmViMjk0NTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"canvrno-oai","email":"kbond@openai.com","date":"2026-06-23T00:31:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-23T00:31:14Z"},"message":"TUI Plugin Sharing 4 - cover remote plugin catalog flows (#26704)\n\nRemote plugin catalogs now span workspace, shared, and local sources, so\ntheir TUI behavior needs focused regression coverage across loading,\nnavigation, actions, and refreshes.\n\nThis PR:\n\n- Covers product labels and rendered loading/error states for Workspace,\nShared with me, Shared with me (link), and Local tabs, including tab\npersistence across refresh and detail navigation.\n- Covers remote/local deduplication, Installed-tab remote detail\nrouting, marketplace load-error handling, and disabled install/uninstall\nnavigation.\n- Adds a full detail snapshot for local shared-plugin metadata plus\nfocused snapshots for marketplace labels and admin-disabled status.\n- Verifies shared plugins remain eligible for mentions and successful\nuninstalls trigger a catalog refresh.","tree":{"sha":"5e535f6e8e1ae470dbd09ef715988a0b19d6e1f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/trees/5e535f6e8e1ae470dbd09ef715988a0b19d6e1f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/git/commits/fbd575ab4a8f786a535223856e4b8fd8beb29458","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOdPSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9c0QADywNQVNK75guYgvVn1MwfNM\ncn9czxtwzow1LKZdB3fckHx31q503LKbE+5juGb0BdbueadGcr+u5aLmpNF1/1pq\nNF5gEo8DY5KVOT0EO9u2tIxHooGPq/ZgfgCMFpKuOnYC5wOQUEPT4TDNOy82RVc0\nd/7zyjxk6Nt1Jcyj3PVhWEhkdYCM0YqI478r7QzFfwCexw8e4to8aicCr4+WRYJj\nSVJWnicrZ7DYFN2oHNy/2s+LLZ0zeHE8WgkgshPW5eT0+X/7dXVJfTA/b6hTvbRn\nieBvtP4YlFNx51qrtvbfNaDM1MT+ZW+91vkHTKfDuLtHQweFuH4Mpx+z+v8IoIXb\nIwdiY7rDDzSr0wnez5YpiEaDfyf+37ywzXQDaNTV1b03El5w8xI/Fiss2x7BUKzX\nbjOXXfGXkypj78mBFJ4k1wfpmkYLEHcCFvrg/DvGGuSqucOZg90oXCAugmqQ3REF\n1jthZmNkCE2i+qgZ1fbVi1IE3IMhigfhWSBwJa3d8GnnsCJ7pJd1OaBdUeKJ0AKB\njA7MTPEdvefemu1tG9BdX23YkMgQ4e9rwRCngLen9+RJLlv3T9K3diLLcF+4fGAm\nuMox1m03P2NS2ERtjpKGGqNbK2lMoYvAzYhGM6PfSbYTzKoOs5SaDBXRQheqmnME\ngYV6BWWDMLXg1/ATWfJD\n=RMbs\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5e535f6e8e1ae470dbd09ef715988a0b19d6e1f8\nparent 97dc6abb11a1e5e15acb5b8a499e853418ea4902\nauthor canvrno-oai <kbond@openai.com> 1782174674 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782174674 -0700\n\nTUI Plugin Sharing 4 - cover remote plugin catalog flows (#26704)\n\nRemote plugin catalogs now span workspace, shared, and local sources, so\ntheir TUI behavior needs focused regression coverage across loading,\nnavigation, actions, and refreshes.\n\nThis PR:\n\n- Covers product labels and rendered loading/error states for Workspace,\nShared with me, Shared with me (link), and Local tabs, including tab\npersistence across refresh and detail navigation.\n- Covers remote/local deduplication, Installed-tab remote detail\nrouting, marketplace load-error handling, and disabled install/uninstall\nnavigation.\n- Adds a full detail snapshot for local shared-plugin metadata plus\nfocused snapshots for marketplace labels and admin-disabled status.\n- Verifies shared plugins remain eligible for mentions and successful\nuninstalls trigger a catalog refresh.","verified_at":"2026-06-23T00:31:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fbd575ab4a8f786a535223856e4b8fd8beb29458","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/commit/fbd575ab4a8f786a535223856e4b8fd8beb29458","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/commits/fbd575ab4a8f786a535223856e4b8fd8beb29458/comments","author":{"login":"canvrno-oai","id":257630656,"node_id":"U_kgDOD1shwA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257630656?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai","html_url":"https://github.com/canvrno-oai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/canvrno-oai/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/us